window.GNAMMA_CRITICAL_CORPUS={"schema":"gnamma-tahdhib-critical-v1","work":"Tahdhīb al-Kalām","title_ar":"تهذيب الكلام","author":"Saʿd al-Dīn al-Taftāzānī","edition":"Stage 75 Cairo 1912 working bilingual text","witness":"Cairo 1330 AH / 1912, pp. 15–127","editorial_status":"Working bilingual edition; 108/113 Cairo printed pages recorded as source checked; five pages outstanding; no independent manuscript collation","pending_pages":[39,77,80,100,124],"units":[{"id":"KAL-015.01","page":15,"ar":"هذا قسم الكلام من التهذيب.","en":"This is the kalām section of the Tahdhīb.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-015.02","page":15,"ar":"وعلى الستة وقع التبويب.","en":"And the text has been organized into six chapters.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-015.03","page":15,"ar":"الباب الأول في المقدمة.","en":"Chapter One: Introduction.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-015.04","page":15,"ar":"الكلام هو العلم بالعقائد الدينية عن الأدلة اليقينية.","en":"Kalām is knowledge of religious doctrines derived from certain proofs.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-015.05","page":15,"ar":"وموضوعه المعلوم من حيث يتعلق بذلك.","en":"Its subject is the knowable insofar as it is connected with that [purpose].","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-015.06","page":15,"ar":"والعلم لا يحد.","en":"Knowledge is not susceptible of a [strict] definition.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-015.07","page":15,"ar":"والتفسير له بمثل حصول صورة الشيء في العقل، أو الاعتقاد الجازم المطابق الثابت، أو صفة يتجلى بها المذكور لمن ...","en":"It may instead be explained by such formulations as: the occurrence of a thing’s form in the intellect; or a firm, reality-conforming, settled belief; or a quality through which the thing mentioned becomes disclosed to the one in whom [that quality] ...","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-016.01","page":16,"ar":"... قامت هي به، أو إدراك المركب أو الكلي؛ تنبيه على اختلاف الاصطلاحات.","en":"... subsists; or apprehension of a composite or of a universal. These [different formulations] call attention to differences in technical usage.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-016.02","page":16,"ar":"وحقيقة النظر حركة النفس في المعقولات عودًا على بدء لتحصيل المجهول.","en":"The reality of rational inquiry (naẓar) is the soul’s movement among intelligibles, going forth and returning, in order to acquire what was unknown.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-016.03","page":16,"ar":"وكونه مفيدًا للعلم في الجملة، ولو في الإلهيات، وبدون النظر ضروري.","en":"That [inquiry] yields knowledge in at least some instances, even in divine matters, is evident immediately, without [needing further] inquiry.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-016.04","page":16,"ar":"والمنكر معاند، كالسفسطائي المنكر للحسيات أو الأوليات أو كليهما.","en":"Whoever denies it is obstinate, like the sophist who rejects sensory judgments, first principles, or both.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-016.05","page":16,"ar":"وهل هو بطريق العادة أو التوليد أو الوجوب؟ فيه خلاف.","en":"There is disagreement whether [knowledge results from rational inquiry] through customary concomitance, through generation (tawlīd), or necessarily.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-016.06","page":16,"ar":"والنظر في معرفة الله تعالى واجب بالنص والإجماع، ولكونه مقدمة للمعرفة الواجبة عندنا بذلك.","en":"Inquiry directed toward knowledge of God Most High is obligatory by scriptural text and consensus; for us this is because it is a prerequisite of the knowledge whose obligation is established by those means.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-016.07","page":16,"ar":"وعند المعتزلة لكونها دافعة لضرر خوف العقاب.","en":"According to the Muʿtazila, [it is obligatory] because [knowledge] averts the harm associated with fear of punishment.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-016.08","page":16,"ar":"قالوا: لو لم يجب إلا شرعًا، لما صح إلزام النظر في المعجزة لعدم الوجوب قبل ثبوت الشرع.","en":"They object: if [inquiry] were obligatory only by revelation, it would not be legitimate to require examining a miracle, since no such obligation would exist before revelation’s authority had been established.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-017.01","page":17,"ar":"ورُدَّ بأن المتوقف على الشرع هو العلم بالوجوب، لا نفس الوجوب.","en":"The reply is that what depends upon revelation is *knowledge of the obligation*, not the obligation itself.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-017.02","page":17,"ar":"ثم إنها أول الواجبات المقصودة؛ تتوقف البواقي عليها.","en":"Moreover, [knowledge of God] is the first of the obligations intended for their own sake, for the remaining obligations depend upon it.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-017.03","page":17,"ar":"والنظر فيها وسيلة إليها، فيجب لذلك.","en":"Inquiry concerning it is a means to it, and so is obligatory for that reason.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-017.04","page":17,"ar":"والدليل ما يمكن أن يُتوصّل بالنظر فيه إلى حكم.","en":"A proof (dalīl) is something through consideration of which one can arrive at a judgment.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-017.05","page":17,"ar":"وقد يختص بالجازم، فيقابله الأمارة.","en":"[The term] is sometimes restricted to what establishes certainty; in that usage an indicative sign (amāra) is contrasted with it.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-017.06","page":17,"ar":"ثم إن توقف على نقل فنقلي، وإلا فعقلي.","en":"If it depends on transmission, it is a transmitted proof; otherwise it is a rational proof.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-017.07","page":17,"ar":"وقد يستفاد منه بمعونة القرائن القطع.","en":"With the help of corroborating indications, certainty may be obtained from it [transmission].","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-017.08","page":17,"ar":"ولا يثبت ما استوى طرفاه عند العقل إلا بالنقل، وما يتوقف النقل عليه لا يثبت إلا بالعقل.","en":"What has two alternatives equally balanced for reason is established only by transmission; but that upon which transmission itself depends can be established only by reason.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-017.09","page":17,"ar":"الباب الثاني في الأمور العامة.","en":"Chapter Two: General Matters.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-017.10","page":17,"ar":"تصور الوجود ضروري، والتعريف بالكون والتحقق والشيئية لفظي.","en":"The conception of existence is immediate; defining it by “being,” “actuality,” or “thinghood” is merely verbal.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-017.11","page":17,"ar":"بُني على اشتراكه المعنوي صحةُ التقسيم إلى الواجب ...","en":"The validity of dividing [existence] into the necessary [and other classes] rests upon its possession of a common meaning ...","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-018.01","page":18,"ar":"... وغيره، والجزم به مع التردد في الخصوصية، وتمام الحصر في الموجود والمعدوم.","en":"... and what is other than the necessary; [also] our certainty that it applies while remaining uncertain about a specific determination, and the completeness of the division into existent and nonexistent.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-018.02","page":18,"ar":"وعلى زيادته على الماهية ذهنا صحة سلبه عنها، وإفادة حمله عليها، واكتساب ثبوته لها.","en":"That [existence] is additional to quiddity **in the mind** is shown by the legitimacy of denying it of that quiddity, by the fact that predicating it of the quiddity is informative, and by our needing to establish that it belongs to the quiddity.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-018.03","page":18,"ar":"والحكماء على أن حقيقة الواجب وجود خاص قائم بنفسه مقيم لغيره، مخالف لوجود الممكن في حقيقته.","en":"The philosophers hold that the reality of the Necessary is a particular existence subsisting in itself and sustaining what is other than itself, different in its very reality from contingent existence.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-018.04","page":18,"ar":"ولذا صح تفرده بالقيام بالماهية ذهنا لا عينا، كبياض الجسم مشارك له في عارض الكون.","en":"Accordingly, [the kind of existence under discussion] may be distinguished as attached to a quiddity conceptually, but not as a distinct thing in external reality, as the whiteness of a body shares with that body the incidental characterization of being.","status":"SECOND_PASS_READING_UNRESOLVED"},{"id":"KAL-018.05","page":18,"ar":"المقول على الموجودات بالتشكيك كالنور على الأنوار.","en":"[Existence] is predicated of existents analogically or by gradation (tashkīk), as light is predicated of lights.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-018.06","page":18,"ar":"وما يقال إنه في الكل نفس الماهية فمعناه أنه لا ينفرد كل بتحقق على حدة في الخارج، وإنما هو في العقل.","en":"As for the statement that in every case it is identical with the quiddity: this means that the two do not enjoy separately distinct actualizations in external reality; their distinction is in the intellect.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-018.07","page":18,"ar":"ثم الوجود ينقسم إلى العيني والذهني حقيقة، وإلى اللفظي والخطي مجازا.","en":"Existence is divided, properly speaking, into extramental existence and mental existence, and, figuratively, into verbal and written existence.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-018.08","page":18,"ar":"إذ ليس في اللفظ والخط من الإنسان الشخص والماهية كما في الخارج ...","en":"For, in utterance and writing, the human individual and the human quiddity are not present as they are in external reality ...","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-019.01","page":19,"ar":"... والذهن، بل الاسم وصورته.","en":"... and in the intellect. In utterance and writing there is instead the name and its representation.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-019.02","page":19,"ar":"والدليل على الذهني أنا نعقل ما لا ثبوت له في الخارج إذ نحكم على الممتنعات إيجابا، ونجد من المفهومات كليا ومن القضايا حقيقية.","en":"The proof for mental existence is that we apprehend what has no establishment outside the mind: we make affirmative judgments about impossibilities, and among concepts we find universals and among propositions real [universal] propositions.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-019.03","page":19,"ar":"فالتعقل إن كان بالحصول في الذهن فذاك، وإلا فلا محالة يقتضي إضافة بين العاقل والمعقول.","en":"If intellectual apprehension occurs through [a form’s] being present in the mind, that establishes the point; if it does not, it nevertheless necessarily entails a relation between the apprehender and what is apprehended.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-019.04","page":19,"ar":"ولا تعقل إلى النفي الصرف، وإذ ليس الثبوت في الخارج كان في العقل.","en":"That relation cannot have sheer negation as its term; and, since the relevant establishment is not extramental, it must be in the intellect.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-019.05","page":19,"ar":"وهو وجود غير متأصل لا يقتضي الاتصاف، كالمؤمن يتصور الكفر فلا يوجب اتصاف الذهن بالأعراض حتى المتضادات.","en":"This is a non-fundamental mode of existence that does not entail being qualified by the thing conceived: a believer conceives unbelief, but the mind is not thereby qualified by [the conceived] accidents, even contrary accidents.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-019.06","page":19,"ar":"ولا وجود الممتنع في الخارج لكون الذهني فيه كالماء في البيت.","en":"Nor does this imply external existence for the impossible, as though its mental existence were located externally in the manner of water in a house.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-019.07","page":19,"ar":"ثم المعقول من الوجود والشيئية ليس إلا الثبوت، ومن العدم إلا النفي.","en":"What is understood by existence and thinghood is only establishment (thubūt), and by nonexistence only negation (nafy).","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-019.08","page":19,"ar":"فالمعدوم ليس بشيء ولا ثابت ولا واسطة بينه وبين الموجود.","en":"The nonexistent is not a thing, nor established; there is no intermediate [category] between it and the existent.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-019.09","page":19,"ar":"ومنهم من أثبتهما جمعًا وتفريقًا ويسمى الواسطة حالًا وجعل ...","en":"Some affirm the two [considerations] jointly and separately, calling an intermediary position a state (ḥāl), and also maintain ... [continued on p. 20].","status":"SECOND_PASS_READING_UNRESOLVED"},{"id":"KAL-020.01","page":20,"ar":"... الوجود منه، إذ لو وجد تسلسل، ولو عدم اتصف بالنقيض.","en":"... existence one of those [intermediate states], arguing that if [existence itself] existed an infinite regress would ensue, while if it were nonexistent it would bear its own contradictory.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-020.02","page":20,"ar":"ورُدَّ بأن وجوده عينه، ونقيضه العدم لا المعدوم.","en":"The reply is that its existence is itself, and its contradictory is nonexistence (ʿadam), not the nonexistent (maʿdūm).","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-020.03","page":20,"ar":"قالوا: المعدومات متمايزة، ولا يعقل التميز بدون الثبوت.","en":"They contend that nonexistent objects are distinguishable, while distinction cannot be intelligible without some kind of establishment.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-020.04","page":20,"ar":"والإمكان ثبوتي للفرق بين إمكان له ولا إمكان له، فثبت موصوفه.","en":"They further argue that possibility has a positive character: one distinguishes what possesses possibility from what does not, and the subject to which possibility belongs must therefore be established.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-020.05","page":20,"ar":"قلنا: التميز إنما هو عند العقل، وإلا انتقض بالممتنعات والمركبات الخيالية.","en":"We answer: differentiation resides only in the intellect; otherwise the assertion would be overturned by impossible objects and imaginary composites.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-020.06","page":20,"ar":"وإن الفرق بين الإمكان والإمكان المنفي على تقدير كونه منفيا ثابت أيضا.","en":"Moreover, the distinction between possibility and negated possibility can itself be affirmed even on the hypothesis that [the latter] is negated.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-020.07","page":20,"ar":"ثم كل من الوجود والعدم قد يقع محمولا وقد يقع رابطة.","en":"Both existence and nonexistence may function as predicates, and each may also function as a copula or connective.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-020.08","page":20,"ar":"ويفتقر الحمل الإيجابي إلى اتحاد الطرفين هوية ليصح، وتغايرهما مفهوما ليفيد.","en":"Affirmative predication requires the two terms to be identical as to the subject [or referent] for it to be true, and different in conception for it to be informative.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-020.09","page":20,"ar":"وصدقه يكون بمطابقته لما في نفس الأمر، ومعناه ما يفهم من قولنا: هذا الأمر كذا في نفسه، مع قطع النظر عن حكم الحاكم وإدراك المدرك.","en":"The truth of affirmative predication consists in its agreement with what obtains in the matter itself (nafs al-amr). By this is meant what one understands from saying “This matter is such-and-such in itself,” apart from any person’s judgment or apprehension.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-020.10","page":20,"ar":"فصل: ماهية الشيء ما به يجاب عن السؤال بما هو، وقد تؤخذ بشرط شيء فتسمى المخلوطة، ولا خفاء في وجودها؛ وبشرط ...","en":"Section. A thing’s quiddity is that by which the question “What is it?” is answered. It can be considered under the condition of something additional, and is then called mixed; its existence is beyond dispute. Or [considered] under the condition ...","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-021.01","page":21,"ar":"... لا شيء فتسمى المجردة، ولا توجد في الأذهان فضلا عن الأعيان.","en":"... of nothing additional, and is then called the abstract [quiddity]. It does not exist in minds, much less among extramental individuals.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-021.02","page":21,"ar":"ولا شرط شيء، وهي أعم من المخلوطة، فتوجد لكونها نفسها لا جزءا منها لعدم التغاير، وإنما ذلك في العقل.","en":"Or [quiddity] may be taken without stipulating anything; this is more inclusive than the mixed consideration. It exists as being those very things, not as a distinct constituent of them, since there is no real otherness; such a distinction obtains only in the intellect.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-021.03","page":21,"ar":"ثم إذا اعتبرت معروضة للكل فهو الكلي الطبيعي، وإنما يوجد منه المعروض دون العوارض مجردًا عن العوارض وهي الأفراد.","en":"If [quiddity] is considered as the subject of universality, it is the natural universal. What actually exists is the subject of that characterization, not the mentally attributed accidents as separately existing things; the concrete instances are individuals.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-021.04","page":21,"ar":"وقد يقال الماهية بشرط لا شيء فتكون مادة للشخص متقدمة عليه في الوجودين.","en":"A quiddity is also spoken of as taken on condition of nothing additional; in this use it becomes the matter of the individual and is prior to it in both modes of existence.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-021.05","page":21,"ar":"ثم لا خفاء في وجود الماهية المركبة، ولا بد من انتهائها إلى البسيطة.","en":"There is no doubt that composite quiddities exist, and they must ultimately terminate in simple [quiddities].","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-021.06","page":21,"ar":"واحتياج بعض الأجزاء إلى البعض في المركب الحقيقي ضروري بخلاف الاعتباري.","en":"In a genuine composite, the dependence of some parts upon others is necessary, unlike a composite constituted merely by consideration.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-021.07","page":21,"ar":"ومن خالف في مجعولية الماهية أراد أنها من لوازم الوجود كتناهي الأجسام، لا الماهية كزوجية الأربعة، وإلا فاحتياج الممكن إلى العلة ضروري.","en":"Whoever disputes the quiddity’s being made means that its being made is among the concomitants of existence, like the finitude of bodies, rather than of quiddity, like the evenness of four; otherwise the contingent’s need for a cause is evident.","status":"STAGE56_VISUAL_CORRECTED_1912_PRINT"},{"id":"KAL-022.01","page":22,"ar":"فصل في التعين.","en":"Section: On Individuation (taʿayyun).","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-022.02","page":22,"ar":"أفراد النوع إنما تتمايز بالعوارض، ربما تنتهي إلى ما يفيد المادية.","en":"Individuals of a species are distinguished by accidents, which may ultimately terminate in what supplies materiality.","status":"STAGE65_FULL_PAGE_1912_SINGLE_PRINT_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-022.03","page":22,"ar":"فقد تلخص أن التعين والتشخص هو تلك المادية أو ما يفيدها، أو كون الفرد بحيث لا يقبل الشركة، أو عدم قبوله لها.","en":"Thus, in summary, individuation and particularization may be identified with that materiality or its source, with the individual’s being such that it cannot be shared, or simply with its not admitting sharing.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-022.04","page":22,"ar":"وأن العدمي هو المعدوم أو العدم المضاف أو ما يدخل في مفهومه العدم، والوجودي بخلافه.","en":"“Negative” may mean what is nonexistent, a related privation, or something whose very concept includes nonexistence; “positive” is the opposite.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-022.05","page":22,"ar":"وأن الحقيقي ما له ثبوت في نفس الأمر من غير شائبة فرض وتقدير، والاعتباري بخلافه.","en":"What is real (ḥaqīqī) has establishment in the fact itself without admixture of supposition or stipulation; the considerational (iʿtibārī) is otherwise.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-022.06","page":22,"ar":"لا شبهة أن التعين وجودي أو عدمي ...","en":"There is no doubt that individuation is either positive or negative ...","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-023.01","page":23,"ar":"... حقيقي أو اعتباري.","en":"... real or considerational.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-023.02","page":23,"ar":"ولا شبهة أنه إما يستند إلى الفاعل القادر، أو إلى الوجود الخارجي، أو إلى أسباب أخر.","en":"Individuation must be referred either to a voluntary capable agent, to extramental existence, or to other causes.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-023.03","page":23,"ar":"كنفس الماهية أو المادة المتشخصة بما يلحقها من العوارض بحسب تعاقب الاستعدادات.","en":"Examples are the quiddity itself, or the matter individuated by accidents that attach to it according to the succession of dispositions.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-023.04","page":23,"ar":"فصل: الوجوب والامتناع والإمكان معقولات تحصل من ...","en":"Section: Necessity, impossibility and possibility are intelligibles arising from ...","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-024.01","page":24,"ar":"... نسبة المفهوم إلى الماهية بسيطة أو مركبة، وتصورها ضروري.","en":"... the relation of a concept to a quiddity, whether simple or composite. Their apprehension is immediate.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-024.02","page":24,"ar":"والتعريف بمثل ضرورة الوجود وضرورة العدم ولا ضرورتهما لفظي.","en":"Defining these through such expressions as the necessity of existence, necessity of nonexistence, or the absence of necessity on either side is merely verbal.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-024.03","page":24,"ar":"وتنقسم كل من الأولين إلى الذاتي والغيري.","en":"Each of the first two [necessity and impossibility] divides into intrinsic and derivative kinds.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-024.04","page":24,"ar":"والموصوف بالذاتي من الواجب واجب الوجود لذاته وهو الله تعالى أو لشيء آخر كزوجية الأربعة.","en":"What is called intrinsically necessary may be necessary in its own existence—namely God Most High—or necessary with respect to something else, as the evenness of four is.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-024.05","page":24,"ar":"ومن الممتنع ممتنع الوجود لذاته كشريك الباري أو لشيء آخر كفردية الأربعة.","en":"Among things described as impossible, one is impossible in itself, such as a partner to the Creator; another is impossible with respect to something else, such as four’s being odd.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-024.06","page":24,"ar":"والموصوف بالغيري كممكن هو واجب الوجود حين وجوده وممتنع الوجود حين عدمه.","en":"In the derivative kind, a contingent thing is necessary in respect of its being when it exists and impossible [to be existing] when it does not exist.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-024.07","page":24,"ar":"وقد يؤخذ بمعنى سلب ضرورة الوجود أو العدم، فيسمى بالإمكان العام لعمومه الخاص وضرورة الطرف الآخر.","en":"[Possibility] can be taken as denying the necessity of existence or of nonexistence; this is called general possibility, embracing particular possibility and necessity of the opposite alternative.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-024.08","page":24,"ar":"وقد يعتبر بالنظر إلى الاستقبال ويسمى بالاستقبالي.","en":"It may also be considered with respect to the future, and is then called future possibility.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-024.09","page":24,"ar":"ومعنى تهيؤ المادة لحصول الشيء باعتبار تحقق الشرائط شيئا فشيئا فيسمى بالاستعدادي، وهذا مراد ...","en":"The readiness of matter for something to arise, as the requisite conditions are realized one after another, is called dispositional possibility. This is what is intended ...","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-025.01","page":25,"ar":"من قال: كل حادث مفتقر إلى مادة تكون محلا للإمكان، ومدة بها يكون تعاقب الحوادث، وإنما يتم لو سلّم أن كل حادث بهذا المعنى ممكن.","en":"The person who argues that every originated thing needs matter as the subject of its possibility, and a duration in which events succeed one another, establishes this only if one concedes that every originated thing is possible in precisely this sense.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-025.02","page":25,"ar":"ثم احتياج الممكن إلى المؤثر بامتناع ترجيح أحد طرفيه بلا مرجح ضروري.","en":"The contingent’s need for an efficient determinant is necessary [knowledge], because one of its alternatives cannot prevail without a preponderating ground.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-025.03","page":25,"ar":"وهذا غير ترجيح المختار أحد المتساويين على الآخر بالتخصيص بمحض الإرادة.","en":"This is distinct from an agent’s freely selecting one of two equivalent options rather than the other, solely through the particular determination of will.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-025.04","page":25,"ar":"كالهارب يسلك أحد الطريقين والجائع يأكل أحد الرغيفين.","en":"For instance, a fleeing person takes one of two routes and a hungry person eats one of two loaves.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-025.05","page":25,"ar":"فإن قيل: قبل التأثير حال الوجود تحصيل الحاصل، وحال العدم جمع بين النقيضين.","en":"If it is said: prior to the causal operation, in the state of existence, producing the effect would be producing what already exists; and in the state of nonexistence it would combine contradictories.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-025.06","page":25,"ar":"قلنا: الممتنع تحصيل الحاصل بتحصيل آخر، والموجب هو الإمكان أو الحدوث، ولكل وجهة.","en":"We reply: what is impossible is producing an already-produced thing through a *second* production. The ground of causal dependence is [variously held to be] possibility or origination, and each view has its argument.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-025.07","page":25,"ar":"ومعنى الاحتياج إما توقف الوجود أو العدم أو استمرارهما على أمر ما.","en":"The meaning of dependence is that existence, nonexistence, or the persistence of either depends upon something.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-025.08","page":25,"ar":"ولا تعقل أولوية بالذات لأحد الطرفين ...","en":"No intrinsic precedence or preferability of either alternative is intelligible ...","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-026.01","page":26,"ar":"... إلا بمعنى نوع اقتضاء الوجود أو العدم لا إلى حد الوجوب.","en":"... only in the sense of a kind of inclination toward existence or nonexistence, not reaching the point of necessity.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-026.02","page":26,"ar":"وهي أيضًا منتفية وإلا لما تحقق الطرف الآخر لاستلزامه انتفاء الأولوية الذاتية.","en":"Even such an intrinsic tendency must be denied: otherwise the opposite alternative could not obtain, because it would entail the absence of the supposed intrinsic preference.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-026.03","page":26,"ar":"ثم وجود الممكن محفوف بوجوبين: سابق ولاحق.","en":"The existence of a possible thing is surrounded by two necessitations: one prior and one subsequent.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-026.04","page":26,"ar":"لأنه ما لم يجب لم يوجد، لامتناع الترجيح بلا مرجح.","en":"For unless its existence becomes necessitated it does not come to exist, because one alternative cannot prevail without a determinant.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-026.05","page":26,"ar":"وحين الوجود امتنع العدم لامتناع الجمع.","en":"While it exists, its nonexistence is impossible, because contradictories cannot occur together.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-026.06","page":26,"ar":"وهذا لا ينافي الاختيار.","en":"This does not negate voluntary choice.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-026.07","page":26,"ar":"والثلاثة، بل كل ما يوصف، أي فرد يفرض","en":"And the three [modal qualifications]—indeed, everything that is predicated—[are considered] in respect of any individual that may be supposed. [The sentence continues on the next printed page.]","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-027.01","page":27,"ar":"... منه بمفهومه كالقدم والحدوث والوحدة والكثرة والبقاء والتعين.","en":"... of which [one can suppose] its concept, as with pre-eternity, origination, unity, plurality, persistence and individuation.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-027.02","page":27,"ar":"والموصوفة اعتبارات عقلية ولا يلزم التسلسل.","en":"Such ascriptions are rational considerations; an infinite regress does not follow.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-027.03","page":27,"ar":"ومعنى كون الشيء واجبًا في الخارج أنه بحيث إذا عُقل مستندًا إلى الوجود لزم في العقل معقول هو الوجوب، وكذا البواقي.","en":"That something is necessary outside the mind means that, when it is apprehended as grounded in existence, the mind necessarily apprehends the intelligible called necessity. The same holds for the other [modal and general notions].","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-027.04","page":27,"ar":"فصل: القدم بمعنى عدم المسبوقية بالغير، وهو الذاتي، أو بالعدم، وهو الزماني؛ والحدوث بخلافه.","en":"Section. Pre-eternity means not being preceded by another, which is essential priority; or not being preceded by nonexistence, which is temporal priority. Origination is the opposite.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-027.05","page":27,"ar":"ولا قديم بالذات سوى الله تعالى، وبالزمان سوى صفاته.","en":"Nothing besides God Most High is pre-eternal in itself; and [nothing] besides His attributes [is pre-eternal] in time.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-027.06","page":27,"ar":"ولزم المعتزلة كثير من الأحوال وعند الفلاسفة كثير.","en":"The Muʿtazila are thereby committed to numerous states (aḥwāl), and among the philosophers to numerous [such cases; the second noun is left unexpressed in the print].","status":"STAGE59_SEMANTIC_UNRESOLVED_AFTER_ARABIC_VISUAL_CHECK"},{"id":"KAL-027.07","page":27,"ar":"ولا يُستند القديم إلى المختار لأن القصد إلى الإيجاد يقارن العدم ضرورة.","en":"A pre-eternal thing is not referred to a voluntary agent, because the intention to bring something into being necessarily accompanies [its] nonexistence.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-027.08","page":27,"ar":"ولا يمكن عدمه لكونه واجبًا أو مستندًا إليه إيجابًا.","en":"Its nonexistence is not possible, since it is necessary or referred to what is necessary in a necessitating manner.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-028.00","page":28,"ar":"قاعدة.","en":"Rule.","status":"STAGE65_NEW_PRINTED_HEADING_VISUALLY_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-028.01","page":28,"ar":"التقدم والتأخر والمعية تكون بالعلية أو بالطبع أو بالزمان أو بالشرف أو الرتبة الحسية أو العقلية وضعًا أو طبعًا أو بالذات.","en":"Priority, posteriority, and simultaneity may be by causality, nature, time, excellence, sensory or intellectual rank, conventional placement, natural placement, or by essence.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-028.02","page":28,"ar":"فسبق العدم على الحادث لا يلزم أن يكون بالزمان ليلزم قدم الزمان.","en":"Therefore nonexistence’s precedence over an originated thing need not be *temporal*, so that the pre-eternity of time would be inferred.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-028.03","page":28,"ar":"كما لا يلزم أن يكون له إمكان استعدادي ليلزم قدم مادة له.","en":"Nor does it follow that [the originated thing] must possess dispositional possibility, such that matter would have to be pre-eternal for it.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-028.04","page":28,"ar":"فصل: الوحدة والكثرة من المعاني الواضحة.","en":"Section. Unity and plurality are among the self-evident meanings.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-028.05","page":28,"ar":"ومقوليتهما بالتشكيك.","en":"Their predication is by gradation (tashkīk).","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-028.06","page":28,"ar":"فتكون جهة الوحدة مقومة أو عارضة أو منتسبة.","en":"The aspect of unity may be constitutive, accidental, or relational.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-028.07","page":28,"ar":"وتسمى الوحدة في الجنس مجانسة، وفي النوع مماثلة.","en":"Unity in genus is called *mujānasa* (sharing a genus), and unity in species *mumāthala* (sharing a species).","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-028.08","page":28,"ar":"وفي الكم مساواة، وفي الكيف مشابهة.","en":"In quantity [it is called] equality; in quality, similarity.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-028.09","page":28,"ar":"وفي الخاصة مشاكلة، وفي الأطراف مطابقة.","en":"With regard to a distinguishing property, [it is] correspondence (mushākala); with regard to boundaries or extremities, matching (muṭābaqa).","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-028.10","page":28,"ar":"وفي الوضع موازاة، وفي النسبة مناسبة.","en":"With regard to position, parallelism; and with regard to relation, proportion.","status":"1912_PRINT_SECOND_PASS_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-029.01","page":29,"ar":"ويمتنع اتحاد الاثنين ضرورة.","en":"It is immediately necessary that two distinct things cannot be identical as one.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-029.02","page":29,"ar":"والاستدلال عليه بأن اختلاف الماهيتين أو الهويتين ذاتي لا يزول ليس بأوضح من المدعى.","en":"The purported proof that the difference between two quiddities or individuated identities is essential and cannot vanish is no more evident than the proposition to be proved.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-029.03","page":29,"ar":"وبأنهما إما موجودان أو معدومان أو مختلفان فلا اتحاد.","en":"A further argument claims that the two are either both existent, both nonexistent, or different in that respect; no [numerical] identity is thereby established.","status":"STAGE65_FULL_PAGE_1912_SINGLE_PRINT_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-029.04","page":29,"ar":"مدفوع بأنهما موجودان بوجود واحد هو نفس الوجودين الصائرين واحدًا.","en":"This is countered [with the supposition] that both exist by one existence which is the very two existences having become one.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-029.05","page":29,"ar":"والغيرية نقيض الهوهوية، وقد يخص الغيران بوجودين يجوز انفكاكهما.","en":"Otherness (ghayriyya) is the contrary of identity (huwahuwiyya); yet the appellation “two others” is sometimes restricted to two existents capable of separation.","status":"STAGE65_FULL_PAGE_1912_SINGLE_PRINT_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-029.06","page":29,"ar":"كما في الجزء مع الكل ليس هو ولا غيره، وكذا الصفة مع الموصوف.","en":"Thus a part, in relation to its whole, is neither simply identical with it nor other than it; likewise an attribute in relation to what it qualifies.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-029.07","page":29,"ar":"ولذا صح ما في الدار غير زيد وغير عشرة مع أن فيها الأجزاء والصفات الغير المحمولة.","en":"Hence it can be correct to say “There is nothing in the house other than Zayd,” or “other than ten,” even if their parts and certain nonpredicable attributes are there.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-029.08","page":29,"ar":"فليس المعنى أنه لا هو بحسب المفهوم ولا غيره بحسب ...","en":"So the intended meaning is not that it is “not identical” in the conceptual sense, and “not other” in the sense of ...","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-030.01","page":30,"ar":"... الوجود، والتماثل الاشتراك في الصفات النفسية، ولذا ليس كل منهما ضد الآخر.","en":"… existence. Similarity is sharing the essential attributes; consequently, two distinct things need not be contraries.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-030.02","page":30,"ar":"واختلف في لزوم تغايرهما وامتناع اجتماعهما.","en":"There is disagreement about whether they must be other than one another and incapable of coexisting.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-030.03","page":30,"ar":"والتضاد كون المعنيين بحيث يستحيل لذاتهما اجتماعهما في محل واحد من جهة واحدة.","en":"Contrariety (taḍādd) is the condition of two meanings such that, of themselves, they cannot both belong to one subject in the same respect.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-030.04","page":30,"ar":"وعند الفلاسفة كل اثنين غيران إن اشتركا في تمام الماهية فمثلان وإلا فمختلفان.","en":"According to the philosophers, two distinct things are alike if they share the entire quiddity, but different in kind otherwise.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-030.05","page":30,"ar":"وهما متقابلان إن امتنع اجتماعهما في محل واحد من جهة واحدة، فإن كانا وجوديين فإن كان تعقل أحدهما بالقياس إلى الآخر فمتضايفان، وإلا فمتضادان.","en":"They are opposed when they cannot coexist in one subject in the same respect. If both are positive, and the conception of one is made by reference to the other, they are correlatives; otherwise, they are contraries.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-030.06","page":30,"ar":"وإن لم [يكونا وجوديين] فإن قيد بكون الموضوع مستعدا للوجودي شخصه أو نوعه أو جنسه القريب أو البعيد فملكة وعدم.","en":"If they are not both positive existents, and the subject’s preparedness for the positive member is stipulated—whether individually, by species, or by proximate or remote genus—the opposition is that of possession and privation.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-030.07","page":30,"ar":"وإلا فإيجاب وسلب.","en":"Otherwise the opposition is affirmation and negation.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-030.08","page":30,"ar":"وقد يشترط في التضاد غاية الخلاف ويختص باسم الحقيقي، والأول بالمشهور.","en":"The greatest possible difference is sometimes required for contrariety: this is called contrariety in the strict sense, while the former is the customary sense.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-030.09","page":30,"ar":"وقد يشترط في الملكة والعدم الاستعداد للوجودي في ذلك الوقت ويختص باسم المشهوري، والأول الحقيقي.","en":"Some make receptivity for the positive form at that very time a condition of possession and privation, calling that the customary use and the former the strict use.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-030.10","page":30,"ar":"ولا تقابل بين الوحدة والكثرة لتغاير موضوعيهما، ولتقوّم أحدهما بالآخر.","en":"Unity and plurality are not opposites in the same sense, because their subjects differ and one is constituted in terms of the other.","status":"STAGE65_FULL_PAGE_1912_SINGLE_PRINT_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-031.01","page":31,"ar":"فصل في العلة والمعلول.","en":"Section: On Cause and Effect.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-031.02","page":31,"ar":"العلة هي ما يحتاج إليه الشيء.","en":"A cause is that upon which a thing depends.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-031.03","page":31,"ar":"فإن كانت داخلة فوجوب الشيء معها، إما بالفعل فهي صورية، وإما بالقوة فهي مادية.","en":"If the cause is intrinsic [to the thing], the thing’s being necessitated together with it is either in actuality, in which case it is a formal cause, or in potentiality, in which case it is a material cause.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-031.04","page":31,"ar":"وإن كانت خارجة فالشيء إما بها فهي فاعلية أو لها فهي غائية.","en":"If the cause lies outside the thing, the thing is either [brought about] by it, in which case it is an efficient cause, or is for its sake, in which case it is a final cause.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-031.05","page":31,"ar":"ومرجع الشروط والآلات إلى الفاعل.","en":"Conditions and instruments are referred back to the efficient agent.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-031.06","page":31,"ar":"وجميع ما يتوقف عليه الشيء يسمى علة تامة.","en":"The totality of that upon which a thing depends is called its complete cause.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-031.07","page":31,"ar":"وعند تمام الفاعل يجب وجود المعلول لامتناع الترجيح بلا مرجح.","en":"When the agent [together with all that its action requires] is complete, the effect must exist, because [its] becoming actual without a determinant is impossible.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-031.08","page":31,"ar":"وبالعكس، لأن الاحتياج من لوازم الإمكان.","en":"And conversely [the existence of an effect requires its complete cause], because dependence is among the concomitants of possibility.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-031.09","page":31,"ar":"ووجوده مع انعدامها إنما يتصور في المعدات، كالابن بعد الأب والبناء بعد البنّاء.","en":"An effect can continue to exist when the antecedent causes have passed away only in the case of preparatory causes, such as a son after his father, or a building after its builder.","status":"STAGE56_VISUAL_CORRECTED_1912_PRINT"},{"id":"KAL-031.10","page":31,"ar":"والمؤثر في الوجود قد يغاير المؤثر في البقاء.","en":"The cause responsible for bringing a thing into existence may differ from the cause of its persistence.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-031.11","page":31,"ar":"ووحدة المعلول بالشخص توجب وحدة الفاعل لامتناع الاحتياج والاستغناء معا ...","en":"The numerical unity of an effect entails the unity of its efficient cause, since it is impossible for it simultaneously to be dependent and independent ...","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-032.01","page":32,"ar":"... ولا عكس، لاستناد الكل إلى الواجب تعالى ابتداء.","en":"... but the converse does not hold, since everything ultimately depends upon the Necessary Existent, Most High, directly.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-032.02","page":32,"ar":"والاستدلال بأنه لو لم يصدر من الواحد إلا الواحد لزم اتحاد السلسلة والعلة فيما بين كل شيئين ضعيف.","en":"The argument that if only one thing proceeds from one source, the causal series and the cause between every pair of things would become identical is weak.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-032.03","page":32,"ar":"وتمسك المخالف بأنه لو صدر عنه شيئان فمصدريته لهذا غير مصدريته لذاك.","en":"The opponent argues that, if two things proceeded from it, its being source of one would differ from its being source of the other.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-032.04","page":32,"ar":"فإن دخل شيء منهما فيه تركب، وإلا تسلسل.","en":"If either of these source-relations entered into [its essence], it would be composite; otherwise an infinite regress would ensue.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-032.05","page":32,"ar":"ورد بأنها اعتبار عقلي، وبأنه يرد على صدور الواحد.","en":"The reply is that [these differences in being-source] are intellectual considerations, and that the same objection arises even when a single effect proceeds.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-032.06","page":32,"ar":"وقولهم: المراد أنه كلما تكثّر المعلول تكثّر الفاعل ولو بالحيثية.","en":"Their further claim is that what is intended is this: whenever the effect is multiplied, the agent is multiplied as well, even if only with respect to an aspect of agency.","status":"STAGE56_VISUAL_CORRECTED_1912_PRINT"},{"id":"KAL-032.07","page":32,"ar":"ضرورة أن فاعليته لهذا غير فاعليته لذاك لا يفيد شيئا.","en":"For the assertion that its agency toward this is other than its agency toward that establishes nothing [to the point].","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-032.08","page":32,"ar":"ولا يوافق ما بنوا عليه من امتناع تعدد أثر البسيط.","en":"Nor does this fit the principle on which [the philosophers] based their argument: that a simple source cannot produce multiple effects.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-032.09","page":32,"ar":"ومن أن الفاعل البسيط لا يكون","en":"And [they argue further] that a simple efficient agent cannot be ...","status":"STAGE57_NEW_SOURCE_CLAUSE_DIRECT_VISUAL_CHECK"},{"id":"KAL-033.01","page":33,"ar":"... قابلًا لأن الفعل والقبول أمران.","en":"... receptive [to the effect], since acting and receiving are two distinct considerations.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-033.02","page":33,"ar":"وقد يستدل بأن نسبة الفاعل بالوجوب والقابل بالإمكان.","en":"It is argued that the efficient cause bears a relation of necessity, while the recipient bears a relation of possibility.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-033.03","page":33,"ar":"ورد بعد التسليم بأنه لا امتناع في الوجوب واللاوجوب بجهتين.","en":"Even if this is granted, the answer is that necessity and non-necessity in different respects are not incompatible.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-033.04","page":33,"ar":"فصل: يجوز دوام أفعال القوى الجسمانية بخلق الله تعالى.","en":"Section. The actions of bodily powers may persist indefinitely by God’s creation.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-033.05","page":33,"ar":"وعند الفلاسفة يلزم تناهيها بحسب الشدة والمدة والعدة.","en":"According to the philosophers, these must be finite in intensity, duration and number.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-033.06","page":33,"ar":"لأن القسري يختلف باختلاف القابل، والطبيعي باختلاف الفاعل.","en":"For forced motion differs according to differences in the recipient, whereas natural motion differs according to differences in the agent.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-033.07","page":33,"ar":"فإذا فرض في حركتيهما الاتحاد في المبدأ تفاوت الجانب الآخر.","en":"Thus, if the two motions are supposed equal at their starting point, they must differ at the other end.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-033.08","page":33,"ar":"ورد بعد تسليم التأثير بأنه إنما يتم لو كانت القوة بقدر الجسم.","en":"The response, even granting the causal influence [of corporeal power], is that the proof succeeds only if power is proportional to the magnitude of the body.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-033.09","page":33,"ar":"فصل: يستحيل الدور، وهو توقف الشيء على ما توقف عليه.","en":"Section. Circular dependence is impossible: it consists in a thing’s depending on what itself depends upon that very thing.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-033.10","page":33,"ar":"لأن امتناع تقدم الشيء على نفسه ضروري.","en":"For it is immediately necessary that a thing cannot precede itself.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-033.11","page":33,"ar":"والتسلسل هو تراقي معروضي العلية والمعلولية لا إلى نهاية، لأن المؤثر ...","en":"Infinite regress is an endless ascent through things bearing the relations of cause and effect, since the productive cause ...","status":"STAGE65_FULL_PAGE_1912_SINGLE_PRINT_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-034.01","page":34,"ar":"... المستقل للجملة ليس نفسها ولا جزءا منها للدور، بل خارجًا واجبًا.","en":"... the independently sufficient ground of the whole cannot be the whole itself, nor a part of it, on pain of circularity; rather it must be external to the whole, and necessary.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-034.02","page":34,"ar":"يوجب شيئًا من الجملة فينقطع.","en":"That external necessary cause necessitates one of the members of the collection, and thus the regress terminates.","status":"STAGE56_VISUAL_CORRECTED_1912_PRINT"},{"id":"KAL-034.03","page":34,"ar":"ولأنّا نفصل من السلسلة جملة بنقصان واحد، ثم نطبق بين الجملتين.","en":"We may also take from the series a totality shorter by one member, and then align the two collections.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-034.04","page":34,"ar":"فإن وقع بإزاء كل جزء من التامة جزء من الناقصة لزم تساوي الكل والجزء.","en":"If each member of the complete series corresponds to a member of the deficient series, the whole would equal its proper part.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-034.05","page":34,"ar":"وإلا انقطعت الناقصة فتناهت التامة.","en":"If not, the deficient series terminates, and so does the supposedly complete series.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-034.06","page":34,"ar":"ولأنها لما اشتملت على معلول محض لزم اشتمالها على علة محضة تحقيقًا للتكافؤ.","en":"Because the series contains a purely dependent effect, it must also contain a purely independent cause if [its members’ causal statuses] are to balance.","status":"STAGE59_1912_CLAUSE_RECHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-034.07","page":34,"ar":"ولأنّا نجعل كلا من الآحاد التي فوقه متعددًا باعتبار وصفي العلية والمعلولية.","en":"For we may consider each higher member as two in respect of its characterizations as both cause and effect.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-034.08","page":34,"ar":"ثم نطبق بين وصفي العلية والمعلولية فيلزم لضرورة سبق العلية زيادة العلية وتناهيان.","en":"Then, aligning the series considered under the attributes of causehood and effecthood, the necessary priority of the cause entails an excess of causehood and termination.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-034.09","page":34,"ar":"ولأنه لو انقسمت بمتساويين فزوج، وإلا ففرد، وكل منهما أقل بواحد مما فوقه فتتناهيان.","en":"Furthermore, if [the number] admits division into two equal parts it is even; otherwise odd. In either case it is one less than what is above it, and the two [sequences] would accordingly be finite.","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-035.01","page":35,"ar":"خاتمة: قد يقال الصورة لكل هيئة في قابل وحداني بالذات أو بالاعتبار.","en":"Conclusion. The term “form” may be applied to any configuration in a receptive subject that is one either essentially or by consideration.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-035.02","page":35,"ar":"والمادة محلها كالبياض والجسم.","en":"Matter is its receptive substrate, as the body is the substrate of whiteness.","status":"STAGE56_VISUAL_CORRECTED_1912_PRINT"},{"id":"KAL-035.03","page":35,"ar":"والغاية لما ينتهي إليه الفعل، وإن لم يكن له جهة علية واحتياج من الفعل إليه.","en":"An end is that toward which an action tends, even when it has no [real] aspect of causing the action or of the action’s depending upon it.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-035.04","page":35,"ar":"بل وإن لم يكن للفاعل قصد.","en":"Indeed, even when the agent has no intention [toward that end].","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-035.05","page":35,"ar":"ولما كان الموجد عندنا هو الله وحده، فمعنى العلية والتأثير في الممكن هو التسبيب العادي.","en":"Since, according to us, God alone brings things into existence, the meaning of causality and efficacy among contingent things is customary occasioning (al-tasabbub al-ʿādī).","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-035.06","page":35,"ar":"الباب الثالث في الأعراض. وفيه فصول. الفصل الأول.","en":"Chapter Three: Accidents. It contains several sections. Section One.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-035.07","page":35,"ar":"الموجود إن لم يسبق بالعدم فقديم وإلا فحادث.","en":"An existent that was not preceded by nonexistence is pre-eternal; otherwise it is originated.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-035.08","page":35,"ar":"فإن تحيز بذاته فهو جوهر أو بتبعيته فعرض مختص بالحيز ...","en":"If it is spatially located through itself, it is a substance; if through dependence upon another, it is an accident characterized by spatial location—[continued on the following page].","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-036.01","page":36,"ar":"... كالحياة والعلم والإدراكات، أو غير مختص كالأكوان والمحسوسات.","en":"... such as life, knowledge and acts of perception, or not confined [to a single subject], such as spatial states and sensible conditions.","status":"STAGE59_1912_CLAUSE_RECHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-036.02","page":36,"ar":"وقالوا: الموجود إن كان وجوده لا في موضوع، فجوهر، وإلا فعرض.","en":"The philosophers say: if an existent’s existence is not in a subject (lā fī mawḍūʿ), then it is a substance; otherwise it is an accident.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-036.03","page":36,"ar":"وهو أن يستغني عن محل يقوّمه، وسُمّي الموضوع.","en":"This means that it has no need of a subject that sustains it; that sustaining locus is called a “subject” (mawḍūʿ).","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-036.04","page":36,"ar":"والعرض أجناسه الكم والكيف والأين والإضافة ومتى والوضع والملك وأن يفعل وأن ينفعل.","en":"The genera of accidents are quantity, quality, place (where), relation, time (when), position, possession, acting and being acted upon.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-036.05","page":36,"ar":"وامتناع قيام العرض بنفسه، أو بأكثر من محل واحد بالذات أو بالاجتماع، كوحدة العشرة وحياة البنية المتجزئة، ضروري.","en":"That an accident cannot subsist by itself, or subsist in more than one individual bearer either intrinsically or collectively—as in the unity of ten or the life of an aggregate structure—is immediately evident.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-036.06","page":36,"ar":"والعرض في مثل القرب والجوار والتركيب متعددة.","en":"In cases such as proximity, adjacency, and composition, there is a plurality of accidents [despite the print’s awkward singular «العرض»].","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-036.07","page":36,"ar":"ويستحيل انتقاله من محل لأن وجوده في نفسه هو وجوده ...","en":"Its transfer from one subject to another is impossible, because its existence in itself is precisely its existence ...","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-037.01","page":37,"ar":"... في محله، ولأن تشخصه ليس إلا بمحله.","en":"... in its bearer, and because its individuation is only through that bearer.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-037.02","page":37,"ar":"وقد تُوُهِّم من حدوث المثل في المجاور أنه انتقال، وفي جواز انتقاله بالعرض خلاف مبني على الاختلاف في معنى القيام: أنه التبعية في التحيز أو الاختصاص الناعت.","en":"The arising of a like accident in an adjoining locus has been mistaken for a transfer. Whether an accident can be transferred is disputed, because inherence (qiyām) is variously understood as dependence in occupying place or as a qualifying attachment to a subject.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-037.03","page":37,"ar":"وأن الجمهور من المتكلمين على امتناع بقاء العرض زمانين.","en":"Most kalām theologians maintain that an accident cannot persist through two instants of time.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-037.04","page":37,"ar":"لأن مفهومه ينبئ عن ذلك؛ ولأنه يستلزم قيام عرض البقاء به، ولامتناع زواله لأنه إما بنفسه فيمتنع أو بزوال شرطه فيتسلسل.","en":"[They argue] that its concept implies this; that persistence would require an additional accident of persistence inhering in it; and that its cessation would be impossible, since it would occur either by itself (which is impossible) or through the removal of a condition (leading to regress).","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-037.05","page":37,"ar":"أو بطريان ضده فيدور أو بفاعل فيصير النفي المحض أثرًا، والكل ضعيف.","en":"Or [the accident’s cessation would occur] through the arrival of its contrary—yielding a circle—or through an agent, in which case sheer nonexistence would become an effect. All these arguments are weak.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-038.01","page":38,"ar":"فصل: الكم عرض يقبل القسمة لذاته بمعنى فرض شيء غير شيء.","en":"Section: Quantity is an accident which admits division intrinsically, that is, supposing a part distinct from another part.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-038.02","page":38,"ar":"فمنفصل إن لم يكن لأجزائه حد مشترك وهو العدد.","en":"It is discrete if its parts have no common boundary; this is number.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-038.03","page":38,"ar":"ومتصل إن كان، وهو إن كان غير قار فزمان، وإلا فمقدار خط أو سطح أو جسم تعليمي.","en":"It is continuous if they do have one. If it is nonpersistent [in its parts], it is time; otherwise it is a magnitude: a line, surface, or mathematical body.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-038.04","page":38,"ar":"وقد يؤخذ مع إضافة فيسمّى الطول والعرض والعمق.","en":"Considered with an added relation or determination, these are called length, breadth, and depth.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-038.05","page":38,"ar":"وعند المتكلمين العدد اعتباري والمقادير جواهر مجتمعة، أو نهايات وانقطاعات.","en":"According to the theologians, number is a considerational notion; spatial magnitudes are either aggregated substances or their boundaries and terminations.","status":"STAGE59_1912_CLAUSE_RECHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-038.06","page":38,"ar":"والزمان وهمي إذ لا وجود للماضي والمستقبل، ووجود الحاضر يستلزم وجود الجزء أولًا.","en":"Time, in the theologians’ account, is imaginary: neither the past nor the future exists, while existence of a present interval would require a first [indivisible] part.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-038.07","page":38,"ar":"ولأن تقدم أجزائه ليس إلا بالزمان فيتسلسل، ولأنه لو وجد لامتنع عدمه بعد وجوده لكونه زمانيًا، فيلزم وجوبه مع تركبه وتناقضه.","en":"For the priority of its parts would itself be temporal, generating a regress. Were time to exist, its nonexistence after its existence would be impossible because that would itself be temporal; this would entail its necessity despite its composition and contradiction.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-038.08","page":38,"ar":"ورد بأن الماضي والمستقبل موجودان، والعدم في الحال لا يستلزم العدم مطلقا، والتقدم بالذات، وبعدية العدم في طرف الماضي، ولو سلم فامتناع العدم بعد الوجود لا ينافي الإمكان.","en":"The response distinguishes the existence of past and future from the absence of something at the present instant: absence at that instant does not entail absolute nonexistence. It also invokes priority by essence and the subsequent nonexistence on the past side. Even if the disputed premise is conceded, the impossibility of nonexistence after existence does not negate possibility.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-038.09","page":38,"ar":"وقالوا: الزمان وجود ممتد متصف بالماضي والاستقبال ويلحقه التقدم والتأخر بالذات بحيث ...","en":"The philosophers say that time is a continuous extended existent subject to descriptions of pastness and futurity, and intrinsically to priority and posteriority, such that ...","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-039.01","page":39,"ar":"... لا يصير قبله بعد ولا بعده قبل، ضروري تعرف به العامة، ولهذا يقسمونه إلى السنين والشهور والأيام والساعات.","en":"... what comes before does not become after, nor what comes after become before. [Time] is immediately known even to ordinary people; hence they divide it into years, months, days, and hours.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-039.02","page":39,"ar":"وأما حقيقته فقيل مقدار حركة الفلك الأعظم، لأنه لتفاوته كمّ.","en":"As to its reality, one account makes time the magnitude of the motion of the outermost celestial sphere; because it admits degrees of greater and lesser duration, it is a quantity.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK","editorial_note":"The 1912 print continues beyond «الفلك الأعظم» with «لأنه لتفاوته كم». The exact argument is corroborated in the author’s Sharḥ al-Maqāṣid, but the latter is not a Tahdhīb witness. | Recover the omitted quantitative premise «لأنه لتفاوته كم» rather than presenting the view without its first proof."},{"id":"KAL-039.03","page":39,"ar":"ولامتناع تألفه من الآنات متصل، ولعدم استقراره مقدار هيئة غير قارة هي الحركة.","en":"Because it cannot be composed of successive, indivisible instants, time is continuous; and because it does not remain fixed, it measures a non-abiding disposition—namely motion. [The exact wording in the condensed print remains under single-print review.]","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK","editorial_note":"Sharḥ al-Maqāṣid explains the two distinct arguments: against a sum of instants, and from the non-abiding nature of motion."},{"id":"KAL-039.04","page":39,"ar":"ولامتناع فنائه [قراءة رابطة الاستنتاج غير محسومة] مقدار الحركة المستديرة إذ المستقيمة تنقطع.","en":"Since time cannot simply cease, the philosophers associate its measure with circular movement, which can be continuous; rectilinear movement, by contrast, comes to an end. [The precise linking verb of the Cairo print awaits a second direct Tahdhīb witness.]","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK","editorial_note":"The 1912 print clearly establishes non-cessation and circular rather than rectilinear movement; the intermediate inferential verb remains unresolved. Do NOT silently import the parallel. | Restore the logical grounds and keep uncertainty about exact connecting form explicit."},{"id":"KAL-039.05","page":39,"ar":"ولتقدير جميع الحركات به مقدار الأسرع منها، ومبناه على أصول الفلاسفة.","en":"Because all motions are measured by it, it is the measure associated with the fastest of them. The account rests upon the philosophers’ principles.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-039.06","page":39,"ar":"وقيل متجدد معلوم يقدَّر به متجدد موهوم.","en":"Another account calls time a known renewed occurrence by which an imagined renewed occurrence is measured.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-039.07","page":39,"ar":"والقدماء على أنه جوهر مستقل يقطع بوجوده وإن لم يوجد جسم ولا حركة.","en":"Some ancients hold that [time] is an independent substance whose existence is certain even in the absence of bodies and motion.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-039.08","page":39,"ar":"فصل في المكان: قيل هو السطح الباطن من الجسم الحاوي المماس للظاهر ...","en":"Section: On Place. It has been said to be the inner surface of the containing body, in contact with the outer surface ...","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-040.01","page":40,"ar":"... من المحوي.","en":"... of the contained body.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-040.02","page":40,"ar":"وقيل البعد الذي ينفذ فيه بعد الجسم، والأمارات مثل مساواة المكان للمتمكن وعمومه لكل جسم وكون الطير في الهواء المتحرك والحجر في الماء الجاري ساكنًا.","en":"Others say it is the extension penetrated by the body’s magnitude. The indications include equality between place and what occupies it, that every body has a place, and the possibility of describing a bird as at rest within moving air or a stone as at rest within flowing water.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-040.03","page":40,"ar":"كلها تدل على الثاني. وهل يجوز خلوه عن الشاغل؟","en":"All these indications support the second account [that place is an extension penetrated by a body]. Can a place be empty of an occupant?","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-040.04","page":40,"ar":"قيل نعم، لأنّا إذا رفعنا صفيحة ملساء عن مثلها لزم في أول زمان الارتفاع خلوّ الوسط.","en":"Some answer yes: if we raise a perfectly smooth plate from another similar plate, the space between them must initially be empty.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-040.05","page":40,"ar":"وإذا رفعنا أحد جانبي الزق المشدود الرأس والمسام عن الآخر خلا جوفه.","en":"Likewise, if one side of a sealed skin-vessel whose neck and pores are closed is raised away from the other, its interior would be empty.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-040.06","page":40,"ar":"وقيل لا، وإلا لزم تساوي وجود المعاوق وعدمه ...","en":"Others say no: otherwise the presence and absence of a resisting medium would be equivalent ...","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-040.07","page":40,"ar":"فإنّا إذا فرضنا حركة جسم في فرسخ خلاء ولتكن ساعة وأخرى مثلها في ملاء، ولتكن ساعتين ...","en":"Suppose a body crosses a farsakh of void in one hour, and the same distance through a filled medium in two hours ...","status":"STAGE59_1912_CLAUSE_RECHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-041.01","page":41,"ar":"... وأخرى مثلها في ملاء قوامه نصف قوام الأول فيكون ساعة ضرورة أن تفاوت الزمان بحسب تفاوت المعاوق.","en":"... and through another medium half as resistant as the first, it would [by this assumption] take one hour, since differences in time track differences in resistance.","status":"STAGE59_1912_CLAUSE_RECHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-041.02","page":41,"ar":"ومن أماراته ارتفاع اللحم في المحجمة والماء في الأنبوبة وعدم نزول الماء من قبة الكوز المسدود الرأس والمخرق مستظهر من الجانبين.","en":"Other indications are flesh rising into a cupping cup, water in a tube, and water’s failure to descend from a vessel with its mouth sealed, as observed in devices arranged from both sides.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-041.03","page":41,"ar":"فصل في الكيف: عرض لا يقبل لذاته قسمة ولا نسبة.","en":"Section: On Quality. An accident which, in itself, admits neither division nor relation.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-041.04","page":41,"ar":"وأقسامه بحسب الاستقراء أربعة.","en":"Its divisions according to induction are four.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-041.05","page":41,"ar":"الأول المحسوسات، وأصول الملموسات الحرارة والبرودة والرطوبة واليبوسة.","en":"The first class is sensible qualities. The fundamental tangible qualities are heat, cold, moisture and dryness.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-041.06","page":41,"ar":"وقد يقال الحار لما يحدث الحرارة إما بسبب ملاقاة البدن أولًا ...","en":"The term “hot” may also be applied to what produces heat, whether by first coming into contact with the body ...","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-042.01","page":42,"ar":"... كالسماويات.","en":"... as [in heavenly influences].","status":"STAGE59_1912_CLAUSE_RECHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-042.02","page":42,"ar":"وأما الغريزية التي بها قوام الحياة فقيل نارية وقيل سماوية وقيل مخالفة لها.","en":"As for the innate heat by which life is sustained, some call it fiery, others heavenly, and others distinct from both.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-042.03","page":42,"ar":"ومنها الاعتماد يعني المدافعة المحسوسة.","en":"Another such quality is iʿtimād, meaning a perceptible pushing against or resistance (mudāfaʿa).","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-042.04","page":42,"ar":"وقد يجعل أنواعه ستة بحسب العرف.","en":"Its kinds are sometimes made six by customary classification.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-042.05","page":42,"ar":"والطبيعي منها ما يكون إلى فوق وهي الخفة أو إلى تحت وهو الثقل، وهما متضادان.","en":"The natural [impetus] is either upward, namely lightness, or downward, namely heaviness; these two are contrary.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-042.06","page":42,"ar":"والفلاسفة يسمونه الميل ويجعلونه قسريًا وطبيعيًا وإراديًا.","en":"The philosophers call it inclination (mayl) and distinguish forced, natural, and voluntary kinds.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-042.07","page":42,"ar":"لأن مبدأه إما من خارج فقسري، وإلا فإن كان من شعور فإرادي، وإلا فطبيعي. قيل: ميل النبات إلى التبرز والتزيد طبيعي.","en":"Its principle either comes from outside, in which case it is forced; or, if it proceeds from awareness, it is voluntary; otherwise natural. Thus the plant’s inclination toward protrusion and increase is said to be natural.","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-042.08","page":42,"ar":"وأصول المبصرات الألوان والأضواء، ولكل منهما أنواع.","en":"The fundamental visible qualities are colors and lights; each has several kinds.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-042.09","page":42,"ar":"إلا أن لكل من أنواع اللون اسما خاصا","en":"But every variety of colour has a distinctive name. [The comparison with light continues on the next page.]","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-043.01","page":43,"ar":"... بخلاف الضوء، وتخيل البياض من مخالطة الضوء الأجسام الشفافة كما في الثلج وزبد الماء ومسحوق الزجاج.","en":"... unlike light. Some conceive whiteness as the mixing of light with transparent bodies, as in snow, foam, and powdered glass.","status":"STAGE59_SEMANTIC_UNRESOLVED_AFTER_ARABIC_VISUAL_CHECK"},{"id":"KAL-043.02","page":43,"ar":"لا يمنع كونه حقيقة تحصل بأسباب.","en":"This does not prevent [whiteness] from being a genuine quality arising through causes.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-043.03","page":43,"ar":"والضوء إن كان لذات المحل فذاتي كالشمس ويسمى ضياء، والعارضي إن كان من مقابلة المضيء لذاته فأول وإلا فثان أو ثالث.","en":"Light, if it belongs intrinsically to its subject, is essential light, as with the sun, and is called radiance (ḍiyāʾ). Accidental light arising from facing an intrinsically luminous source is first-order; otherwise it is second- or third-order.","status":"STAGE56_VISUAL_CORRECTED_1912_PRINT"},{"id":"KAL-043.04","page":43,"ar":"والظلمة عدم ملكة له، وحصوليتها لا توجب كونها كيفية موجودة، كيف ولو كان لكان حائلًا للجالس في الغار من إبصار الخارج، كالعكس لعدم الفارق.","en":"Darkness is the privation of light. Its positive apprehensibility does not entail that darkness is an existing quality. How could it? Were it such a quality, it would obstruct a person sitting in a cave from seeing outside, just as in the reverse direction, since there is no relevant difference.","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-043.05","page":43,"ar":"والذاتي من المتفرق كالشمس يسمى شعاعًا، والعرضي كالمرآة بريقًا.","en":"Light spreading from an intrinsically luminous body, such as the sun, is called a ray; reflected illumination, as from a mirror, is brilliance.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-043.06","page":43,"ar":"وقد يتوهم أن الضوء أجسام صغار تنفصل من المضيء وتتصل بالمستضيء.","en":"It has been imagined that light is composed of small bodies separating from the luminous object and reaching what is illuminated.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-043.07","page":43,"ar":"بناء على أن حدوثه من مضيء عال أو متحرك أو متوسط بينه وبين المستضيء يوهم حركته انحدارا وارتفاعا وانعكاسا.","en":"The reason given is that light arising from a high luminous source, from a moving source, or from something between source and illuminated object gives the impression that light moves downwards, upwards, or by reflection.","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-043.08","page":43,"ar":"وعدم رؤية اللون في الظلمة قيل لكون الضوء شرطًا لوجوده، والحق أنه شرط لرؤيته.","en":"Some say that color is unseen in darkness because light is a condition for the color’s existence; the correct position is that it is a condition for *seeing* the color.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-043.09","page":43,"ar":"وأما المسموعات ...","en":"As for audible things ...","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-044.01","page":44,"ar":"... فالأصوات. وسببه القريب تموّج الهواء المعلول للقرع أو القلع.","en":"... they are sounds. Their proximate cause is the wave-like movement of air resulting from impact or separation.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-044.02","page":44,"ar":"ودليل على وجوده خارج الصماخ وعلى تعلق الإحساس به هناك إدراك جهته ولو من جانب المخالف، والتمييز بين قريبه وبعيده.","en":"Evidence that sound exists outside the ear canal, and that our sensation is directed to it there, is our perception of its direction, including when it comes from the opposite side, and our ability to distinguish a near sound from a distant one.","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-044.03","page":44,"ar":"وعلى كون إدراكه بوصول الهواء أنه يميل مع الرياح وأنه ينفرد بسماعه من ينفرد بذلك.","en":"The view that sound is heard through arriving air is supported by the way it bends with winds and how its hearability can depend upon that medium.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-044.04","page":44,"ar":"وإذا رجع بمصادمة جسم أملس فهو الصدى.","en":"When [a sound] returns after striking a smooth body, it is an echo (ṣadā).","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-044.05","page":44,"ar":"وإذا عرض له كيفية بها يمتاز عما يماثله في الحدة والثقل تميزا في المسموع فهو الحرف.","en":"When [a sound] acquires a quality by which it is audibly distinguished from another resembling it in highness or lowness of pitch, it is a letter (ḥarf).","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-044.06","page":44,"ar":"وينقسم إلى مصوّت مقصور هي الحركات أو ممدود هي المدات، وصامت، والصامت مع المقصور يسمى مقطعًا مقصورًا ومع الممدود ممدودًا.","en":"A letter divides into a vowel-like sound, either short (the vowel movements) or prolonged (the long vowels), and a consonant. A consonant joined to a short vowel makes a short syllabic segment, or to a prolonged vowel a long segment.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-044.07","page":44,"ar":"مثل (ل) و(لا).","en":"As in the short and long utterances exemplified by the written sequences “la” and “lā”.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-044.08","page":44,"ar":"والمؤلف منها يسمى باسم الكلام واللفظ.","en":"A composite of these sounds is called speech (kalām) or utterance (lafẓ).","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-044.09","page":44,"ar":"وقد يخص الكلام بما يفيد، واللفظ بما يتألف من المقاطع.","en":"Speech is sometimes reserved for meaningful utterance, and “wording” for what is compounded of articulatory segments.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-044.10","page":44,"ar":"وقد يتوهم أن اللفظ من مقولة الكم إذ قد يقدر جميعه بجزء منه، ورد بأنه بالعرض.","en":"One might suppose that utterance belongs to the category of quantity, since its whole can be measured by one of its parts. The reply is that this applies only incidentally (bi-l-ʿaraḍ).","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-044.11","page":44,"ar":"وأصول المذوقات الطعوم التسعة، والمشمومات الروائح، والثاني الكيفيات ...","en":"The fundamental objects of taste are the nine tastes, and of smell the odors. The second [division of quality] consists of the qualities ...","status":"STAGE59_1912_CLAUSE_RECHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-045.01","page":45,"ar":"النفسانيّة، وتسمى مع الرسوخ ملكة، وبدونه حالًا.","en":"[These qualities are] psychic, called a settled disposition (malaka) when firmly rooted and a passing state (ḥāl) when not.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-045.02","page":45,"ar":"فمنها الحياة، وهي مبدأ لقوة الحس والحركة.","en":"One such quality is life, the principle of the power of sensation and motion.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-045.03","page":45,"ar":"ولا تشترط باعتدال المزاج ووجود البنية والروح، وإن كان قد تنتفي بفقدها.","en":"Life does not require a balanced temperament, bodily structure, or spirit as conditions, although it may cease when they are absent.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-045.04","page":45,"ar":"والموت زوالها، وقيل كيفية تضادها.","en":"Death is its cessation; another view makes death a positive quality contrary to life.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-045.05","page":45,"ar":"وقد يطلق على عدمها كما في الجماد.","en":"Death is sometimes applied simply to the absence of life, as in an inanimate thing.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-045.06","page":45,"ar":"ومنها الإدراك، وهو تميز وحضور وظهور الشيء عند العقل بحقيقته كالنفس وصفاتها.","en":"Among them is apprehension: the distinguishing, presence, and manifestation of a thing to the intellect by its very reality, as with the soul and its attributes.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-045.07","page":45,"ar":"أو بصورته المنتزعة كما في الماديات، أو الحاصلة ابتداء كما في المجردات والمعدومات.","en":"Or apprehension may occur through its abstracted representation, as with material things, or through a representation acquired without such abstraction, as in immaterial things and nonexistents.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-045.08","page":45,"ar":"وهي مع كونها مغايرة للهوية التي بها الاتصاف ليس حصولها في الذهن كحصول العرض في المحل.","en":"Although these representations differ from the identity through which a subject is intrinsically qualified, their occurrence in the intellect is not the inherence of an accident in a subject.","status":"STAGE56_VISUAL_CORRECTED_1912_PRINT"},{"id":"KAL-045.09","page":45,"ar":"فلا يجب اتصاف المدرك بالمدرك، فالكريم يتصور البخيل ولا يتصف به.","en":"Consequently the apprehender need not acquire the property apprehended: the generous man may conceive the miser without becoming miserly.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-045.10","page":45,"ar":"ويتصف بالكرم ولا يتصوره.","en":"Conversely, he may actually be generous without at that moment conceiving generosity.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-045.11","page":45,"ar":"ومن أنكر الوجود العقلي جعل الإدراك مجرد إضافة أو صفة ذات إضافة.","en":"Those who deny intellectual existence construe cognition as a bare relation or a quality bearing a relation.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-045.12","page":45,"ar":"فأشكل عليه العلم بالمعدومات، فلزم القول بالصورة في المعدوم، بل في الكل.","en":"They then have difficulty explaining knowledge of nonexistent things and must concede a representation in the case of nonexistents, indeed in all cases.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-045.13","page":45,"ar":"ومعناها أن للمعدوم وجودًا غير متأصل وهي من حيث قيامها بالذهن علم، ومن حيث ذاتها معلوم، بخلاف الموجود ...","en":"This means that the nonexistent has a non-fundamental kind of existence; the [cognitive form], insofar as it subsists in the mind, is knowledge, while insofar as considered in its own identity it is the known—unlike the existent [as continued on p. 46].","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-046.01","page":46,"ar":"فإن العلم ما في الذهن، والمعلوم ما في الخارج.","en":"For the act or content of knowledge is what lies in the mind, while what is known is what is external.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-046.02","page":46,"ar":"وأنواع الإدراك إحساس وتخيّل وتوهّم وتعقّل.","en":"The kinds of apprehension are sensation, imagination, estimation, and intellection.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-046.03","page":46,"ar":"وقد يقال العلم لمطلق الإدراك، وللثلاثة الأخيرة، وللأخير.","en":"The word knowledge may be applied to apprehension generally, to the latter three kinds, or to the last of them alone.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-046.04","page":46,"ar":"وللتصديق الجازم المطابق الثابت.","en":"It may also be reserved for firm, reality-conforming, stable assent.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-046.05","page":46,"ar":"فيسمى الخالي عن الجزم ظنا، وعن المطابقة جهلا مركبا، وعن الثبات اعتقادا.","en":"Assent lacking firmness is called opinion (ẓann); lacking correspondence, compound ignorance; and lacking stability, belief or conviction (iʿtiqād).","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-046.06","page":46,"ar":"وأما الشك والوهم فتصور.","en":"Doubt and estimation [in the restricted sense] are counted under conception rather than certain assent.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-046.07","page":46,"ar":"والذهول عن الصورة الإدراكية إن انتهى إلى زوالها فنسيان، وإلا فسهو.","en":"When a cognitive form drops from attention, its complete loss is forgetting; if the form remains without being recalled, that is inadvertence.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-046.08","page":46,"ar":"والجهل البسيط عدم ملكة للعلم، والمركب مضاد له، وقيل مماثل له.","en":"Simple ignorance is privation of knowledge; compound ignorance is contrary to it, although some call it a quality of the same general kind.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-046.09","page":46,"ar":"إذ لا اختلاف الأعراض بالطباق.","en":"For [on this account] accidents do not differ by [mere] correspondence (ṭibāq).","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-046.10","page":46,"ar":"والعلم الحادث قد يكون بالقوة، وهو الاستعداد، وقد يكون بالفعل.","en":"Created knowledge can be potential, namely preparedness to know, or actual.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-046.11","page":46,"ar":"إما إجمالًا بأن يلاحظ أمر بسيط وهو مبدأ للتفاصيل، أو تفصيلًا بأن يلاحظ التفاصيل.","en":"Actual knowledge is either summary—by grasping a simple consideration which serves as the source of detailed cognitions—or detailed, by considering those particulars explicitly.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-046.12","page":46,"ar":"ويجوز انقلاب النظر ضروريًّا، وفي عكسه خلاف.","en":"Acquired knowledge may become immediate; whether an originally immediate cognition may become acquired is disputed.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-046.13","page":46,"ar":"كما في تعدد العلم بتعدد المعلوم، ومحله القلب.","en":"There is likewise a disagreement about the multiplication of knowledge with the multiplication of its objects; its seat is the heart.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-046.14","page":46,"ar":"ولا كلام في توسط الآلات في الجزئيات.","en":"There is no dispute here that instruments may mediate cognition of particulars.","status":"STAGE57_PRINT_READING_VISUALLY_CHECKED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-047.01","page":47,"ar":"ومناط التكليف القوة الحاصلة عند العلم ببعض المعلومات الضرورية.","en":"The condition of moral accountability is the faculty obtained through cognition of certain immediate truths.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-047.02","page":47,"ar":"بحيث يتمكن بها من اكتساب النظريات، وهي القوة المميزة بين الأمور الحسنة والقبيحة.","en":"It enables one to acquire demonstrative knowledge and to distinguish good from bad matters.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-047.03","page":47,"ar":"ومنها الإرادة، وهي كسائر الوجدانيات يسهل معرفتها ويعسر تعريفها.","en":"Among the psychic qualities is will: like other immediately experienced states, it is easy to recognize but difficult to define.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-047.04","page":47,"ar":"وتفارق الشهوة في الوجود وشدته وتعلقها بالقوة الإدراكية، كالشهوة بالطبيعة.","en":"Will differs from appetite in its occurrence and its intensity, and in that will is attached to the apprehensive faculty whereas appetite is attached to nature.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-047.05","page":47,"ar":"قيل هي اعتقاد النفع، أو ميل يعقب ذلك، أو العلم بما هو عند العالم كمال وخير.","en":"One view identifies will with belief in benefit, another with the inclination following such belief, and another with knowledge of what the knowing subject regards as perfection and good.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-047.06","page":47,"ar":"والتفسير بصفة بها يرجح الفاعل أحد مقدوريه من الفعل والترك لا يكشف عن حقيقتها.","en":"Defining it as a quality through which an agent selects one of two possible acts—doing and not doing—does not disclose its essence.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-047.07","page":47,"ar":"وزعم الأشعري أن إرادة الشيء نفس الكراهة.","en":"Al-Ashʿarī is reported to maintain that willing one thing is identical with aversion [to its contrary].","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-047.08","page":47,"ar":"ومنها القدرة، وهي صفة تؤثر وفق الإرادة، أو مبدأ الأفعال المختلفة.","en":"Power (qudra) is a quality producing an effect in accordance with will, or the principle of acts of different kinds.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-047.09","page":47,"ar":"والقوة ...","en":"The discussion now turns to the more inclusive concept of power (quwwa) ...","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-048.01","page":48,"ar":"أعم، إذ هي مبدأ للتغيير في آخر من حيث هو آخر، إما مع القصد أو بدونه.","en":"Power (quwwa) is broader: it is a principle of producing change in something else insofar as it is other, whether intentionally or without intention.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-048.02","page":48,"ar":"وكل إما مختلفة الآثار أو لا.","en":"Within each of the intentional and non-intentional divisions, the effects are either diverse or not diverse; this yields four combinations.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-048.03","page":48,"ar":"فالأولى القوة الحيوانية، والثانية الفلكية، والثالثة النباتية، والرابعة العنصرية.","en":"These four cases, in order, are: animal power (intentional, with diverse effects); celestial power (intentional, with effects of one kind); vegetative power (without intention, with diverse effects); and elemental power (without intention, with effects of one kind).","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-048.04","page":48,"ar":"ثم القدرة الحادثة مع الفعل لا قبله لامتناع بقاء الأعراض.","en":"According to the doctrine under discussion, created capacity accompanies the act, rather than preceding it, because accidents cannot endure.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-048.05","page":48,"ar":"ورد بأنها تستمر بتجدد الأمثال كالعلم وغيره مما هو قبل الفعل.","en":"The response is that [a created power] can persist through the successive renewal of like instances, as knowledge and other qualities that precede the act do.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-048.06","page":48,"ar":"قالوا لو لم تكن القدرة إلا حال الفعل لزم إيجاد الموجود وامتناع التكليف.","en":"They argue that if capacity existed only during an act, one would have to produce something already existing and moral obligation would become impossible.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-048.07","page":48,"ar":"ورد بما سبق، وبأنه يكفي في التكليف كون الفعل مما يتعلق به القدرة في الجملة.","en":"The reply invokes the earlier distinction and holds that moral obligation is sufficiently possible if an act is generally within the scope of capacity.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-048.08","page":48,"ar":"كإيمان الكافر بخلاف خلق الجسم، فعلى الأول الممنوع لا يكون قادرًا كالزَّمِن.","en":"An unbeliever’s act of believing is an example, unlike bringing a body into being. On the first account, someone prevented from acting is not considered able, as in the case of a paralysed person.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-048.09","page":48,"ar":"وكذا القدرة الواحدة لا تتعلق بمقدورين.","en":"Likewise, it is maintained that one particular capacity does not attach to two distinct possible acts.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-048.10","page":48,"ar":"والحق أن القوة التي هي مبدأ الأفعال المختلفة تأثيرًا أو تسببًا عاديًّا.","en":"A more precise view distinguishes a general faculty capable of diverse acts, whether through efficacy or through customary occasioning.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-048.11","page":48,"ar":"توجد مع الفعل وقبله وبعده.","en":"Such a faculty can persist with the act, before it and after it.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-048.12","page":48,"ar":"ومع جميع شرائط التأثير لا تكون إلا معه، والعجز قيل هو ضد القدرة.","en":"But the complete conjunction of all conditions of efficacy occurs only with the act itself. Incapacity is said to be contrary to capacity.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-048.13","page":48,"ar":"فلا يتعلق إلا بالموجود، وقيل عدم ملكة، للقطع بأن عجز المتحدي","en":"On the view that inability is the contrary of power, inability relates only to what is existent. Another view calls it privation of a faculty, since the challenged person’s inability is certainly [the inability to produce its like, continued on p. 49].","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-049.01","page":49,"ar":"هو عن الإتيان بالمثل، وجعله مشتركا بين المعنيين خلاف اللغة.","en":"[The incapacity at issue] is an incapacity to produce the like of [what is challenged]; to make the word equivocal between the two meanings conflicts with linguistic usage.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-049.02","page":49,"ar":"والقدرة تضاد الخُلُق لما أن أفعاله بلا روية.","en":"Capacity is contrary to settled character (khuluq), since actions proceeding from character occur without deliberation.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-049.03","page":49,"ar":"وهل تضاد النوم فيه تردد.","en":"Whether sleep is contrary to power remains disputed.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-049.04","page":49,"ar":"ومنها اللذة والألم.","en":"Further psychic qualities include pleasure and pain.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-049.05","page":49,"ar":"وقد يفسران بإدراك الملائم والمنافر من حيث هما كذلك، إنما نوعان من الإدراك.","en":"They are sometimes explained as apprehending what is agreeable and disagreeable precisely as such; on this account they are kinds of apprehension.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-049.06","page":49,"ar":"على احتمال أن يراد الإصابة والوجدان.","en":"This holds if the intention is the actual feeling or encounter [of the appropriate object].","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-049.07","page":49,"ar":"وبعضهم على أن اللذة خروج عن الحالة غير الطبيعية.","en":"Others maintain that pleasure consists in departure from a state contrary to nature.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-049.08","page":49,"ar":"وكل إما حسي أو عقلي، وهو أقوى.","en":"Each of pleasure and pain can be sensory or intellectual; the intellectual kind is stronger.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-049.09","page":49,"ar":"والحسي من الاستيلام باللمس يسمى وجعا.","en":"Sensible suffering associated with the sense of touch is called ache or bodily pain (wajaʿ).","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-049.10","page":49,"ar":"ومنها الصحة والمرض، فالصحة ملكة أو حالة يصدر عنها الأفعال من الموضوع لها سليمة.","en":"Also health and disease: health is a stable condition or passing state from which a subject’s actions arise in sound form.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-049.11","page":49,"ar":"والمرض ملكة أو حالة مضادة لها، وقيل عدم ملكة لها.","en":"Disease is a contrary condition, whether stable or passing; some consider it privation of the sound faculty.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-049.12","page":49,"ar":"وقد يتسامح بجعلهما من المحسوسات.","en":"By a loose extension of usage, both health and disease may be included among sensible qualities.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-049.13","page":49,"ar":"ثم إذا اعتبر فيهما سلامة جميع الأفعال وآفة الجميع كانت بينهما واسطة كالأطفال والمشايخ، وإلا فلا.","en":"If, in defining health and disease respectively, one requires the soundness of all functions and the impairment of all functions, an intermediate state between them must be acknowledged, as in children and the elderly. Otherwise there is no such intermediate state.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-049.14","page":49,"ar":"الثالث: الكيفيات المختصة بالكميات كالاستقامة والانحناء","en":"The third class is qualities particular to quantities, such as straightness and curvature—[of a line; continued on p. 50].","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-050.01","page":50,"ar":"للخط، والتقعير والتقبيب للسطح، وكالزوجية والفردية للعدد.","en":"[Straightness and curvature belong] to a line; concavity and convexity to a surface; and evenness and oddness to number.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-050.02","page":50,"ar":"وكالخلقة، أعني مجموع الشكل واللون الذي بحسبه يوصف الشيء بالحسن والقبح.","en":"Another instance is outward configuration (khilqa), meaning the combined shape and colour in virtue of which a thing is described as beautiful or ugly.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-050.03","page":50,"ar":"وكالزاوية، وهي هيئة إحاطة الخطين بالسطح عند الملتقى.","en":"Another is angle: the configuration in which two lines enclose a surface at their meeting.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-050.04","page":50,"ar":"وما قيل إنها سطح أحاط به خطان يلتقيان عند نقطة ففيه تسامح.","en":"The claim that an angle is a surface enclosed by two lines which meet at a point uses the term loosely.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-050.05","page":50,"ar":"الرابع الكيفيات الاستعدادية، وهي استعداد شديد على أن ينفعل ويسمى ضعفًا كالممراضية، أو لا ينفعل ويسمى قوةً كالمصحاحية.","en":"The fourth class comprises dispositional qualities: an intense readiness to be affected, called weakness, as in a susceptibility to disease; or a resistance to being affected, called strength, as in a disposition to health.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-050.06","page":50,"ar":"فصل في الأين، وهو الكون في الحيز.","en":"Chapter on where: it is a thing’s occupancy of a spatial region.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-050.07","page":50,"ar":"فإن اعتبر حصول جوهر باعتبار جوهر فإما أن يمكن تخلل ثالث بينهما فافتراق وإلا فاجتماع.","en":"If the occupancy of one substance is considered in relation to another, then, if a third can be interposed, the two are separated; otherwise they are conjoined.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-050.08","page":50,"ar":"وإن لم يعتبر فإن كان مسبوقًا بحصوله في ذلك الحيز فسكون، أو في آخر فحركة.","en":"Without that comparative consideration, if occupancy was preceded by occupancy of the same region, it is rest; if by occupancy of a different region, it is motion.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-050.09","page":50,"ar":"فالحصول في آن الحدوث خارج، وقيل بل سكون.","en":"Thus the occupancy occurring at the instant of origination falls outside both [motion and rest]; another opinion counts it as rest.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-051.01","page":51,"ar":"والحق أن حقيقة الكون في الكل واحدة، وإنما التغاير بالحيثيات.","en":"The correct position is that the real nature of occupancy is one in all the cases, and their difference arises only through the respects under which it is considered.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-051.02","page":51,"ar":"حتى أن الواحد بالشخص ربما يكون افتراقًا واجتماعًا وحركةً وسكونًا باعتبارات مختلفة.","en":"So one and the same individual state may count as separation, conjunction, motion and rest under different considerations.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-051.03","page":51,"ar":"والقول بتضاد الأكوان معناه امتناع الاجتماع عند تحققها في الوجود.","en":"To say that these occupancies are contrary is to say that they cannot coexist when their relevant conditions are actual.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-051.04","page":51,"ar":"والحركة قد يراد بها ما هو المتحقق منها وهو الحصول بعد الحصول في حيز آخر.","en":"“Motion” may refer to what is actually realised: one occupancy following another in a different region.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-051.05","page":51,"ar":"ويراد بها ما هو الموهوم وهو الحصولات المتعاقبة على الاستمرار دون الاستقرار.","en":"Or it may refer to what is imagined: a continuous series of successive occupancies without stable remaining.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-051.06","page":51,"ar":"والسكون إن لم يشترط باللبث فالحركة سكون أو سكنات.","en":"If dwelling or remaining is not imposed as a condition of rest, then motion itself would be rest—or a plurality of rests.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-051.07","page":51,"ar":"وهل هو الحصول الثاني أو مجموع الحصولين فيه تردد.","en":"There is hesitation over whether rest is the second occupancy alone or the two occupancies together.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-051.08","page":51,"ar":"والحق أن الباطن من أجزاء المتحرك متحرك.","en":"The correct position is that the inner parts of a moving body are also moving.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-051.09","page":51,"ar":"والواقف عند هبوب الرياح وعند جريان الماء عليه ساكن.","en":"A person standing while the wind blows or water flows over him remains at rest.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-051.10","page":51,"ar":"ومبنى التردد على التردد في حقيقة الحيز.","en":"The uncertainty depends on a corresponding uncertainty concerning the nature of spatial region.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-051.11","page":51,"ar":"وقول الفلاسفة الحركة ...","en":"The philosophers’ account of motion is introduced here and continues onto the following page.","status":"STAGE59_1912_PRINT_PAGE_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-052.01","page":52,"ar":"خروج من القوة إلى الفعل تدريجًا أو يسيرًا يسيرًا أو لا دفعة، مبنيّ على بداهة تصور هذه المعاني.","en":"[They say that motion is] coming out of potentiality into actuality gradually, little by little, rather than all at once; this is grounded in the supposed self-evidence of these notions.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-052.02","page":52,"ar":"والموجود منها كون الجسم متوسطًا بين المبدأ والمنتهى على الاستمرار.","en":"What exists of motion is the body’s continuously being intermediate between its starting point and its end.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-052.03","page":52,"ar":"وأما كليته المعقولة المتصلة الممتدة فوهمية.","en":"The intellectually conceived connected and extended entirety of motion, on the other hand, is an imaginary construction.","status":"STAGE59_1912_CLAUSE_RECHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-052.04","page":52,"ar":"ولا بد لها من ما منه وإليه وفيه وهو وله وزمان.","en":"Motion also requires six conditions or considerations: that from which it proceeds, that to which it proceeds, that in which it occurs, what it is [the print has «وهو»], that to which it belongs, and time. [The technical fourth item remains for independent witness collation.]","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-052.05","page":52,"ar":"فالحركة في الأين ظاهرة، وفي الوضع كحركة الفلك.","en":"Motion in the category of place is obvious; motion in position is exemplified by the revolution of the celestial sphere.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-052.06","page":52,"ar":"وفي الكم كالنمو والذبول والتخلخل والتكاثف.","en":"Motion in quantity includes growth, wasting, rarefaction and condensation.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-053.01","page":53,"ar":"وفي الكيف كسود العنب وتسخن الماء.","en":"Motion in quality is illustrated by grapes becoming black and water becoming hot.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-053.02","page":53,"ar":"مع الجزم بعدم الكون فيه أو الورود عليه.","en":"This is said while affirming that the quality was not already present in the subject and had not merely arrived upon it from without.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-053.03","page":53,"ar":"وتكون بالذات كحركة السفينة، وبالعرض كحركة راكبها.","en":"Motion may belong primarily to a thing, as the motion of a ship does, or accidentally, as the motion of its passenger does.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-053.04","page":53,"ar":"والمحرك إن كان خارجًا حركته قسرية، وإلا فمع القصد والشعور إرادية وبدونهما طبيعية.","en":"If the moving cause is external, motion is forced. If internal, it is voluntary when accompanied by intention and awareness, and otherwise natural.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-053.05","page":53,"ar":"فيدخل فيها حركة النمو والنبض وحركة النفس من حيث الاحتياج إلى مطلقها.","en":"This includes growth, pulsation, and breathing insofar as the occurrence of those activities in general is necessary.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-053.06","page":53,"ar":"وأما من حيث إمكان تغير جزئياتها عن أوقاتها فإرادية.","en":"But insofar as their particular occurrences can be varied in their timing, they are voluntary.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-053.07","page":53,"ar":"وما قيل إن الطبيعية لا تكون إلا هابطة أو صاعدة إنما هو في البسائط العنصرية.","en":"The assertion that natural motion must always be descending or ascending applies only to elemental simple bodies.","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-053.08","page":53,"ar":"ووحدتها النوعية بوحدة ما فيه وما منه وما إليه، والشخصية بوحدة ما سوى المحرك، والجنسية بوحدة ما فيه.","en":"Motion has specific unity through the unity of what it takes place in, what it proceeds from, and what it proceeds to; numerical unity through the unity of everything other than the mover; and generic unity through what it takes place in.","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-053.09","page":53,"ar":"وتضادها بتضاد ما منه وما إليه، كالسود والبيض، وكالصعود والهبوط.","en":"Motions are contrary when their points of origin and their termini are contrary—for example blackening and whitening, or ascent and descent.","status":"STAGE60_LEXICAL_UNRESOLVED"},{"id":"KAL-053.10","page":53,"ar":"وانقسامها بانقسام الزمان وما فيه وما له.","en":"Motion is divisible according to the divisions of time, the category in which motion occurs, and that to which motion belongs [«ما له»].","status":"VISUAL_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-053.11","page":53,"ar":"ومن لوازم الحركة كيفية متفاوتة ...","en":"Among the concomitants of motion is a quality susceptible to degrees ...","status":"STAGE59_1912_CLAUSE_RECHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-054.01","page":54,"ar":"تسمى باعتبار الشدة سرعة والضعف بطأ.","en":"That quality is termed speed when intense and slowness when weak.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-054.02","page":54,"ar":"وليس هو تخلل السكنات لامتناع عدم الحركة مع خلوص المقتضي لها وعدم رفع المانع.","en":"Slowness is not the interposition of moments of rest: motion cannot simply be absent when its complete determinant is present and the impediment has been removed.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-054.03","page":54,"ar":"ولزوم الانفكاك في مثل حركة طوق في الرحى، وزيادة سكنات الطائر على حركاته ما لا يحصى.","en":"That account would also imply disjunction in examples such as the motion of a ring in a mill, and an inconceivably greater number of moments of rest than movement for a flying bird.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-054.04","page":54,"ar":"وأجيب بأن الحركة بمحض خلق الله، وأن الانفكاك ثم الالتئام جائز.","en":"The reply is that motion is due solely to God’s creation, and that separation followed by reunion is possible.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-054.05","page":54,"ar":"وأن الحركات لكونها وجودية متجددة متميزة عن السكنات وإن كانت أضعاف الآلاف.","en":"Because motions are renewed positive occurrences, they differ from rests, even if they are many thousands of times more numerous.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-054.06","page":54,"ar":"قالوا لا بد بين كل حركتين من سكون، لأن آن الوصول غير آن الرجوع، فلولا زمان السكون بينهما لزم تتالي الآنين المستلزم لوجود الجزء.","en":"They say that rest must intervene between any two motions, for the instant of arrival differs from the instant of return. Without an interval of rest between them, two instants would follow immediately upon one another, entailing an indivisible [temporal] part.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-054.07","page":54,"ar":"وأجيب بأنه لا آن بدون الانقطاع، وعورض بأنه لو لزم لكان بلا سبب ولا في زمان معين.","en":"It is answered that there is no such instant without a discontinuity; and objected that if it occurred it would lack a determinate cause or time.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-054.08","page":54,"ar":"ولوقف الجبل الهابط بملاقاة خردلة صاعدة، وأجيب بأن السبب عدم الحركة.","en":"[The opposing argument says] a descending mountain would have to halt on meeting an ascending mustard seed. The reply invokes the absence of motion as the cause.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-054.09","page":54,"ar":"وبأنه يقع في زمان لا ينقسم فعلًا، وبأن الخردلة ترجع بمصادمة هواء الجبل.","en":"It is further answered that the event occurs in a duration that is not actually divisible, and that the mustard seed is turned back by striking the air displaced by the mountain.","status":"STAGE60_PRINT_VERIFIED_SOURCE_AND_ENGLISH"},{"id":"KAL-055.01","page":55,"ar":"فصل: إذا تحرك الجسم إلى جهتين متقابلتين فبعده عن المبدأ بقدر الفضل، وإلا فسكن.","en":"Chapter. If a body moves in two opposite directions, its distance from its starting point corresponds to the excess [of motion in one direction over the other]; otherwise it is at rest.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-055.02","page":55,"ar":"والسكون في الآن بقاء النسب، وفي غيره بقاء النوع.","en":"Rest, considered at an instant, is the persistence of the relevant relations; considered otherwise, it is the persistence of the same kind.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-055.03","page":55,"ar":"فهو يضاد الحركة، وقيل عدم الحركة فعدم ملكة.","en":"It is therefore opposed to motion; alternatively, it is said to be the absence of motion, and is accordingly a privation.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-055.04","page":55,"ar":"ويكون طبيعيا وقسريا وإراديا.","en":"Rest may be natural, forced, or voluntary.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-055.05","page":55,"ar":"ويتضاد بتضاد ما فيه، كالسكون في المكان الأعلى والأسفل.","en":"Different states of rest are contrary when the places in which they occur are contrary, as with rest in an upper and a lower location.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-055.06","page":55,"ar":"فصل: الإضافة هي النسبة المنعكسة، وتسمى مضافا حقيقيا.","en":"Chapter. Relation (iḍāfa) is a reciprocal reference (nisba munʿakisa), which is called a relative in the strict sense.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-055.07","page":55,"ar":"والمركب منه ومن المعروض مشهورا.","en":"The complex composed of the relation and its subject is called a relative in the customary sense.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-055.08","page":55,"ar":"والنسبتان قد تتوافقان وقد تتخالفان.","en":"The two correlated relations may agree in their descriptions or differ.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-055.09","page":55,"ar":"والانعكاس قد يستغنى عن حرف، وقد يفتقر عروضها إلى رابطة.","en":"Reciprocity can dispense with an overt relational particle, while the attribution of a relation can require a connecting expression.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-055.10","page":55,"ar":"وقد يكون لصفة في الطرفين","en":"Its ground can be a quality in both correlates—[continued on the next page].","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-056.01","page":56,"ar":"أو في أحدهما، وتعرض لكل موجود، وتتكافأ الطرفان في التحصيل والإطلاق والوجود والعدم ذهنا وخارجا قوة وفعلا.","en":"—or in only one of them. Relation is predicable of every existent; its two terms are on a par as regards realization, application, existence and nonexistence, in mind and outside it, potentially and actually.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-056.02","page":56,"ar":"والجمهور على أنه أمر اعتباري، وإلا لتسلسل؛ لأن الحلول إضافة لها حلول.","en":"Most regard relation as something established by consideration; otherwise there would be a regress, since inherence itself is a relation, and that relation would itself have inherence.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-056.03","page":56,"ar":"ولزم لا تناهي أوصاف كل عدم بحسب ما له من الإضافة إلى ما عداه.","en":"It would follow that every nonexistent [item] has indefinitely many attributes through the relations it bears to everything besides itself.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-056.04","page":56,"ar":"ويجاب بأن سلب الكل لا يقتضي السلب الكلي.","en":"It may be replied that negating the members individually does not entail negation of the universal considered as such.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-056.05","page":56,"ar":"والتمسك في وجودها بأننا نقطع بفوقية السماء وتحتية الأرض وأبوة زيد وبنوة عمرو وإن لم يوجد اعتبار العقل ضعيف.","en":"The argument for their real existence based on our certainty that heaven is above and earth below, and that Zayd is a father and ʿAmr a son, even if the intellect did not consider these relations, is weak.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-056.06","page":56,"ar":"ثم إنها في جنسيتها ونوعيتها وتشخصيتها وتضادها تابعة للمعروضات.","en":"As to their genera, species, individuation, and contrariety, relations follow the subjects in which they are considered.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-056.07","page":56,"ar":"والمتى هي النسبة إلى الزمان أو الآن.","en":"The category of “when” (matā) is the relation to time or to an instant.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-056.08","page":56,"ar":"والوضع هو كون الجسم بحيث يكون لأجزائه نسبة فيما بينها أو إلى الأمور الخارجة عنها.","en":"Position (waḍʿ) is the condition of a body in which its parts stand in a relation among themselves or to things external to them.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-056.09","page":56,"ar":"والملك هو نسبة الجسم إلى حاصر له أو لبعضه وينتقل بانتقاله.","en":"Possession (milk) is the relation of a body to something enclosing it, or part of it, which moves when the body moves.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-056.10","page":56,"ar":"وأن يفعل هو تأثير شيء في شيء ما دام سالكا.","en":"“Acting upon” is one thing’s exercising an effect upon another for as long as the process continues.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-056.11","page":56,"ar":"وأن ينفعل هو التأثر عن الغير كذلك.","en":"“Being acted upon” is undergoing another’s influence in the same way.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-056.12","page":56,"ar":"وأما الحاصل بعد الاستقرار فيكون كيفا أو وضعا أو غير ذلك.","en":"What remains once the process is settled, however, is a quality, a position, or something else [rather than action or passion].","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-056.13","page":56,"ar":"الباب الرابع في الجواهر.","en":"Chapter Four: On Substances.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-056.14","page":56,"ar":"الجوهر إن انقسم جسم، والآخر فرد. وقالوا: الجوهر","en":"A substance, if divisible, is a body; the other [indivisible kind] is an atom. The philosophers then say: substance—[their alternative division continues on p.57].","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-057.01","page":57,"ar":"إن كان قابلا للأبعاد جسم، وإلا فما جزء له بالفعل فصورة أو بالقوة فمادة، وإما خارج يتعلق به فنفس، وإلا فعقل.","en":"If [substance] is capable of dimensions, it is a body; if not, then what belongs to a body as an actual component is form, as a potential component is matter; what is outside it but connected with it is soul; otherwise it is intellect.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-057.02","page":57,"ar":"فصل: فالجسم عندنا الجوهر القابل للانقسام، فيتناول المؤلف من جزأين فصاعدا.","en":"Chapter. According to us, body is substance capable of division; this includes anything composed of two or more parts.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-057.03","page":57,"ar":"وعند المعتزلة ما له عرض وعمق وطول.","en":"According to the Muʿtazila, it is what has breadth, depth, and length.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-057.04","page":57,"ar":"فيخرج ما يكون تركيب أجزائه على سمت أو سمتين فقط، وما يكون عددها أقل من أدنى ما يتركب منه الجسم، أعني ثمانية أو ستة أو أربعة.","en":"Hence what is arranged only along one or two dimensions is excluded, as is any composition with fewer than the minimum particles needed for a body—reckoned as eight, six, or four.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-057.05","page":57,"ar":"وعند الفلاسفة هو الجوهر الذي يمكن أن تفرض فيه الأبعاد الثلاثة المتقاطعة على زوايا قوائم.","en":"According to the philosophers, body is substance in which three mutually intersecting dimensions can be supposed at right angles.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-057.06","page":57,"ar":"ولهم تردد في أن هذا حد أو رسم.","en":"They differ over whether that account is a strict definition or a descriptive characterization.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-057.07","page":57,"ar":"ثم انقسامات الجسم البسيط حاصلة بالفعل عندنا خلافا للفلاسفة.","en":"Furthermore, the divisions of simple body actually exist according to us, contrary to the philosophers.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-057.08","page":57,"ar":"وجمهورهم على أنه مركب من مادة بها الانقسام، وصورة عليها تدل الامتدادات الفرضية.","en":"Most of them hold that [body] is composed of matter, through which it admits division, and form, as indicated by its hypothesized extensions.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-057.09","page":57,"ar":"وبعضهم على أنه بسيط في نفسه كما هو عند الحس.","en":"Others hold that a body is simple in itself, as it appears to sense.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-057.10","page":57,"ar":"لنا أن القابل للقسمة لو كان واحدًا لكانت","en":"Our argument is that, if what admits division were a single thing, its unity would itself be divisible—[continued on p.58].","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-058.01","page":58,"ar":"الوحدة منقسمة والتفريق إعدامًا له.","en":"—its unity would itself be divisible, and severance would amount to its destruction.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-058.02","page":58,"ar":"ولما كان الجبل أعظم من الخردلة لكونهما غير متناهيي الأجزاء.","en":"And a mountain could not be greater than a mustard seed if both possessed infinitely many actual parts.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-058.03","page":58,"ar":"ولتناهي امتداد الجسم الحاصل، ولما وجد الزمان إذ لا يوجد منه غير الحاضر اللامنقسم المنطبق على الحركة المنطبقة على المسافة.","en":"Moreover, the extension of an actual body is finite; and time would [on the opposing account] fail to exist, for only its indivisible present exists, corresponding to motion and, through it, to the traversed distance.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-058.04","page":58,"ar":"وأيضًا النقطة طرف الخط، وبها تماس الكرة سطحًا مستويًا، وبها قيام الخط على الخط.","en":"Furthermore, a point is a line’s extremity; by a point a sphere touches a plane, and by a point one line stands upon another.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-058.05","page":58,"ar":"فوجودها غير منقسم.","en":"Its existence is thus [an instance of] something indivisible.","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-058.06","page":58,"ar":"ثم أن الأجزاء متناهية، وإلا لم تقع بين الطرفين ولم يصل المتحرك إلى الغاية ولا السريع إلى البطيء.","en":"The number of [actual] parts must be finite: otherwise they could not be located between two termini, and neither a moving body could reach its goal nor a faster one catch a slower.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-058.07","page":58,"ar":"وللتناهي وجوه: الأول ما منه إلى جهة غير ما منه إلى أخرى.","en":"There are several arguments for finitude. First, what extends from [a part] in one direction differs from what extends in another.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-058.08","page":58,"ar":"الثاني تلاقي الجزأين، إما بالأسر فلا حجم، وإلا انقسم.","en":"Second, consider the contact of two parts. If their contact is throughout their entirety, [their combination has] no magnitude; otherwise [one of them] is divisible.","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-058.09","page":58,"ar":"الثالث إذا فرض ثلاثة فالوسط إن منع","en":"Third, suppose three [parts]; if the middle one prevents [the contact of the two outer ones—continued].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-059.01","page":59,"ar":"الطرفين عن التلاقي انقسم، وإلا فلا حجم.","en":"—the two outer ones from meeting, it must be divisible; if it does not, there is no magnitude.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-059.02","page":59,"ar":"الرابع إذا وقع جزء على ملتقى جزأين انقسمت الثلاثة.","en":"Fourth, if a part falls upon the junction of two other parts, all three would be divided.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-059.03","page":59,"ar":"الخامس يلزم التفكيك في كل جسم قطع البعض منه جزءًا أو أكثر، كطوق حجر الرحى، وشعبي فرجار ذي ثلاث شعب، وعقب الإنسان مع سائر أطرافه حين يدور على نفسه.","en":"Fifth, disjunction would follow in every body in which some part traverses one part or more [relative to another], as in the hoop of a millstone, the two arms of a three-armed compass, and a person’s heel in relation to the other extremities when that person turns around.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-059.04","page":59,"ar":"والمفترض مستظهر من الجانبين.","en":"The supposition under discussion is supported from both sides [«مستظهر من الجانبين»; the precise technical force awaits another witness].","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-059.05","page":59,"ar":"قالوا إذا لم يكن اتصال الجسم باجتماع الأجزاء وانفصاله بافتراقها فله هوية امتدادية لا تنتفي بتبديل المقادير.","en":"They say: if bodily continuity is not merely particles joining, and bodily separation not merely their parting, then the body has an extended identity that does not disappear through change of magnitudes.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-059.06","page":59,"ar":"وهو الجوهر الذي شأنه الاتصال وفرض الأبعاد فيه، وتسمى صورة.","en":"This is the substance characterized by continuity and by the possibility of dimensions being posited in it; this is called form.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-059.07","page":59,"ar":"وهي لا تبقى بعينها مع الانفصال، بل تزول إلى هويتين متصلتين.","en":"This [corporeal] form does not persist as the very same form upon separation; rather, it ceases and is succeeded by two connected identities.","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-059.08","page":59,"ar":"فلا بد من أمر قابل للاتصال والانفصال باق في الحالتين، وهو المسمى بالهيولى.","en":"There must therefore be something receptive of both continuity and discontinuity that persists in both conditions: what they call prime matter (hayūlā).","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-059.09","page":59,"ar":"والآخرون على أن الأمر القابل للاتصال والانفصال هو الجسم نفسه، وما يطرأ عليه من الاتصال والانفصال أعراض.","en":"Others maintain that the thing capable of continuity and separation is the body itself and that continuity and separation occurring to it are accidents.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-059.10","page":59,"ar":"وما يتوهم من الامتداد الباقي هو نفس المقدار المستحفظ بتعاقب الخصوصيات.","en":"What is imagined to be an enduring extension is simply magnitude preserved through a succession of particular determinations.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-059.11","page":59,"ar":"فصل: اختلف القائلون بالجزء في أنه هل يقبل الحياة وتوابعها، وهل يمكن وقوع جزء على مفصل الجزأين، وهل يمكن جعل","en":"Chapter. Those who affirm the indivisible part disagree whether it can receive life and its concomitants; whether a part can be placed upon the junction of two parts; and whether it is possible to make—[continued on p.60].","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-060.01","page":60,"ar":"الخط المؤلف من الأجزاء دائرة، وهل له شكل فاختلف المثبتون.","en":"—a line made up of [indivisible] parts into a circle, and whether such a part has a shape; those who affirm the part disagree.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-060.02","page":60,"ar":"فقيل شكله يشبه الكرة، وقيل المثلث، وقيل المربع.","en":"Some say its shape resembles a sphere, others a triangle, and others a square.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-060.03","page":60,"ar":"واتفقوا على أنه لا حظ له من الطول والعرض والعمق، وأن طبيعة الأجزاء واحدة.","en":"They agree that the [individual part] has no share of length, breadth, or depth, and that the nature of the parts is one.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-060.04","page":60,"ar":"فاختلاف الأجسام إنما هو بالأعراض المختلفة بإرادة القادر المختار، وقيل باختلاف الأشكال.","en":"Differences among bodies therefore result from their differing accidents, by the will of the freely choosing omnipotent agent; alternatively, differences of shape have been proposed.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-060.05","page":60,"ar":"واعلم أن في إثبات الجزء سد طريق كثير من أصول الفلاسفة، وسهولة الأمر في كثير من القواعد الدينية.","en":"Know that establishing the indivisible part blocks the route to many of the philosophers’ foundational doctrines and makes many religious principles easier to establish.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-060.06","page":60,"ar":"فصل: زعمت الفلاسفة أن الأجسام أنواع مختلفة باختلاف الصور النوعية التي بها اختلاف الآثار.","en":"Chapter. The philosophers claim that bodies belong to distinct species by virtue of distinct specific forms, which account for their differing effects.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-060.07","page":60,"ar":"والمتكلمون على أنها متماثلة لا تختلف إلا بالعوارض المستندة إلى القادر المختار لتماثل الجواهر الفردة.","en":"The theologians, however, maintain that bodies are alike and differ only through accidents deriving from the freely choosing omnipotent agent, since their constituent indivisible substances are alike.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-060.08","page":60,"ar":"فيجوز على كل ما يجوز على الآخر.","en":"Accordingly, anything possible for one [of these substances] is possible for another.","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-060.09","page":60,"ar":"ثم إنها باقية بحكم الضرورة وفانية بدلالة النص، ولا يخلو كل عن","en":"Further, these [bodies] endure as a matter of necessary judgment, yet perish according to the indication of the revealed text; and none of them is without ... [the sentence continues on the next printed page].","status":"STAGE61_FULL_PAGE_1912_PRINT_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-061.01","page":61,"ar":"شكل لتناهيه، ولا عن حيز بحكم الضرورة، ويمتنع خلوه عن العوارض وضدها كالحركة والسكون وكالاجتماع والافتراق.","en":"—a shape, since it is finite, nor without spatial occupation, as is immediately evident; nor can it be without accidents and their opposites, such as motion and rest, conjunction and separation.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-061.02","page":61,"ar":"واستدل على تناهيها بوجوه.","en":"Several arguments are offered for the finitude of [spatial] dimensions.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-061.03","page":61,"ar":"الأول أنه لو وجد بعد غير متناه لا يمكن بالضرورة أن يتحرك إليه كرة، فيميل قطرها الموازي له إلى المسامتة فيلزم تعين نقطة لا ولي لها لحدودها.","en":"First, if an unbounded extension existed, consider a sphere turned so that its diameter, initially parallel to that extension, approaches alignment with it. This would require a determinate point without an immediately preceding one [the geometrical inference still requires further checking].","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-061.04","page":61,"ar":"لكن كل نقطة تفرض فالمسامتة ممتنعة فوقها قبل المسامتة معها.","en":"Yet for every point posited, alignment at some point beyond it would be impossible before alignment occurred there.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-061.05","page":61,"ar":"الثاني يفرض من نقطة خطان كساقي المثلث يكون بعد ما بينهما بمقدار امتدادهما.","en":"Second, suppose two lines issuing from one point, like the legs of a triangle, such that the distance between them grows with their extension.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-061.06","page":61,"ar":"فيلزم من عدم تناهيهما عدم تناهي ما بينهما.","en":"If the lines extended without end, the distance between them would likewise be without end.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-061.07","page":61,"ar":"الثالث ننقص من البعد غير المتناهي ذراعًا ثم نطبق.","en":"Third, take a cubit away from a supposedly infinite extension and then superimpose the remaining extent upon the original.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-061.08","page":61,"ar":"فإما أن يقع بإزاء كل ذراع من التام ذراع من الناقص فيتساويان، أو لا فينقطعان.","en":"Either each cubit in the complete series faces a cubit in the shortened series, in which case they would be equal, or not, in which case the [shortened] series must end.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-061.09","page":61,"ar":"فإن قيل ما يلي الجنوب غير ما يلي الشمال فلا يكون عدما محضا، وأيضا الواقف على طرف العالم إن أمكنه مد اليد فثمة بعد أو لا فثمة مانع.","en":"An objection says that what lies south of a boundary differs from what lies north, so what is outside the world would not be sheer nothing; furthermore, a person at the world’s edge either can stretch out a hand—in which case there is distance beyond—or cannot, in which case something obstructs the act.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-061.10","page":61,"ar":"قلنا الأول وهم محض، وعدم إمكان مد اليد لعدم الشرط.","en":"We reply: the first is sheer imagining, and inability to extend a hand may result from the absence of a necessary condition [not an external obstacle].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-061.11","page":61,"ar":"ثم طرف الامتداد من حيث كونه منتهى الإشارة ومقصد المتحرك بالحصول فيه جهة.","en":"Moreover, the terminus of an extension, insofar as it is the endpoint of indication and the destination reached by a moving body, is a direction (jiha).","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-061.12","page":61,"ar":"وباعتبار ما للإنسان من الرأس والقدم والظهر والبطن واليدين تنحصر الجهات في ست، ولا حصر","en":"As related to a human being’s head, feet, back, belly, and hands, directions are enumerated as six; but there is no [such fixed enumeration—continued].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-062.01","page":62,"ar":"لها في الحقيقة، والطبيعي الذي لا تبدل العلو والسفل، والأجسام محددة بذواتها وصفاتها.","en":"—in reality. The naturally fixed directions above and below do not interchange; bodies are specified by their natures and properties.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-062.02","page":62,"ar":"وجمهور الفلاسفة على أن الفلكيات قديمة سوى الجزئي من الأوضاع والحركات.","en":"Most philosophers hold that the celestial bodies are eternal, apart from particular positions and motions.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-062.03","page":62,"ar":"وأن العنصريات قديمة بموادها وصورها الجسمية نوعا والنوعية جنسا.","en":"They hold that elemental bodies are eternal with respect to their matter and corporeal form at the specific level, and their specific forms at the generic level.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-062.04","page":62,"ar":"وبعضهم على أن هناك مادة قديمة هي العناصر أو الأرض أو الماء أو الهواء أو النار والبواقي بتلطف أو بتكثف.","en":"Some instead posit an eternal substratum—whether all the elements or earth, water, air, or fire—from which the others arise by rarefaction or condensation.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-062.05","page":62,"ar":"والسماء من دخان يرتفع منها أو جوهر غيرها أو أجسام صغار صلبة كرية أو مختلفة الأشكال أو نور وظلمة أو وحدات تجردت.","en":"Others hold that heaven originated from vapour rising from that substratum, or from a different substance, or from small solid spherical bodies, differently shaped bodies, light and darkness, or isolated units.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-062.06","page":62,"ar":"فصارت نقطا ثم خطوطا ثم سطوحا ثم جسما.","en":"These units then became points, then lines, then surfaces, and finally body.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-062.07","page":62,"ar":"لنا وجوه: الأول أن الجسم لا يخلو عن العرض الممتنع البقاء، وخصوص الحركة والسكون.","en":"We have several arguments [for the createdness of bodies]. First, body is never without accidents, which cannot persist; this applies particularly to motion and rest.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-062.08","page":62,"ar":"لأن كونه في الحيز إن لم يسبقه كون في غير ذلك الحيز فسكون وإلا فحركة.","en":"For when a body occupies a location, if that occupation was not preceded by occupation in a different location, it is rest; otherwise it is motion.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-062.09","page":62,"ar":"وكل منهما في معرض الزوال المنافي للقدم.","en":"Each is liable to cessation, which is incompatible with pre-eternity.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-062.10","page":62,"ar":"فالحركة ظاهرة، وأما السكون فلأن كل جسم قابل للحركة بالاتفاق وبدلالة التماثل ابتداء","en":"The case of motion is evident. As for rest, every body is susceptible to motion, as is conceded and as the similarity of bodies shows, both from the outset—[continued on p. 63].","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-063.01","page":63,"ar":"وانتهاء.","en":"—to its endpoint.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-063.02","page":63,"ar":"فإن قيل لعل لها حركات لا بداية لها ويدوم الكلي بتعاقب جزئياتها الحادثة، قلنا يبطله برهان التطبيق والتكافؤ، وأنه لا وجود للكلي إلا في ضمن الجزئي.","en":"If it is said that there may be motions without a first beginning, while their universal kind endures through successive originated particulars, we reply that this is refuted by the matching and correspondence arguments and by the fact that a universal exists only in its particulars.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-063.03","page":63,"ar":"والثاني أن الجسم محل للحوادث ولا شيء من القديم كذلك لما سيأتي.","en":"Second, body is a locus of originated events, whereas nothing pre-eternal can be such a locus, as will be established.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-063.04","page":63,"ar":"والثالث أن الجسم أثر المختار لما سيأتي من اختيار الواجب.","en":"Third, body is an effect of a choosing agent, as will follow from the proof that the Necessary Existent chooses.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-063.05","page":63,"ar":"قالوا إن وجد في الأزل جميع ما لا بد منه للعالم لزم وجوده، وإن توقف على حادث ينقل الكلام إليه فيتسلسل.","en":"They object: if everything required for the world existed in eternity, the world itself must have existed; but if the world depends on a new event, the same question passes to that event, producing an infinite regress.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-063.06","page":63,"ar":"قلنا لعل من جملة ما لا بد منه الإرادة التي شأنها الترجيح والتخصيص أي وقت شاء الفاعل.","en":"We reply that one of the necessary conditions may be will, whose function is to prefer and specify whichever time the agent chooses.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-063.07","page":63,"ar":"وأما حديث قدم المادة والزمان لاقتضاء حدوثهما تسلسل المواد والأزمنة فضعيف.","en":"As for the argument for the pre-eternity of matter and time on the ground that their origination would imply an infinite regress of materials and times, this is weak.","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-063.08","page":63,"ar":"فصل: قالت الحكماء الجسم إن تألف من أجسام مختلفة الطبائع فمركب، وإلا فبسيط.","en":"Chapter. The philosophers say that a body composed of bodies of different natures is composite; otherwise it is simple.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-063.09","page":63,"ar":"أما فلكي أو عنصري، والمركب إما ممتزج أو غير ممتزج.","en":"The simple body is either celestial or elemental; a composite body is either thoroughly mixed or not.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-063.10","page":63,"ar":"الفلكي ما هو فوق الكل ويسمى محدد الجهات، وينبّه بأنه لا بد لتحديد الجهات الحقيقية كالعلو والسفل من جسم واحد كري محيط بالكل.","en":"The celestial body at the outermost boundary is called the determiner of directions. It is argued that real directions, such as up and down, must be fixed by a single spherical body surrounding the whole.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-063.11","page":63,"ar":"يتحدد بمحيطه القريب وبمركزه البعيد.","en":"Its near direction is determined by its circumference and its remote direction by its centre.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-064.01","page":64,"ar":"أما الجسمية فلوجوب كونه ذا وضع، وأما الوحدة فلأنه لو تعدد فإن أحاط البعض بالبعض تعين المحيط.","en":"Its corporeality follows because it must have position. Its unity follows because if several bodies were posited and some encompassed others, the encompassing one would be the determiner.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-064.02","page":64,"ar":"وإلا تحدد القريب فقط، على أن كون كل منهما في جهة من الآخر يقتضي تقدم محدد آخر.","en":"Otherwise, only the nearer direction would be determined. Moreover, the fact that each of the two would lie in a direction relative to the other would require an antecedent determiner.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-064.03","page":64,"ar":"وأما الكرية فلأن غير الكروي لا يتحدد به البعيد، ولأن تركيبه وزواله عن الاستدارة يقتضي كون الجهة قبله، لأن ذلك بالحركة المستقيمة.","en":"As for sphericity: what is not spherical cannot serve to determine the remote direction. Composition or departure from roundness would already presuppose direction, since that happens through rectilinear motion.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-064.04","page":64,"ar":"وأما الإحاطة فلأن غير المحيط لا يحدد سوى القريب، ولا بد من الإحاطة بالكل، لأن المحاط قد تمتد الإشارة منه إلى الغير فلا يكون هو المنتهى.","en":"As for encompassing: a non-encompassing body defines only the nearer direction. There must be enclosure of the whole, for if what is enclosed admits an indication extending beyond it, it cannot be the final terminus.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-064.05","page":64,"ar":"وزعموا أن المحدد تاسع الأفلاك التي قام الدليل عليها، وأنه يتحرك من المشرق إلى المغرب على منطقة تسمى معدل النهار وقطبين تسميان قطبي العالم.","en":"They suppose that this determiner is the ninth of the celestial spheres said to have been demonstrated, and that it moves from east to west about a circle called the celestial equator and two poles known as the poles of the world.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-064.06","page":64,"ar":"وتحته فلك الثوابت ثم زحل ثم المشتري ثم المريخ ثم الشمس ثم الزهرة ثم عطارد ثم","en":"Beneath it are the sphere of the fixed stars, then Saturn, Jupiter, Mars, the Sun, Venus, and Mercury, followed by—[continued on p.65].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-065.01","page":65,"ar":"ثم القمر، ومنطقة حركة الثامن تسمى منطقة البروج، وتقاطع منطقة العالم على نقطتين تسميان قطتي الاعتدالين الربيعي والخريفي.","en":"—then the Moon. The circle of motion of the eighth sphere is called the zodiacal belt; it intersects the [equatorial] circle at two points, known as the vernal and autumnal equinoctial points.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-065.02","page":65,"ar":"وما بينهما الانقلابين الصيفي والشتوي.","en":"Between them lie the summer and winter solstitial points.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-065.03","page":65,"ar":"وقُسِّم الفلك بتوهم ست دوائر متقاطعة على قطبي البروج اثني عشر قسمًا يسمى كل منها برجًا.","en":"By supposing six circles intersecting at the zodiacal poles, the celestial sphere is divided into twelve divisions, each called a zodiacal sign.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-065.04","page":65,"ar":"وتفاصيل ذلك في علم الهيئة.","en":"The details belong to astronomy (ʿilm al-hayʾa).","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-065.05","page":65,"ar":"وعندنا الخلاء ممكن والحركة مستندة إلى الفاعل المختار.","en":"According to us, the void is possible, and motion depends upon a freely choosing agent.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-065.06","page":65,"ar":"والحركات المستقيمة التي بها الخرق والالتئام جائزة على الفلك.","en":"Rectilinear motions, through which division and reunion would occur, are possible for the celestial sphere.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-065.07","page":65,"ar":"والكواكب سابحة في الأفلاك على الوجه الذي يعلمه الله.","en":"The heavenly bodies swim in their spheres in the manner known to God.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-065.08","page":65,"ar":"قالوا وتحت فلك القمر عنصر النار حارة يابسة شفافة.","en":"They say that beneath the sphere of the Moon lies the element fire, hot, dry, and transparent.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-065.09","page":65,"ar":"ثم الهواء حار رطب شفاف، ثم الماء بارد رطب شفاف، ثم الأرض بارد يابس.","en":"Then comes air, hot, moist, and transparent; then water, cold, moist, and transparent; then earth, cold and dry.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-065.10","page":65,"ar":"ويتقلب كل إلى ما يجاوره، وهو الكون والفساد.","en":"Each changes into the element adjacent to it: this is generation and corruption.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-065.11","page":65,"ar":"ومن العناية الإلهية أن انكشاف البعض من الأرض معاشا للحيوان.","en":"It belongs to divine providence that some of the earth is uncovered and provides the means of life for animals.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-065.12","page":65,"ar":"وللنار طبقة واحدة ولكل من البواقي طبقات.","en":"Fire has one layer, while each of the remaining elements has several.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-065.13","page":65,"ar":"والبخار المتصاعد قد يبلغ الطبقة الزمهريرية من الهواء فيتكاثف","en":"Rising vapour may reach the freezing layer of the air and condense—[continued on p. 66].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-066.01","page":66,"ar":"سحابا وينزل مطرا أو ثلجا أو بردا، وقد لا يبلغها فيصير ضبابا أو ينزل صقيعا أو طلا.","en":"—as cloud, descending as rain, snow, or hail. If it does not reach that layer, it becomes fog or falls as frost or dew.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-066.02","page":66,"ar":"وقد يتصاعد مع البخار دخان فيحتبس في السحاب فيحصل من تمزيقه ومصادمته صوت هو الرعد، ونار لطيفة هي البرق أو كثيفة هي الصاعقة.","en":"Smoke may rise with the vapour and become enclosed in clouds, producing through tearing and collision the sound of thunder and a delicate fire called lightning, or a dense one called the thunderbolt.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-066.03","page":66,"ar":"وقد تتكاثف الأدخنة المتصاعدة بالبرد فتنزل بتموج الهواء وهي الريح الباردة.","en":"Rising exhalations may condense through cold and descend by agitating the air; this is cold wind.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-066.04","page":66,"ar":"وما فيها من الأهوال والأحوال يشهد بأنها ليست إلا من عند مرسل الرياح.","en":"The awe-inspiring occurrences associated with winds testify that they come from none but the Sender of winds.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-066.05","page":66,"ar":"والطين اللزج الكثير إذا انعقد بحر عظيم تكون حجرا، وإذا انحفر أجزاؤه بأسباب تكونت الجبال.","en":"When abundant viscous clay hardens under great heat, it becomes stone; when some of it is hollowed out by various causes, mountains form.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-066.06","page":66,"ar":"ولقلة تسخنها بانعكاس الشعاع تبقى عليها الثلوج والأنداء فتكون المعادن والسحب والعيون.","en":"Because they receive little warmth from reflected rays, snow and moisture remain upon them; minerals, clouds, and springs are consequently formed [on this reported physical account].","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-066.07","page":66,"ar":"وإذا انشقت الأرض بأبخرة وأدخنة محتقنة فيها حدثت الزلازل.","en":"When the earth is split by vapours and exhalations trapped within it, earthquakes result.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-066.08","page":66,"ar":"وقد يكون معها نيران محرقة وأصوات هائلة.","en":"These may be accompanied by burning fires and tremendous sounds.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-066.09","page":66,"ar":"وربما ينقلب بخارها ماء فتنشق عيونًا جارية أو راكدة، وربما يفتقر إلى الكشف عنه، وهي الآبار والقنوات.","en":"Sometimes its vapour turns into water and openings form flowing or still springs; sometimes the water must be exposed by excavation, giving wells and channels.","status":"STAGE56_VISUAL_CORRECTED_1912_PRINT"},{"id":"KAL-066.10","page":66,"ar":"فصل: إذا اجتمعت العناصر المصغرة الأجزاء فتفاعلت","en":"Chapter. When the elements, reduced to minute parts, come together and act upon one another—[continued].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-067.01","page":67,"ar":"قواها فانكسرت سورة كل من الكيفيات حدثت كيفية متوسطة متشابهة في الكل تسمى بالمزاج.","en":"—their powers [interact] and the intensity of each quality is broken; an intermediate quality, similar throughout the mixture, arises and is called temperament (mizāj).","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-067.02","page":67,"ar":"فإن كان من قوى متساوية المقادير فمعتدل وإلا فخارج، إما بكيفية أو بكيفيتين غير متضادتين فينحصر في ثمانية.","en":"If it derives from powers equal in magnitude, it is balanced; otherwise it is unbalanced, through one quality or two nonopposing qualities, so that eight classes result.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-067.03","page":67,"ar":"وقد يقال المعتدل لما يتوفر فيه على الممتزج القسط الذي ينبغي له من الكميات والكيفيات نوعا أو صنفا أو شخصا أو عضوا.","en":"“Balanced” is also applied when the mixture receives the appropriate share of quantities and qualities for its species, subclass, individual, or organ.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-067.04","page":67,"ar":"كل بحسب الخارج أو الداخل، وأعدل البقاع بحسب أوضاع العلويات هو الإقليم الرابع عند الأكثرين.","en":"Balance can be estimated by external or internal criteria; according to most, the fourth climatic zone is the most temperate by the arrangement of the heavenly bodies.","status":"STAGE62_1912_PRINT_AND_ENGLISH_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-067.05","page":67,"ar":"والممتزج إن تحقق فيه مبدأ التغذية والتنمية فإما مع تحقق مبدأ الحس والحركة فهو الحيوان، وإلا فهو النبات، وإلا فالمعدني.","en":"If a mixture possesses a principle of nutrition and growth, it is an animal if it also possesses sensation and motion, but a plant if it does not; if the first principle is absent as well, it is mineral.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-067.06","page":67,"ar":"وهو إما ذائب مع الانطراق كالأجساد السبعة أو مع","en":"Mineral substance is either fusible together with malleability, as in the seven metals; or [fusible] together with—[the next page continues].","status":"STAGE62_1912_PRINT_AND_ENGLISH_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-068.01","page":68,"ar":"الاشتعال كالكبريت أو بدونهما كالزجاج، وإما غير ذائب لإفراط الرطوبة كالزيبق أو اليبوسة كالياقوت.","en":"—combustible, as sulphur is, or neither, as glass is; or it is non-fusible through excessive moisture, as mercury, or dryness, as ruby.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-068.02","page":68,"ar":"ويشارك النبات الحيوان في الاحتياج إلى قوى طبيعية منها الغاذية التي تحيل الغذاء إلى مشابهة المتغذي.","en":"Plants share with animals a need for natural faculties, including the nutritive faculty, which transforms food into the likeness of the nourished body.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-068.03","page":68,"ar":"وتخدمها الجاذبة والماسكة والهاضمة والدافعة.","en":"It is served by the attractive, retentive, digestive, and expulsive faculties.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-068.04","page":68,"ar":"وأولى مراتب الهضم في المعدة وابتداؤه في الفم، ثم في الكبد ثم في العروق ثم في الأعضاء.","en":"Digestion proceeds first in the stomach, beginning in the mouth, and then in the liver, blood vessels, and organs.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-068.05","page":68,"ar":"ومنها النامية التي تدخل الغذاء في أجزاء الجسم فيزيد في أقطاره بنسبة طبيعية.","en":"Another faculty is growth: it introduces nourishment into the bodily parts, increasing their dimensions in a natural proportion.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-068.06","page":68,"ar":"ومنها المولدة التي تحصل من الغذاء ما يصلح مبدأ لشخص آخر وتفصله إلى أجزاء مختلفة وتفيدها الهيئات اللائقة به.","en":"Another is the reproductive faculty: from food it produces material fit to begin another individual, differentiates it into various parts, and imparts the appropriate configurations.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-068.07","page":68,"ar":"وقد يستند هذا إلى أخرى تسمى مصورة.","en":"This latter activity is sometimes attributed to another faculty, called the formative faculty.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-068.08","page":68,"ar":"ثم اضطربوا في أن تعدد هذه القوى بالذات أو بالحيثيات، وفي أن الجامع للأجزاء والحافظ لها والمدبر لها إلى أن يتم الشخص ماذا.","en":"They then became divided over whether these faculties are multiple in their own essences or merely through distinct aspects (ḥaythiyyāt), and over what exactly unifies, preserves and governs the parts until the individual is fully constituted.","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-068.09","page":68,"ar":"وتحيروا في كيفية صدور الأفعال المتقنة والصور","en":"They are perplexed as to the manner in which such well-ordered actions and forms arise—[continued].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-069.01","page":69,"ar":"العجيبة والأشكال الغريبة التي تشاهد في أنواع النبات عن القوى الطبيعية، واللجوء آخرا إلى الخالق القدير.","en":"—the extraordinary forms and unusual shapes observable among plant species from natural faculties, ultimately taking refuge in the explanation provided by the powerful Creator.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-069.02","page":69,"ar":"ويختص الحيوان بقوى نفسانية مدركة ومحركة.","en":"Animals possess psychic faculties of apprehension and motion.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-069.03","page":69,"ar":"فالمدركة الحواس الظاهرة والباطنة.","en":"The apprehensive faculties are the external and internal senses.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-069.04","page":69,"ar":"فمن الظاهرة اللمس وهي قوة سارية في البدن بها يدرك الحرارة والبرودة ونحوها.","en":"Among the external senses is touch, a power diffused throughout the body by which heat, cold, and similar qualities are perceived.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-069.05","page":69,"ar":"الذوق وهي قوة منبثة في العصب المفروش على جرم اللسان بها يدرك الطعوم.","en":"Taste is a power distributed in the nerves spread over the tongue, through which flavours are apprehended.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-069.06","page":69,"ar":"ومنها الشم وهو قوة في زائدتي مقدم الدماغ بها يدرك الروائح بوصول الهواء لا بانفصال الأجزاء.","en":"Smell is a power in the two projections at the front of the brain by which odours are known through the arrival of air, not by the separation of particles from odorous objects.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-069.07","page":69,"ar":"ومنها السمع وهي قوة مودعة في عصب باطن الصماخ يدرك بها الأصوات بوصول الهواء.","en":"Hearing is a power in a nerve of the inner auditory passage, by which sounds are apprehended through the arrival of air.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-069.08","page":69,"ar":"ومنها البصر وهي قوة مودعة في ملتقى العصبتين المجوفتين المتفرقتين إلى العينين يدرك بها الألوان والأضواء.","en":"Sight is a power located at the meeting of two hollow nerves branching toward the eyes, by which colours and lights are perceived.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-069.09","page":69,"ar":"إما بالانطباع أو بخروج الشعاع، ولكل أمارات.","en":"This occurs either by imprinting [of a form] or by the emission of a ray; each view has indications in its favour.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-069.10","page":69,"ar":"فالأول أن نور العين ضروري وانطباع الشبح في القابل المقابل ضروري.","en":"The indications for the first theory include the necessity of light in the eye and the necessity of the likeness being imprinted in the facing receptive subject.","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-069.11","page":69,"ar":"وأن سائر الحواس يأتيها المحسوس، وأن صورة الشمس قد تبقى زمانا في عين من أطال النظر إليها ثم أعرض.","en":"Other senses are affected by the sensible object coming to them, and an image of the sun can remain for a time in the eyes of one who gazed at it and then looked away.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-069.12","page":69,"ar":"والثاني أن الرؤية تتفاوت بتفاوت الشعاع، وأنه يشاهد في الظلمة انفصال النور من العين وعند تغميض العين على السراج خطوط شعاعية","en":"For the second [theory], visual perception varies with the ray; light is reportedly seen leaving the eye in darkness, and rays are perceived when one closes one’s eyes while looking at a lamp—[continued].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-070.01","page":70,"ar":"وعندنا الرؤية بمحض خلق الله.","en":"For us, sight occurs solely through God’s creation [of vision].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-070.02","page":70,"ar":"وما يقال إنه يشترط في الإبصار بعد سلامة الحاسة والقصد وحضور المبصر كونه كثيفا مضيئا مقابلا أو في حكمه بلا حجاب ولا إفراط قرب ولا بعد ولا صغر ولا غلط ممنوع.","en":"It is not accepted that seeing additionally requires, after the soundness of the organ, attention, and the presence of the visible object, that the object be dense, luminous, opposite the viewer or equivalent to it, and that there be no intervening veil, excessive closeness or distance, diminutiveness, or error.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-070.03","page":70,"ar":"وكذا دعوى لزومها عند تلك الشرائط.","en":"The claim that vision necessarily ensues whenever these conditions are fulfilled is likewise rejected.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-070.04","page":70,"ar":"ومن الباطنة الحس المشترك وهي القوة التي يجتمع فيها صور المحسوسات بالتأدي إليها من طرق الحواس.","en":"Among the internal faculties is the common sense: the power in which forms of the sensible objects converge as they are conveyed along the paths of the senses.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-070.05","page":70,"ar":"بدليل الحكم بالبعض على البعض، ومشاهدة النائم والمريض ما ليس في الخارج.","en":"Evidence includes judging one sensible feature by another, and the sleeper’s or sick person’s perception of what has no external presence.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-070.06","page":70,"ar":"ومشاهدة القطرة النازلة خطا مستقيما والشعلة الجوالة دائرة.","en":"It also explains perceiving a falling drop as a straight line and a moving flame as a circle.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-070.07","page":70,"ar":"والخيال وهي التي تحفظ صور المحسوسات بدليل أنها تزول عن الحس المشترك لا بالكلية كما في النسيان بل مع سهولة الاستحضار.","en":"Imagination (khayāl) preserves sensory forms: they leave the common sense without being wholly lost as in forgetting, since they can readily be recalled.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-070.08","page":70,"ar":"والوهم وهي القوة التي بها إدراك المعاني الجزئية، والحافظة لأحكام الوهم.","en":"Estimation (wahm) is the faculty for perceiving particular intentions; retention preserves the judgments of estimation.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-070.09","page":70,"ar":"والمتصرفة تتصرف في الصور والمعاني وتسمى باعتبار استعمال العقل إياها مفكرة، والوهم متخيلة.","en":"The combinative faculty manipulates forms and intentions: when intellect uses it, it is called the cogitative faculty; when estimation uses it, the imaginative faculty.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-070.10","page":70,"ar":"والحس المشترك مقدم البطن الأول من الدماغ والخيال مؤخره والمتخيلة البطن الأوسط والوهم مقدم البطن الأخير والحافظة مؤخره، بدليل الاختلال باختلال المحل.","en":"Common sense is assigned to the front of the brain’s first ventricle, imagination to its rear, the combinative faculty to the middle ventricle, estimation to the front of the last ventricle, and retention to its rear; the evidence offered is that disturbance of a faculty accompanies disturbance of its assigned locus.","status":"STAGE62_1912_PRINT_AND_ENGLISH_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-070.11","page":70,"ar":"والمحركة منها شوقية تبعث على","en":"Among the moving faculties, one is desiderative: it impels [an animal] towards—[completed on printed p.71].","status":"STAGE62_NEWLY_RESTORED_MISSING_MAIN_TEXT"},{"id":"KAL-071.01","page":71,"ar":"جلب المنافع أو دفع المضار، وتسمى الأولى شهوية والثانية غضبية.","en":"—seeking benefit or warding off harm. The former is called the appetitive faculty, and the latter the irascible faculty.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-071.02","page":71,"ar":"ومنها فاعلية تمديد الأعصاب إلى جهة مبدئها كما في القبض أو إلى خلاف جهتها كما في البسط.","en":"Another is an effective power that tightens nerves toward their origin, as in contraction, or away from it, as in extension.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-071.03","page":71,"ar":"مقالة في المجردات وفيها مبحثان.","en":"Discourse on immaterial things, comprising two inquiries.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-071.04","page":71,"ar":"الأول في النفس وقسموها إلى فلكية وإنسانية.","en":"The first concerns the soul, which they divide into celestial and human.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-071.05","page":71,"ar":"وقد تطلق على مبدأ آثار النبات أو الحيوان وتسمى نباتية أو حيوانية.","en":"The word soul may also designate the source of the operations of plants or animals, in which cases it is called vegetative or animal.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-071.06","page":71,"ar":"والمعتمد من رأي المتكلمين أن النفس الإنسانية جسم لطيف سار في البدن لا يتبدل ولا يتحلل أو الأجزاء الأصلية التي لا تقوم الحياة بأقل منها.","en":"The approved theological view is that the human soul is a subtle body diffused through the organism, which does not alter or dissolve, or that it is the fundamental parts without which life cannot subsist.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-071.07","page":71,"ar":"ومن رأي الفلاسفة وبعض المتكلمين أنها جوهر مجرد متصرف في البدن لتوجهه.","en":"The philosophers and certain theologians hold that it is an immaterial substance directing the body through its orientation toward it.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-071.08","page":71,"ar":"أحدها أنا نحكم على الجزئي ومدرك الجزئي منا هو الجسم ليس إلا.","en":"First: we make judgments about particulars, while what apprehends a particular in us, they contend, is nothing but a body.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-071.09","page":71,"ar":"والثاني أن المشار إليه بأنا وهو معنى النفس يتصف بأوصاف الجسم.","en":"A second is that what “I” refers to—the soul—is described by bodily properties.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-071.10","page":71,"ar":"والثالث أن نسبة المجرد إلى الأبدان على السواء فيجوز أن ينتقل، فلا يقطع بأن زيدا الآن هو الذي كان.","en":"Third, an immaterial entity would stand in the same relation to all bodies, so transfer would be possible and one could not be certain that Zayd now is the same person as before.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-071.11","page":71,"ar":"والرابع ظواهر النصوص. واحتجوا بوجوه: أحدها أنها بتعقلها تكون محلا لما ليس بمادي ولا ذي وضع ومقدار","en":"Fourth, the outward tenor of scriptural texts is appealed to. Proponents of the immaterial soul argue, first, that in knowing intelligibles the soul receives what is neither material nor possessed of spatial position or magnitude—[continued].","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-072.01","page":72,"ar":"ولا قابل للانقسام.","en":"—nor is it susceptible of division.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-072.02","page":72,"ar":"والثاني أنها تدرك ذاتها وآلاتها وإدراكها، ولا تضعف بكثرة الأفعال ولا بضعف الأعضاء ولا شيء من القوى الجسمانية كذلك.","en":"Second, the soul knows itself, its instruments, and its own cognition; it is not weakened by a multiplicity of acts or by bodily weakening, whereas no bodily power is like this.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-072.03","page":72,"ar":"الثالث أن القوة العاقلة لو كانت في جسم فإن كفى في تعقله حضوره لم ينقطع تعقله وإلا لم يحصل لامتناع تعدد الصورة لشيء واحد.","en":"Third, if the rational faculty were in a body, then either the object’s mere presence suffices for intellection, in which case it would never cease to be apprehended, or it does not, in which case intellection cannot occur without positing incompatible duplications of a single form.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-072.04","page":72,"ar":"ثم النفوس متماثلة لوحدة حدها وقيل مختلفة لاختلاف لوازمها.","en":"Souls are then said to be alike because their definition is one; another view holds they differ because their necessary concomitants differ.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-072.05","page":72,"ar":"واتفقوا على أبديتها، وقد يستدل بذلك على قدمها وكذا باستغنائها عن المحل.","en":"They agree that souls endure without end; this is sometimes used to infer their pre-eternity, together with their alleged independence of a locus.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-072.06","page":72,"ar":"وقد يستدل على حدوثها بأنه يلزم تعطيلها قبل البدن، بخلاف ما بعد المفارقة فإنها في شغل شاغل.","en":"Their origination is supported by the objection that, if souls existed before bodies, they would be idle, unlike after separation when they remain occupied.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-072.07","page":72,"ar":"وبأنها لو لم تحدث امتنع تعددها، ولو تعددت تمايزها بالماهية أو لوازمها ينافي التماثل، وما يحل فيها كالشعور بهويتها يستلزم الدور.","en":"Moreover, if souls had not come into being, their plurality would be impossible. If they were nonetheless plural, distinguishing them by their quiddities or essential concomitants would conflict with their being of one kind; distinguishing them by what inheres in them, such as consciousness of their own identities, would entail circularity.","status":"STAGE62_SOURCE_WORDING_UNRESOLVED"},{"id":"KAL-072.08","page":72,"ar":"وبالعوارض المادية بأن يكون قبل كل بدن بدن يستلزم","en":"Distinguishing souls by bodily accidents would require a prior body before every body, implying—[continued].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-073.01","page":73,"ar":"التناسخ وقدم الجسم، ثم هي مع الأبدان على التساوي.","en":"—transmigration and the eternity of body; and souls would stand on an equal footing toward all bodies.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-073.02","page":73,"ar":"فلو تعلقت قبل ذلك ببدن آخر للزم ذكر بعض أحواله.","en":"If one soul had previously been associated with another body, it should remember some of that body’s circumstances.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-073.03","page":73,"ar":"ولاجتمعت نفسان لأن تمام المزاج يقتضي حدوث النفس لعموم الفيض.","en":"Two souls would then coexist [in one body], for the body’s complete temperament would cause a new soul to arise by the universality of emanation.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-073.04","page":73,"ar":"وعلى غاية التناسخية أنه لا تعطل في الوجود وأن شأن النفوس الاستكمال.","en":"Transmigrationists ultimately claim that no soul remains idle and that souls are naturally directed toward perfection.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-073.05","page":73,"ar":"وما ثبت بالشرع من المسخ والحشر ليس من التناسخ.","en":"What revelation establishes concerning transformation and resurrection is not transmigration.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-073.06","page":73,"ar":"وفيما يقال من أن النفوس الكاملة تتصل بعالم العقول والمتوسطة تتعلق بأجرام سماوية أو أشباح مثالية والناقصة بأبدان حيوانات تناسبها فيما اكتسبت من الأخلاق.","en":"As for the account according to which perfected souls join the world of intellects, intermediate ones attach to celestial bodies or imaginal forms, and deficient ones inhabit animals corresponding to their acquired habits—","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-073.07","page":73,"ar":"وتمكنت من الهيئات متدرجة في ذلك إلى أن تتخلص من الظلمات، مجرد حكاية.","en":"—progressively becoming established in such configurations until they are freed from darkness, it is merely a reported story.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-073.08","page":73,"ar":"والثابت بالشرع بقاؤها.","en":"What is established by revelation is the soul’s continuance.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-073.09","page":73,"ar":"ووافق الحكماء بناء على استنادها إلى القديم استقلالا أو بشرط حادث في الحدوث دون البقاء.","en":"The philosophers agree, arguing that the soul depends upon the eternal cause either independently or with an originated condition at its coming to be, but not for its continued existence.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-073.10","page":73,"ar":"وأن قوة الفناء يعني إمكانه الاستعدادي تفتقر إلى محل.","en":"Moreover, the potency for annihilation—meaning a dispositional possibility of ceasing to exist—would require a substrate.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-073.11","page":73,"ar":"فصل: مدرك الجزئيات عندنا النفس لأنها الحاكمة بها وعليها ولها السمع والإبصار.","en":"Chapter. On our view, the soul apprehends particulars because it judges concerning them and possesses hearing and sight.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-073.12","page":73,"ar":"وعند الفلاسفة الحواس للقطع بأن","en":"According to the philosophers, the senses do so, since it is evident that—[continued].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-074.01","page":74,"ar":"الإبصار للباصرة وأن آفتها آفة له وما يمتنع ارتسامه في المجرد كثير.","en":"—vision belongs to the organ of sight and damage to it damages vision; much also resists being imprinted in an immaterial subject.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-074.02","page":74,"ar":"والقول بأنها لا تدرك الجزئيات بالذات بل بالآلات يرفع النزاع إلا أنه يقتضي أن لا يبقى إدراك الجزئيات عند فقد الآلات والشريعة بخلافه.","en":"The claim that the soul does not apprehend particulars in itself but only through bodily instruments would remove the disagreement; however, it entails that apprehension of particulars would not persist after the loss of those instruments, whereas revelation indicates the contrary.","status":"STAGE56_VISUAL_CORRECTED_1912_PRINT"},{"id":"KAL-074.03","page":74,"ar":"فصل: قوة النفس باعتبار تأثرها من المبدأ للاستكمال تسمى عقلا نظريا ومراتبه أربع.","en":"Chapter. The soul’s power, considered as receiving perfection from a higher principle, is called theoretical intellect and has four grades.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-074.04","page":74,"ar":"العقل الهيولاني الذي شأنه الاستعداد المحض.","en":"The material (hylic) intellect, characterized by pure preparedness.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-074.05","page":74,"ar":"والعقل بالملكة الذي له استعداد النظريات بحصول الضروريات.","en":"Intellect in habit, prepared for theoretical propositions through possession of necessary first principles.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-074.06","page":74,"ar":"والعقل بالفعل الذي له التمكن في استحضار النظريات من غير افتقار إلى كسب جديد.","en":"Intellect in actuality, able to bring theoretical cognitions to mind without needing to acquire them afresh.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-074.07","page":74,"ar":"والعقل المستفاد الذي هو حضور النظريات عند المشاهدة.","en":"Acquired intellect, in which the theoretical intelligibles are present in actual contemplation.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-074.08","page":74,"ar":"وباعتبار تأثيرها في البدن للتكميل يسمى عقلا عمليا وهي قوة الاستنباط والتصرف لانتظام أمر المعاش والمعاد.","en":"Considered as exercising influence upon the body for its perfection, the soul’s power is called practical intellect: the capacity to infer and act so as to regulate worldly life and the life to come.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-074.09","page":74,"ar":"ويتفرع على الأول الحكمة النظرية المفسرة بمعرفة الأشياء كما هي بقدر الطاقة البشرية.","en":"From the former proceeds theoretical wisdom, defined as knowing things as they are to the measure of human capacity.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-074.10","page":74,"ar":"والثاني الحكمة العملية المفسرة بالقيام بالأمور على ما ينبغي كذلك.","en":"From the latter proceeds practical wisdom, defined as undertaking actions as they ought to be performed within the same human capacity.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-074.11","page":74,"ar":"ومن هنا يقال أن الفقه","en":"For this reason it is said that jurisprudence (fiqh)—[continued on the following page].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-075.01","page":75,"ar":"اسم للعلم والعمل جميعا وقد يقال للحكمة العملية لمعرفة ما يتعلق باختيارنا","en":"[Fiqh is] a name for knowledge and action together. Practical wisdom is also sometimes said to mean knowledge of what concerns our voluntary choices.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-075.02","page":75,"ar":"وإن تعلقت بإصلاح شخص فتهذيب الأخلاق، أو أهل المنزل فتدبير المنزل، أو أهل المدينة فسياسة المدن.","en":"If it concerns the improvement of an individual, it is refinement of character; of a household, household management; and of the inhabitants of a city, political governance.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-075.03","page":75,"ar":"وأصول الأخلاق الفاضلة اعتدال القوة الشهوية وهي العفة، والغضبية وهي الشجاعة، والنطقية وهي الحكمة، ومجموعها العدالة.","en":"The foundations of virtuous character are moderation of the appetitive faculty, which is temperance; the irascible faculty, which is courage; and the rational faculty, which is wisdom. Taken together, they constitute justice.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-075.04","page":75,"ar":"ولكل منها طرفا إفراط وتفريط هما رذيلة؛ فللعفة الخمود والفجور، وللشجاعة التهور والجبن، وللحكمة الجربزة والغباوة.","en":"Each virtue has two vicious extremes, excess and deficiency: for temperance, insensibility and wantonness; for courage, rashness and cowardice; for wisdom, unscrupulous cleverness and stupidity.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-075.05","page":75,"ar":"البحث الثاني في العقل","en":"Second investigation: concerning intellect.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-075.06","page":75,"ar":"احتجوا على وجوده بأن أول المخلوقات لا يجوز أن يكون جسما لتركيبه ولا هيولى أو صورة للزوم فاعلية أحدهما للأخرى ولا عرضا لافتقاره إلى غير فاعله ولا نفسا لعدم الاستقلال باتحاد ما بعدها.","en":"They argue for its existence thus: the first created thing cannot be a body, because a body is composite; nor prime matter or form, because one would have to be an efficient cause of the other; nor an accident, for it depends on something besides its efficient cause; nor a soul, for it cannot subsist independently owing to its union with what comes after it.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-075.07","page":75,"ar":"وإن علة أول الأجسام لا بد أن تشتمل على كثرة لئلا يتعدد أثر الواحد، وأن يستغني في ذاته وفعله عن الجسمية لئلا يفضي إلى تقدم الشيء على نفسه.","en":"The cause of the first bodies must involve some multiplicity, lest many effects proceed directly from the one; yet it must be independent of corporeality in both its essence and its action, lest a thing be prior to itself.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-075.08","page":75,"ar":"وإن دوام حركات الأفلاك ليس إلا لنيل شبيه دائم غير مستقر، فعقول كامل بالفعل لا تتناهى كمالاته.","en":"They say the ceaseless movement of the spheres aims at attaining an abiding likeness which nevertheless is not stably possessed; an intellect perfect in act has perfections that do not come to an end.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-075.09","page":75,"ar":"وإلا يلزم الانقطاع أو طلب المحال.","en":"Otherwise either the movement would cease or an impossibility would be sought.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-076.01","page":76,"ar":"وليس هو الواجب وإلا لم تختلف الحركات، فتعين العقل.","en":"It is not the Necessary Existent, for then the motions would not differ; therefore [they say] an intellect is required.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-076.02","page":76,"ar":"والعقول جواهر مجردة عن المواد في ذاتها وجميع أفعالها.","en":"The intellects are substances abstracted from matter both in their essences and in all their acts.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-076.03","page":76,"ar":"وزعموا أنها لا تكون أقل من عشرة، والعاشر هو المدبر لعالم العناصر.","en":"They claim that there are at least ten, the tenth being the governor of the world of elements.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-076.04","page":76,"ar":"وأنها أزلية منحصرة أنواعها في أشخاص جامعة لكمالاتها عاقلة لذواتها ولسائر المجردات وجميع الكليات.","en":"They claim that these are eternal; that each species is confined to its individual, which possesses its perfections, understands itself, the other immaterial beings, and all universals.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-076.05","page":76,"ar":"وأنها مبادئ لكمالات النفوس والأجسام ويصدر عن الأول باعتبار وجوده عقل، وباعتبار وجوبه بالغير نفس، وباعتبار إمكانه جسم.","en":"They regard the intellects as sources of perfection for souls and bodies. From the first [intellect], insofar as it has existence, another intellect proceeds; insofar as it is necessary through another, a soul; and insofar as it is possible, a body.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-076.06","page":76,"ar":"وزعموا أن الملائكة هم العقول المجردة والنفوس الفلكية.","en":"They claim that the angels are the immaterial intellects and the celestial souls.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-076.07","page":76,"ar":"وأن الجن أرواح مجردة لها تصرف في الأجسام العنصرية، والشياطين هي القوى المتخيلة.","en":"They claim that the jinn are immaterial spirits exercising influence upon elemental bodies and that the devils are imaginative powers.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-076.08","page":76,"ar":"وأن لكل فلك روحا كليا يتشعب منه أرواح كثيرة، والمدبر لأمر العرش يسمى بالنفس الكلية.","en":"They hold that each sphere has a universal soul, from which numerous souls branch off, and that the soul directing the Throne is called the Universal Soul.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-076.09","page":76,"ar":"ولكل من أنواع الكائنات روحا يدبر أمره يسمى بالطبع التام.","en":"They further posit, for each kind of generated being, a spirit governing its affairs; this they call the “perfect nature” (al-ṭibāʿ al-tāmm).","status":"STAGE62_1912_PRINT_AND_ENGLISH_VERIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-076.10","page":76,"ar":"وعندنا الملائكة أجسام لطيفة تتشكل بأشكال مختلفة شأنهم الخير والطاعة والقدرة على الأعمال الشاقة.","en":"According to us, angels are subtle bodies that assume different forms, characterized by goodness, obedience, and the capacity for arduous tasks.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-077.01","page":77,"ar":"والجن كذلك إلا أن منهم المطيع والعاصي، والشياطين شأنهم الشر والإغواء.","en":"The jinn are likewise [subtle bodies], except that among them are the obedient and the disobedient; devils are marked by evil and seduction.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-077.02","page":77,"ar":"ولا يمتنع ظهور الكل على بعض الأبصار وفي بعض الأحوال.","en":"There is nothing to preclude their appearing to some observers under some circumstances.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-077.03","page":77,"ar":"وفاء على كل كلام في كل باب أعرضنا عنه مخافة الإطناب والله الهادي إلى طريق الصواب.","en":"We have omitted many further discussions belonging to each topic for fear of excessive prolixity. God guides to the right path.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-077.04","page":77,"ar":"الباب الخامس في الإلهيات، وفيه فصول.","en":"Fifth chapter: theological matters, consisting of sections.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-077.05","page":77,"ar":"الفصل الأول: في الذات.","en":"First section: on the divine essence.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-077.06","page":77,"ar":"لا بد للممكنات من واجب وللمحدثات من قديم دفعا للدور والتسلسل.","en":"Possible beings require a Necessary Being, and originated beings an eternal one, to exclude causal circularity and infinite regress.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-077.07","page":77,"ar":"وقد شاع في الكتاب الإلهي الإرشاد إلى الاستدلال بالآفاق والأنفس بذواتها وصفاتها لإمكانها وحدوثها.","en":"Divine scripture frequently directs attention to the horizons and the self—their entities and qualities—as evidence through their possibility and origination.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-077.08","page":77,"ar":"لأنه الظاهر في نظر الكل النافع للجمهور والاستكثار فيه ربما يفضي إلى اليقين.","en":"This approach is evident to everyone and beneficial to the general public; multiplying such reflections can lead to certainty.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-077.09","page":77,"ar":"والتأمل فيه إلى أن الصانع لمثل هذا لا يكون إلا غنيا مطلقا موصوفا بصفات الكمال منزها عن الزوال.","en":"Reflection upon these things leads to the conclusion that the maker of such things cannot be other than absolutely self-sufficient, endowed with attributes of perfection and exalted above passing away.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-077.10","page":77,"ar":"ثم الحق أن ذات الواجب مخالف لسائر الذوات، لئلا يلزم وجوب الممكن أو إمكان الواجب، وأن كونه أزليا أبديا غني عن البيان.","en":"The truth is that the essence of the Necessary Being is unlike every other essence; otherwise the possible would have to be necessary or the Necessary would be possible. That He is beginningless and endless needs no elaboration.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-077.11","page":77,"ar":"فصل في التنزيهات.","en":"Section: on affirming God’s transcendence.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-077.12","page":77,"ar":"الواجب لذاته لا جزء له وإلا لأمكن ولا تعدد لأفراده.","en":"The Necessary in itself has no part—for otherwise it would be possible—and cannot have multiple individual instances.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-078.01","page":78,"ar":"لأن ما به الامتياز إما نفس الماهية الواجبة أو جزؤها أو لازمها فلا تعدد، أو منفصل فلا وجوب.","en":"For that by which alleged instances differ must be identical with necessary essence, a part of it, or something entailed by it—in which case multiplicity disappears—or else extrinsic, in which case necessity is lost.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-078.02","page":78,"ar":"ولأن وقوع ما قصده الواجبان إما بهما معا فلا استقلال، أو بكل منهما فتَوارد العلتين على معلول واحد، أو بأحدهما فيترجح بلا مرجح.","en":"If two necessary beings were posited, the effect intended by both would either occur through both together, denying independent efficacy; or through each separately, bringing two causes to bear upon one effect; or through only one of them, making one prevail without a determinant.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-078.03","page":78,"ar":"ولأن أحدهما إن لم يتمكن من ضد ما قصده الآخر عجز، وإن تمكن فإن وقعا معا لزم اجتماع الضدين، واللازم عجزهما أو عجز أحدهما مع لزوم ارتفاع مثل الحركة والسكون، والترجيح بلا مرجح.","en":"If one could not bring about the contrary of what the other intended, it would be powerless. If it could, the occurrence of both contraries together would be impossible; otherwise one or both would be powerless, or both motion and rest would be excluded, or one alternative preferred without a preferrer.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-078.04","page":78,"ar":"ولأنهما إن اتفقا على كل مقدور فالتوارد وإلا فالتمانع، والنصوص كثيرة ولو كان فيهما آلهة إلا الله لفسدتا إشارة إلى دليل التمانع.","en":"Furthermore, if the two agreed on every possible object, their causes would coincide in producing a single effect; otherwise there would be mutual obstruction. Many texts point to this, including “Had there been in them gods other than God, they would have been corrupted.”","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-078.05","page":78,"ar":"والمشركون هم","en":"Those who associate partners with God are—[the list follows on p. 79].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-079.01","page":79,"ar":"الثنوية القائلون بالنور والظلمة والمجوس (بأهرمن ويزدان) والمثبتون للولد وعبدة الأصنام والكواكب لاستلزام استحقاق المعبودية للوجوب.","en":"—the dualists who affirm light and darkness; the Magians [who affirm] Ahriman and Yazdān; those who attribute offspring [to God]; and worshippers of idols and celestial bodies. For worthiness to be worshipped entails necessary existence.","status":"STAGE63_1912_PRINT_TRANSLATION_DIRECTLY_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-079.02","page":79,"ar":"وأما القائلون بقدم الصفات وخلق الحيوان لأفعاله والشيطان للقبائح والعقول للنفوس ولبعض الأجسام والأفلاك لما في عالم العناصر فيبالغون في التوحيد.","en":"Those who affirm eternal divine attributes, human creation of human acts, the devil’s responsibility for evil, or intellects as causes of souls, certain bodies and sublunary phenomena may nevertheless regard themselves as safeguarding divine unity.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-079.03","page":79,"ar":"إلا أن القول بتعدد الذوات القديمة الموجودة لذوات مستقلة خطب هائل.","en":"Nonetheless, affirming a plurality of eternally existing independent essences is a grave matter.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-079.04","page":79,"ar":"والواجب ليس بجسم ولا عرض للاحتياج ولا متحيز للزوم قدم الحيز بل وجوبه وإمكان الواجب لأن المتحيز يحتاج إلى الحيز دون العكس ولا جوهر لإمكانه.","en":"The Necessary Being is not a body or accident, because of dependence; nor spatially confined, since this would entail the pre-eternity—indeed, the necessity—of spatial locus and the possibility of the Necessary Being: what is spatially confined needs a locus, not conversely. Nor is He a substance in the relevant technical sense, since it admits possibility.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-079.05","page":79,"ar":"ولو أريد بالجوهر القائم بنفسه وبالجسم الموجود فممتنع شرعا واحتياطا.","en":"Even if “substance” were intended simply to mean what subsists in itself, and “body” what exists, these expressions are prohibited on scriptural grounds and as a precaution.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-079.06","page":79,"ar":"والقول بأنه جسم على صورة إنسان أو غيره وفي جهة العلو مماس للعرش أو محاذيا له تمسكا بأن كل موجود جسم أو جسماني ومتحيزا وحال فيه ومتصل بالعالم أو منفصل عنه جهالة.","en":"The claim that God is a body in human or another form, situated above, touching the Throne or facing it—based on the assumption that every existent must be a body or embodied, spatially confined, inhering, connected to the world or detached from it—is ignorance.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-079.07","page":79,"ar":"والنصوص مؤولة.","en":"The scriptural expressions in question receive appropriate interpretation.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-079.08","page":79,"ar":"ولا يتحد لما سبق وللزوم الانقلاب أو اجتماع الوجوب والإمكان ولا يحل لامتناع الاحتياج والتحيز.","en":"Nor does He undergo union (*ittiḥād*), for the foregoing reasons and because this would entail transformation or the conjunction of necessity and possibility; nor does He indwell (*ḥulūl*), since dependence and spatial location are impossible for Him.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-079.09","page":79,"ar":"وحكى الحلول والاتحاد عن النصارى في حق عيسى وعن بعض الغلاة في","en":"The doctrines of indwelling and union are reported of Christians concerning Jesus, and of some extremists concerning—[continued].","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-080.01","page":80,"ar":"حق علي.","en":"—ʿAlī.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-080.02","page":80,"ar":"ويمتنع اتصافه بحادث لأنه تغير ولأنه يمتنع في الأزل فيلزم الانقلاب، ويوجب زوال ضده فيلزم عدم الخلو عن الحادث.","en":"He cannot be characterized by an originated attribute: this would be change; the attribute would have been absent in pre-eternity, implying an inadmissible change of condition, and the removal of its opposite would entail never being free of originated states.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-080.03","page":80,"ar":"وأما الاتصاف بما له تعلق حادث أو ما يتجدد من السلوب والإضافات والأحوال فليس من التنازع.","en":"As for possessing an attribute with an originated relational application, or the renewal of negations, relations, and states, that is not the point in dispute.","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-080.04","page":80,"ar":"فصل في الصفات الوجودية.","en":"Section: on positive or existent attributes.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-080.05","page":80,"ar":"الحق أنها زائدة على الذات إذ لا يعقل من العالم إلا من له العلم وهكذا، ولو كان علمه ذاته لما أفاد حمله ولم تميز الصفات ولم تفتقر إلى الإثبات.","en":"The correct view is that the attributes are additional to the essence: one understands “knowing” as possessing knowledge, and likewise in other cases. If His knowledge were simply His essence, predicating it would contribute nothing; the distinct attributes would not be distinguished and would not need independent establishment.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-080.06","page":80,"ar":"وجاز اتصافه بما يتصف به الذات.","en":"It is possible to predicate of Him what can be predicated of the essence.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-080.07","page":80,"ar":"وقالت المعتزلة فيه استكمال بالغير وتعليل للعالمية بالعلم مع أنها واجبة له وتكثير للقدماء.","en":"The Muʿtazila object that this entails perfection received from another, explains His being knowing by knowledge even though this is necessary to Him, and multiplies eternal entities.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-080.08","page":80,"ar":"قلنا الصفة لا عين ولا غير ولو سلم فلا يلزم امتناع الاستكمال بمعنى ثبوت صفة الكمال له.","en":"We reply: an attribute is neither simply identical [with the essence] nor wholly other; even granting the objection, it would not preclude “completion” in the sense of possessing a perfection.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-080.09","page":80,"ar":"والواجب بمعنى اللازم قد يعلل بما ينشأ عن الذات، والكفر تعدد الذوات القديمة كزعم النصارى.","en":"What is necessary in the sense of being inseparably concomitant may be explained through what proceeds from the essence; unbelief concerns multiplying ancient essences, as in certain Christian claims.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-080.10","page":80,"ar":"قالوا في بقاء الصفات يلزم قيام المعنى بالمعنى وهو محال. قلنا المستحيل قيام العرض بالعرض والمعنى أعم ولو سلم فهي باقية ببقاء الذات أو بقاؤها عينها.","en":"They object that the persistence of attributes would require one meaning to subsist in another, which they deem impossible. We answer that what is impossible is one accident subsisting in another; “meaning” is broader. Even if conceded, attributes persist with the essence or their continuance is identical with them.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-080.11","page":80,"ar":"قالوا تماثل قدرته قدرة الشاهد فلا تختلف آثارهما، قلنا ممنوع [وتتمة التعليل في هذا السطر تحتاج مقابلة شاهد آخر].","en":"They object that His power is of the same kind as that of an observed agent, and so the effects of the two powers cannot differ. We deny this. [The exact subsequent explanation of the dependence of originated things upon God needs a second witness.]","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-081.01","page":81,"ar":"ولا استلزام ارتفاع ما ثبت بالإيجاب ارتفاع الموجب ولا امتناع استناد مواضع الكواكب والأقطاب واختلاف الأوضاع والأشكال إلى غير المختار.","en":"The disappearance of what is established through necessitation does not entail the disappearance of the necessitating cause. Nor, in the argument under consideration, is it impossible to ascribe the positions of stars, the poles, and variations in configurations and shapes to a nonchoosing agent.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-081.02","page":81,"ar":"وقد تمسك بالأدلة السمعية وبأن القدرة وغيرها صفات كمال وأضدادها سمات نقص وبأن إتقان العالم وانتظامه لا يتصور إلا من قادر عالم.","en":"The discussion appeals to revealed proofs, to the fact that power and the other attributes are perfections whereas their opposites are defects, and to the order and precision of the world, which cannot be conceived except as arising from an agent with knowledge and power.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-081.03","page":81,"ar":"تمسك المخالف بأن تعلق القدرة لا يكون إلا بالترجيح فيتسلسل، وبأنه إما قديم فيكون الأثر قديما أو حادث فيتسلسل، وبأن الأثر إنما يصدر بعد تمام الشرائط وحينئذ لا اختيار.","en":"The opponent objects that the exercise of power requires a preference, giving rise to a regress; that if its determining relation is eternal the effect is eternal, whereas if originated it leads to a regress; and that an effect arises only once all conditions are complete, apparently leaving no choice.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-081.04","page":81,"ar":"وبأن أثر الاختيار إن كانت أولى لزم الاستكمال وإلا فالعبث، وبأنه لو امتنع في الأزل لزم الانقلاب أو أمكن فاستناد الأزلي إلى المختار.","en":"They further object that if the chosen effect is preferable this entails acquiring perfection, otherwise acting pointlessly; and if action was impossible in pre-eternity, this implies change, whereas if it was possible an eternal thing would depend upon a free chooser.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-081.05","page":81,"ar":"وبأنه إما معلوم الوجود فمحتم، أو العدم فممتنع.","en":"They argue that if the act is known as existent, it is inevitable, and if known as nonexistent, it is impossible.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-081.06","page":81,"ar":"وأجيب بأن المرجح تعلق الإرادة لذاتها فلا تسلسل، وبأنه يجوز تعلق الإرادة في الأزل بإيجاده في وقته.","en":"The response is that the determining factor is the will’s relation by its own nature, avoiding regress, and that an eternal will can relate to bringing about an effect at its appointed time.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-081.07","page":81,"ar":"وبأن الوجوب بالاختيار عين الاختيار، وبأن الفعل الأولى في نفسه أو للغير لا يكون عبثا.","en":"Necessity through voluntary choice does not negate choice; an act can be preferable in itself or for another without being futile.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-081.08","page":81,"ar":"وبأن الحادث ممكن في الأزل لذاته يمتنع لكونه أثر المختار، وبأنه لزم وجوده بقدرته ثم قدرته غير منقطعة ولا مقتصرة على بعض الممكنات.","en":"An originated effect can be possible in itself from eternity while not realized until the choice of the agent; its existence follows from divine power, which neither ceases nor is confined to some possibilities.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-082.01","page":82,"ar":"للقادرية هو الذات والمصحح للمقدورية هو الإمكان فالله على كل شيء قدير.","en":"The ground of being powerful is the essence, while what qualifies something as an object of power is its possibility: thus God has power over all things.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-082.02","page":82,"ar":"وخالف بعض المعتزلة في القبيح والبعض في مقدور العبد والبعض في مثله.","en":"Some Muʿtazilites dissent concerning evil acts, others concerning what falls within human power, and others concerning cases like these.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-082.03","page":82,"ar":"فالكل مستند إليه ابتداء عندنا، وأعم من أن يكون ابتداء أو بواسطة عند غيرنا، وبلا اختيار ابتداء أو بواسطة عند الفلاسفة.","en":"On our account, everything depends directly upon Him. On other accounts, the dependence may be direct or through an intermediary; for the philosophers it proceeds without choice, whether immediately or mediately.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-082.04","page":82,"ar":"ومنها العلم لاستناد العالم مع إحكامه وانتظامه إليه ولكونه قادرا مختارا وإثباته بالسمع دون خلاف مثل القدرة والكلام.","en":"Another attribute is knowledge, established through the world’s dependence on Him together with its precision and order, and through His being a powerful voluntary agent. Revelation likewise establishes it, as it establishes power and speech.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-082.05","page":82,"ar":"وعلمه تعالى لا ينقطع ولا يقتصر، لمثل ما مر.","en":"His knowledge is neither interrupted nor confined, for reasons analogous to those already given.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-082.06","page":82,"ar":"وخالف بعضهم في العلم بذاته لعدم الإثنينية وبالعلم للزوم لا تناهي الصفات وبغير المتناهي لاستحالة وجوده وبالمعدوم لأنه نفي محض.","en":"Some deny His knowledge of His own essence on the ground that knowledge requires two terms; some object to knowledge of knowledge because it would entail an infinity of attributes; others to knowing the infinite because they deem it impossible to exist; and others to knowing the nonexistent because they take it to be pure negation.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-082.07","page":82,"ar":"والفلاسفة في العلم بالجزئيات لتغيرها.","en":"Philosophers deny [on their account] His knowledge of particulars because these change.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-082.08","page":82,"ar":"ورد بأن من الجزئي ما لا يتغير وبأن تغير الإضافة لا يوجب تغير المضاف، كالقديم يوجد قبل الحادث ثم معه ثم بعده.","en":"The reply is that some particulars do not change, and changes in a relation do not entail a change in the thing related: the eternal exists before an event, then with it, then after it.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-082.09","page":82,"ar":"وهذا معنى ما قيل إن علم الباري بأن الشيء سيوجد هو نفس علمه بأنه وجد.","en":"This is the sense in which it is said that the Creator’s knowing that a thing will exist is the very same knowledge as His knowing that it has existed.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-082.10","page":82,"ar":"فالعلم لا يتغير بتغير المعلوم كما لا يتكثر بكثرته، كمرآة تنكشف بها الصور، وهذا إنما يصح إذا لم يجعل العلم نفس الإضافة بل صفة ذات إضافة.","en":"Knowledge does not change when the known object changes, nor become multiple through the multiplicity of its objects, just as a mirror reveals many images. But this account is sound only if knowledge is not made identical with the relation itself, but is a quality having a relation.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-082.11","page":82,"ar":"ومنها الإرادة وهي صفة غير العلم بها يتخصص أحد طرفي","en":"Another is the will, an attribute other than knowledge, through which one of two sides [of a possibility] is specified—[continued on p.83].","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-083.01","page":83,"ar":"المقدور بالوقوع وتعلقها لذاتها وقدّمها لا يوجب قدم المراد.","en":"—of an object of power as actual. Its relation is grounded in itself, and the eternity of will does not entail the eternity of what is willed.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-083.02","page":83,"ar":"والقول بأنها حادثة قائمة بذاته ظاهر البطلان وبأنها نفس العلم بالنظام الأكمل أو كون القادر غير مكره ولا ساه أو العلم في فعله والأمر في فعل غيره أو الداعية إلى الفعل بمعنى العلم بنفع زائد في الفعل لكل ضعف.","en":"It is plainly false to hold that will is an originated attribute subsisting in God; likewise inadequate are definitions of will as knowledge of the best arrangement, the agent’s absence of compulsion or forgetfulness, knowledge of His own acts or command concerning another’s, or a motive toward an act understood as knowledge of some additional benefit.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-083.03","page":83,"ar":"وقد دل عليه النصوص واستلزامه الفعل بالاختيار لا ينافي الاختيار.","en":"Scriptural texts establish will, and its connection with voluntary action does not negate choice.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-083.04","page":83,"ar":"ومنها الحياة والسمع والبصر ولدلالة النصوص القاطعة وإجماع الأنبياء بل جميع العقلاء على ذلك.","en":"Other attributes are life, hearing and sight, established by decisive scriptural passages and the consensus of the prophets—indeed, of rational people generally.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-083.05","page":83,"ar":"ولأن الخلو عنها نقص، فثبتت صفات ثلاثة قديمة ولا يلزم قدم المسموع والمبصر.","en":"Lacking them would be a defect. Hence these three attributes are affirmed as eternal; it does not follow that things heard and seen are themselves eternal.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-083.06","page":83,"ar":"وما يقال إنها اعتدال المزاج وتأثر الحاسة أو تجرد العلم بالمسموعات والمبصرات ممنوع.","en":"The suggestion that they are merely a balance of bodily temperament, a sensory impression, or abstract knowledge of things heard and seen is rejected.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-083.07","page":83,"ar":"وأما الشم والذوق واللمس فلم يرد بها الشرع ولم يجوزها العقل لكن المذهب أنه يدرك متعلقاتها.","en":"As for smelling, tasting and touching, revelation has not affirmed them as divine attributes, nor has reason allowed them as such; nevertheless, the adopted position is that God apprehends their respective objects.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-083.08","page":83,"ar":"ومنها الكلام بشهادة الأنبياء مع عدم توقف دلالة المعجزة عليه للدور ولأن ضده في الحي نقص وهو صفة أزلية منافية للسكوت والآفة يدل عليها بالعبارة والكتابة.","en":"Another attribute is speech, affirmed by the testimony of the prophets, without making the probative force of a miracle circularly depend on it. Its opposite would be an imperfection in a living being; it is an eternal attribute opposed to silence and incapacity, signified by spoken expression and writing.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-083.09","page":83,"ar":"وجمهور الفرق على أن المعقول من الكلام هو الحسي دون النفسي ولم يقل بقدمه إلا الحنابلة والحشوية وبطلانه ضروري.","en":"Most theological groups take sensible speech, rather than inward speech, to be what “speech” means. Only the Ḥanbalites and those termed ḥashwiyya maintain its eternity, and the falsity of that [claim concerning sensible speech] is held to be evident.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-084.01","page":84,"ar":"لكونه مرتب الأجزاء ممتنع البقاء وعند المعتزلة هو حادث في جسم ويعني بتكلم الباري به هو خلقه فيه.","en":"Because [audible speech] consists of ordered parts and does not persist, the Muʿtazilites hold that it is originated in a body: God’s speaking it means that He creates it therein.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-084.02","page":84,"ar":"لنا أن معنى المتكلم من قام به الكلام ولا يتصور اللفظي فتعين المعنوي.","en":"Our argument is that a speaker is one in whom speech subsists; since verbal speech cannot subsist in God, internal or meaningful speech is intended.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-084.03","page":84,"ar":"والقول بأن النظم قد يكون دفعي الأجزاء كالقائم بنفس الحافظ والطابع وهم.","en":"The claim that ordered discourse can exist all at once, as in the mind of one who memorizes it or in a stamp, is an illusion.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-084.04","page":84,"ar":"وأيضا كل من يأمر وينهى ويخبر يجد في نفسه معنى غير العلم والإرادة يدل عليه بالعبارة والكتابة.","en":"Further, everyone who commands, forbids, or reports finds within himself a meaning other than knowledge or will, which he signifies by utterance and writing.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-084.05","page":84,"ar":"وقد شاع عند أهل اللسان إطلاق الكلام عليه ولا نزاع في أنه يقال بالاشتراك أو المجاز المشهور على النظم المخصوص المسموع.","en":"It is common among speakers of the language to call this “speech”; there is no dispute that the term also applies, by equivocation or common figurative usage, to the particular audible arrangement.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-084.06","page":84,"ar":"لا مجرد الدال على كلامه القديم بل لأنه أنشأه برقمه في اللوح المحفوظ أو بحروفه في الملك ويختص العربي منه باسم القرآن وهو المتعارف عند العامة.","en":"The audible arrangement is not merely an indicator of His eternal speech; He brings it forth as writing on the Preserved Tablet or as articulated letters by an angel. Its Arabic form alone is named the Qurʾān in common usage.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-084.07","page":84,"ar":"وفي علم الأصول وإليه يرجع ما يستدل بالحدوث مثل المنزل والمقروء والمسموع والتحدي به والفرق.","en":"In legal theory, the proofs of the occurrence of the recited or transmitted wording—its being sent down, recited, heard, and used in the challenge—refer to this sense.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-084.08","page":84,"ar":"ونحو ذلك قالوا الإخبار بالماضي في الأزل كذب والأمر والنهي سفه وعبث.","en":"They object: reporting past events in pre-eternity would be false, while commanding and forbidding then would be foolish and pointless.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-084.09","page":84,"ar":"وأجيب بأنه إنما يصير الكلام أحد الأقسام فيما لا يزال مع أنه يكفي مخاطب معقول.","en":"It is answered that speech becomes one of these divisions in temporal application (*fīmā lā yazāl*), and it suffices that an addressee be conceivable.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-084.10","page":84,"ar":"والتحقيق أنه طلب ممن سيوجد هذا، والمذهب أنه واحد في الأزل يتكثر بحسب التعلقات.","en":"More precisely, it is a request addressed to someone who will come into existence. The adopted position holds that speech is one in pre-eternity, becoming multiple by its relational applications.","status":"STAGE63_1912_PRINT_TRANSLATION_DIRECTLY_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-085.01","page":85,"ar":"إذ لم يرد السمع بالتعدد.","en":"For revelation has not established a multiplicity [of the eternal speech itself].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-085.02","page":85,"ar":"وأثبت الشيخ الأشعري البقاء صفة لأن الباقي بلا بقاء كالعالم بلا علم.","en":"Shaykh al-Ashʿarī affirmed subsistence as an attribute, arguing that a thing that abides without an attribute of abiding would resemble something called knowing without knowledge.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-085.03","page":85,"ar":"ورد بأنه استمرار الوجود وبأنه يعود الكلام في بقاء البقاء.","en":"The response is that subsistence means the continuation of existence; moreover, the same question would recur concerning the subsistence of subsistence.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-085.04","page":85,"ar":"وبعض الفقهاء التكوين لأنه تعالى خالق إجماعا ومدح به نفسه بكلام أزلي فيلزم أن يكون صفة أزلية.","en":"Some jurists affirm bringing-into-being (takwīn) as an attribute: God is Creator by consensus and praises Himself as such in eternal speech, so they argue that creation must be an eternal attribute.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-085.05","page":85,"ar":"وهي المعنى بقول الكل إنه يكون الأشياء في أوقاتها بكلمة أزلية هي كن ولا يلزم من قدمه قدم المكون كالعلم.","en":"They explain this by the common statement that He brings things into existence at their appointed times through the eternal command “Be”; the eternity of this attribute no more entails the eternity of what is produced than eternal knowledge entails the eternity of its object.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-085.06","page":85,"ar":"والحق أنه معنى إضافي يعقل من تعلق المؤثر بالأثر وليس سوى تعلق القدرة والإرادة والمدح بالخالقية في الأزل مثل المدح بأنه (يسبح له ما في السماوات وما في الأرض) أي هو بحيث له ذلك فيما لا يزال.","en":"The correct view is that creating is a relational meaning, understood through the connection of agent and effect, and is nothing beyond the relation of power and will. Praising God as Creator in pre-eternity is comparable to praising Him on the basis that “what is in the heavens and what is on earth glorifies Him”: that is, He is such that this is attributable to Him when its time comes.","status":"STAGE63_1912_PRINT_TRANSLATION_DIRECTLY_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-085.07","page":85,"ar":"وما قيل أن التكوين هو المكون فمعناه أن المفهوم من الخلق هو المخلوق وأن الحاصل من التأثير هو الأثر لا غير.","en":"When it is said that “creating is the created thing,” this means that what is conceived through “creation” is the product, and what results from producing is simply the effect.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-085.08","page":85,"ar":"وأما سائر ما يطلق عليه من الصفات فراجعة إلى الصفات المذكورة مثل الاستواء واليد والوجه والعين مجازات وتمثيلات.","en":"Other divine descriptions ultimately refer back to the attributes mentioned: expressions such as sitting upon the Throne, hand, face, and eye are figures and analogical expressions.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-085.09","page":85,"ar":"فصل في أحواله.","en":"Section: concerning His states and what may be predicated of Him.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-085.10","page":85,"ar":"الحق أنه تعالى يصح أن يرى بمعنى حصول الحالة الإدراكية الحاصلة عند النظر إلى القمر من غير جهة ولا","en":"The correct view is that God may be seen, meaning that the perceptual state experienced when looking at the moon may occur [regarding Him], without spatial direction or—[continued].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-086.01","page":86,"ar":"مقابلة وأنه يحصل ذلك للمؤمنين في الجنة.","en":"—confrontation, and that this will occur for believers in Paradise.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-086.02","page":86,"ar":"أما الصحة فلأن موسى عليه السلام طلب الرؤية والله تعالى علقها على الممكن في نفسه وهو استقرار الجبل.","en":"As to its possibility: Moses, peace be upon him, asked for the vision, and God made it conditional upon something possible in itself, the mountain’s remaining in place.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-086.03","page":86,"ar":"والقول بأنه إنما طلب العلم الضروري أو الرؤية لأجل القوم أو زيادة اطمئنان ينفي سماع الكلام ظاهر البطلان.","en":"The suggestions that Moses merely requested necessary knowledge, that he requested the vision for his people, or that he sought added reassurance are plainly implausible in view of his having already heard the divine speech.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-086.04","page":86,"ar":"وقد يستدل بأن متعلق الرؤية المشترك بين الجوهر والعرض ليس إلا الوجود المشترك بينهما وبين الواجب.","en":"One argument maintains that the common object of sight shared by substance and accident is existence itself, which they share with the Necessary Being.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-086.05","page":86,"ar":"لما مر من أن الحدوث أو الإمكان عدمي مع اشتراك المعدوم فيه، وجواز الرؤية عند تحقق ما يصلح متعلقا لها ضروري.","en":"This follows from the previous point: origination and possibility are nonpositive, while nonexistent things share in them. Once something exists that can qualify as a thing seen, the possibility of vision is self-evident.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-086.06","page":86,"ar":"وصحة رؤية كل شيء موجود حتى الطعوم والروائح والعلوم تلزم من الدليل وإن استبعدت.","en":"This argument would permit seeing anything that exists, even tastes, smells and cognitions, however implausible that sounds.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-086.07","page":86,"ar":"فإن قيل الواحد النوعي قد يعلل بعلل مختلفة قلنا الكلام في المتعلق والرؤية قد تتعلق بشيء من غير أن يدرك جوهريته أو عرضيته فضلا عن خصوصيته.","en":"If it is said that one specific kind may have different explanatory grounds, we reply that the issue is what vision has as its object: one may see something without perceiving that it is a substance or an accident, much less its specific nature.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-086.08","page":86,"ar":"وأما الوقوع فلقوله تعالى وجوه يومئذ ناضرة إلى ربها ناظرة ولم يعهد استعمال النظر إليه إلا في الرؤية.","en":"As for its actual occurrence, God says, “Faces on that day will be radiant, looking toward their Lord,” and “looking toward” in this construction is not ordinarily employed except for vision.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-086.09","page":86,"ar":"وحمل النظر على الانتظار وإلى على النعمة تعسف.","en":"Interpreting “looking” as waiting, and “toward” as referring to a blessing, is forced.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-086.10","page":86,"ar":"وقوله تعالى كلا إنهم عن ربهم يومئذ لمحجوبون وقوله تعالى للذين أحسنوا الحسنى وزيادة.","en":"Other evidence includes “No indeed! On that day they shall be veiled from their Lord,” and “For those who do good is the good reward, and an increase.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-087.01","page":87,"ar":"والصلاة والسلام إنكم سترون ربكم كما ترون هذا القمر ليلة البدر.","en":"And the Prophet, upon him be blessings and peace, said: “You will see your Lord as you see this full moon.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-087.02","page":87,"ar":"وقوله (فينظرون إلى وجه الله)، والمخالف يدعي اقتضاءها المقابلة ودورانها عند حصول الشرائط، وكلاهما ممنوع.","en":"Another proof speaks of looking toward the face of God. The opponent claims that vision requires spatial opposition and depends upon the usual conditions of sight; both assertions are denied.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-087.03","page":87,"ar":"والعمدة قوله تعالى لا تدركه الأبصار وهو يدرك الأبصار لظهور أن المنفي على عموم السلب.","en":"The central opposing text is “Eyes do not comprehend Him, but He comprehends eyes,” allegedly excluding every instance of sight.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-087.04","page":87,"ar":"ورد بمنع تسليم كون الإدراك هو الرؤية وأعم منها بأنه لا عموم في الأشخاص ولا الأوقات.","en":"The reply denies that “comprehending” is synonymous with seeing; even if it encompasses vision, the negation does not necessarily extend to all persons and all times.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-087.05","page":87,"ar":"وأما قوله تعالى لن تراني فليس للتأبيد ولا عموم الأوقات.","en":"As for “You shall not see Me,” the particle does not itself imply exclusion forever or across all times.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-087.06","page":87,"ar":"وأما استعظام سؤال الرؤية فلضعفهم.","en":"As for their regarding the request for vision as momentous, that was due to their weakness.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-087.07","page":87,"ar":"خاتمة: الحق أنه لا يعلم من الله تعالى إلا الوجود والصفات والسلوب والإضافات.","en":"Conclusion: The truth is that nothing is known of God Most High except [His] existence, attributes, negations, and relations.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-088.01","page":88,"ar":"فصل في أفعاله.","en":"Section: on divine acts.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-088.02","page":88,"ar":"موجد فعل العبد هو الله وإنما للعبد الكسب وهو أمر إضافي يجب من العبد ولا يوجب وجود المقدور بل اتصاف الفاعل به.","en":"God is the originator of the servant’s act; the servant has acquisition (kasb), which is a relational matter pertaining to the servant. It does not itself bring the possible act into existence but qualifies the agent through it.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-088.03","page":88,"ar":"وذلك كتعيين أحد الطرفين وترجيحه وصرف القدرة.","en":"That is, specifying one of the two alternatives, preferring it, and directing one’s power toward it.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-088.04","page":88,"ar":"وعند المعتزلة الموجد هو العبد وأطلقوا لفظ الخالق عليه ولزمهم كون كل حيوان خالقا.","en":"According to the Muʿtazila the servant brings the act into existence; they even apply “creator” to him, which would make every animal a creator.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-088.05","page":88,"ar":"وقد قال الله تعالى الله خالق كل شيء وخلق كل شيء وإنا كل شيء خلقناه بقدر والله خلقكم وما تعملون.","en":"God says, “God is Creator of everything”; “He created everything”; “We have created everything according to a measure”; and “God created you and what you do.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-088.06","page":88,"ar":"هو الله الخالق فعال لما يريد كل من عند الله كتب في قلوبهم الإيمان إنه هو أضحك وأبكى.","en":"Likewise, “He is God, the Creator”; “Doer of whatsoever He wills”; “All is from God”; “He inscribed faith upon their hearts”; and “He it is Who makes people laugh and weep.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-088.07","page":88,"ar":"وقد تواتر عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم ما يشعر بأن كل كائن بقدرة الله تعالى ومشيئته.","en":"Numerous prophetic reports convey that every occurrence is through God’s power and will.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-088.08","page":88,"ar":"ولو كان فعل العبد بقدرته لزم اجتماع المؤثرين لما ثبت من شمول قدرة الله تعالى وكان عالما بتفاصيله.","en":"Were the servant’s action produced by his own power [as an independent efficient cause], this would bring two efficient causes together, since God’s power encompasses every effect and He knows its details.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-088.09","page":88,"ar":"ولكان متمكنا من تركه مع ترجيح الفعل بمرجح لا يكون منه ويجب عنده الفعل مع أن معلوم الله تعالى هو وقوعه.","en":"He would supposedly be able to refrain while a determinant beyond him favors the act, yet the act must occur when its complete conditions obtain and God already knows that it occurs.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-088.10","page":88,"ar":"وقد يستدل بأنه لو قدر على فعله لقدر على إعادته وعلى مثله وعلى خلق الأجسام ولكن فعله خلق الإيمان أحسن من فعل","en":"Another argument holds that if a servant could independently bring about an act he could reproduce it, produce one like it, or create bodies; yet the creation of faith would be better than the production of—[continued].","status":"STAGE63_SINGLE_1912_PRINT_TRANSLATION_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-089.01","page":89,"ar":"الباري خلق الشيطان وما صح سؤال الإعانة ولا الشكر عليه.","en":"—the Creator’s producing Satan; nor [under the hypothesis of the servant’s independent creation] would it be fitting to ask [God] for help with the act or to thank [Him] for it.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-089.02","page":89,"ar":"وأما المعتزلة فمنهم من ادعى الضرورة لأن كل أحد يفرق بين حركة سقوطه وصعوده ويجد لنفسه فإنه بحسب دواعيه وقصوده.","en":"Among the Muʿtazila, some claim the distinction is immediately evident: everyone distinguishes the motion of falling from that of rising, and finds within himself that [the latter] accords with his motives and intentions.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-089.03","page":89,"ar":"ويقطع بأن ما يبطله أو ينهى عنه أو يتمناه أو يتعجب منه إنما هو فعل فاعله.","en":"He is convinced that what he annuls, prohibits, desires, or finds astonishing is genuinely the action of its agent.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-089.04","page":89,"ar":"والجواب أن ذلك لا يفيد كونه خالقه وقدرته وإيجاده بل هو متعلق قدرته وإرادته واقعا على وفق قصده ودواعيه.","en":"The reply is that this does not show the servant to be its efficient creator; the act is related to the servant’s power and will and occurs in keeping with his intention and motives.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-089.05","page":89,"ar":"ومنهم من احتج عقلا بأنه لولا استقلال العبد لبطل المدح والذم والأمر والنهي والثواب والعقاب وفوائد الوعد والوعيد ونحو ذلك.","en":"Others argue that, unless the servant acted independently, praise and blame, commands and prohibitions, reward and punishment, and the purposes of promise and threat would be void.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-089.06","page":89,"ar":"وبأن من أفعال العبد قبائح لا يجوز أن يخلقها الحكيم كالظلم والشر وسائر المعاصي.","en":"They also contend that some human acts are evil—such as injustice, wrongdoing and sins—which the Wise One could not create.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-089.07","page":89,"ar":"وبأنه يوجب اتصاف الباري بما لا ينبغي كالكافر والظالم والآكل والقاعد وغير ذلك.","en":"They further argue that the position would attribute to the Creator descriptions unbefitting Him, such as “unbeliever,” “wrongdoer,” “eater” or “sitter.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-089.08","page":89,"ar":"ورد بأن الكسب وتعلق القدرة والإرادة كاف ولا نزاع في الوجوب أو الامتناع بناء على أن المرجح الموجب أو المانع هو العلم الأزلي.","en":"The response is that acquisition and the related exercise of power and will suffice; the necessity or impossibility following from the complete determinant need not abolish responsibility, even when that determinant is considered in relation to eternal knowledge.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-089.09","page":89,"ar":"وبأن القبيح فعل القبيح لا خلقه، ألا ترى أنه تعالى خلق أصل جميع القبائح وهو الشيطان.","en":"Producing evil acts is not itself the evil act in the same sense as performing them; consider that God creates the devil, the source of many evils.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-089.10","page":89,"ar":"وبأن الفاعل من قام به الفعل لا من أوجده في محل آخر.","en":"The doer of an act is the one in whom the act occurs, not necessarily the one who brings it into being in another subject.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-089.11","page":89,"ar":"وسمعا بالآيات الواردة في إسناد","en":"As scriptural evidence, [they invoke] the verses attributing—[continued on p. 90].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-090.01","page":90,"ar":"الأفعال إلى العباد سيما ما ينبئ عن الإيجاد مثل (من عمل صالحا) (وما تفعلوا من خير) (فتبارك الله أحسن الخالقين).","en":"—actions to human beings, especially language suggesting production, such as “Whoever works righteousness,” “Whatever good you do,” and “Blessed be God, the best of creators.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-090.02","page":90,"ar":"وفي أنه لا يمنع من الإيمان والطاعة ولا إلجاء إلى الكفر والمعصية وما منع الناس أن يؤمنوا كيف تكفرون.","en":"They also cite passages that God does not prevent faith and obedience, nor force people into disbelief and disobedience, such as “What prevented the people from believing?” and “How can you disbelieve?”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-090.03","page":90,"ar":"ودلالة على تعليق أفعال العباد بمشيئتهم اعملوا ما شئتم فمن شاء فليؤمن.","en":"Other texts connect human acts to human choice: “Act as you will” and “Let whoever wishes believe.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-090.04","page":90,"ar":"والجواب أن بعضها غير متنازع وبعضها مؤول جمعا بين الأدلة ومشيئته ليست إلا بمشيئة الله تعالى وما تشاؤون إلا أن يشاء الله.","en":"The response is that some texts are not in dispute; others are interpreted in light of the whole body of evidence. Human willing occurs only within divine willing: “You do not will unless God wills.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-090.05","page":90,"ar":"والحق أنه لا جبر ولا تفويض لكن أمر بين الأمرين لأن المبادئ القريبة على الاختيار والبعيدة الاضطرار فالإنسان مضطر في صورة مختار أفعاله بقضاء.","en":"The adopted position rejects both compulsion and absolute delegation: immediate principles of action involve choice, while remote principles involve necessity; thus a human acts in the form of voluntary choice while still dependent upon divine determination.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-090.06","page":90,"ar":"الله تعالى وقدره بمعنى خلقه وتقديره ابتداء أو بواسطة موجب والرضا إنما يجب بالقضاء لا بالمقضي، وعند المعتزلة لا يصح إلا بمعنى الإعلام والتبيين أو الكتابة في اللوح أو الإلزام في الواجبات.","en":"God’s decree and determination mean His creating and measuring, immediately or through intermediaries. Acceptance is due to the decree as divine act, not to every thing decreed. For the Muʿtazilites, the expression is admissible only in the senses of making known or clarifying, recording upon the Tablet, or imposing duties.","status":"STAGE63_1912_PRINT_TRANSLATION_DIRECTLY_CHECKED"},{"id":"KAL-090.07","page":90,"ar":"ثم لا خلاف في ذم القدرية وسموا بذلك لفرط اشتغالهم بنفي القدر وما قالوا إن المثبت أولى بأن ينسب إليه مردود.","en":"There is no dispute, he says, over criticism of the Qadariyya, so named because of their zeal in rejecting predestination; the suggestion that the affirmers of predestination deserve that label more is rejected.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-090.08","page":90,"ar":"لقوله عليه السلام القدرية مجوس هذه الأمة. وقوله صلى الله عليه وسلم: «إذا قامت القيامة","en":"He cites the report, “The Qadariyya are the Magians of this community,” and another prophetic report beginning, “When the Resurrection comes ...” [continued on p. 91].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-091.01","page":91,"ar":"نادى مناد أن خصماء الله يوم القيامة القدرية ولأن من يضيف القدر إلى نفسه أولى بالتسمية.","en":"“... a herald proclaims: ‘God’s adversaries on the Day of Resurrection are the Qadariyya.’” He adds that those who attribute determination to themselves more properly deserve the name.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-091.02","page":91,"ar":"ثم النصوص الشاهدة بأن الكل بمشيئة الله أكثر من أن تحصى حتى صار بمنزلة المثل «ما شاء الله كان وما لم يشأ لم يكن» كيف لا وقد ثبت أنه خالق للكل ومريده.","en":"Texts establishing that everything occurs by God’s will are too numerous to count, to the point that the saying “What God wills comes to pass, and what He does not will does not” has become proverbial. How could it be otherwise when He is the creator and willer of everything?","status":"STAGE64_WITNESS_OR_SEMANTIC_RECHECK_REQUIRED"},{"id":"KAL-091.03","page":91,"ar":"وعالم بعدم وقوع ما لم يقع فكيف يريده.","en":"Since God knows that what does not occur will not occur, how could He will it? This is the reported objection that motivates the following discussion.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-091.04","page":91,"ar":"والمعتزلة زعموا بأنه لا يريد القبائح بل أضدادها وإن لم تقع فجعلوا أكثر ما يقع في ملكه خلاف مراده.","en":"The Muʿtazila maintain that God does not will wicked acts but their opposites, even if these do not occur; this implies that much occurring within His dominion runs contrary to His will.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-091.05","page":91,"ar":"تمسكا بأن إرادة القبيح قبيحة وأن العقاب على ما يريده ظلم وأن الأمر بما لا يراد والنهي عما يراد سفه وأن الإرادة تستلزم الأمر والرضا والمحبة والكل فاسد.","en":"They argue that willing evil is itself evil, that punishing what God wills would be unjust, that commanding what is not willed and forbidding what is willed would be futile, and that willing something entails commanding, approving, and loving it. The author rejects each inference.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-091.06","page":91,"ar":"وأما الرد على الذين قالوا ولو شاء الله ما أشركنا فلقصدهم الاستهزاء أو جعلهم ذلك عذرا لهم ولذلك جعلوا مكذبين لا كاذبين.","en":"As for the divine response to those who say, “If God had wished, we would not have associated partners,” it rebukes their mockery or their use of predestination as an excuse, not simply the statement of divine omnipotence.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-092.01","page":92,"ar":"وحكم بأنه لو شاء لهداكم أجمعين أما قوله تعالى كل ذلك كان سيئه عند ربك مكروها أي مكروه من الناس وفي مجاري العادات.","en":"He also says, “Had He willed, He would have guided you all.” As to the verse “The evil of all that is hateful before your Lord,” the objectionable act is described as disliked by people and in ordinary customary judgments.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-092.02","page":92,"ar":"فصل.","en":"Section.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-092.03","page":92,"ar":"الحسن والقبح بمعنى استحقاق المدح والذم والثواب والعقاب في حكم الله تعالى بالشرع.","en":"Goodness and badness, in the sense of deserving praise and blame, reward and punishment, are determined in God’s judgment by revelation.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-092.04","page":92,"ar":"لقوله تعالى وما كنا معذبين حتى نبعث رسولا ولأنه لو كان لذات الفعل لما تخلف عنه ولأن العبد لا يستقل بفعله.","en":"He cites “We do not punish until We send a messenger”; were moral liability intrinsic to an act it would never be absent from that act, and the servant does not independently produce the act.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-092.05","page":92,"ar":"والمدح والذم عقلا ليس إلا مع الاستقلال.","en":"Rationally assigning ultimate praise and blame would require the independent production of an act, which he denies.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-092.06","page":92,"ar":"وقالت المعتزلة بل بالعقل لأن حسن الإحسان وقبح العدوان ضروريان.","en":"The Muʿtazila hold instead that reason determines goodness and badness, because the goodness of beneficence and evil of aggression are self-evident.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-092.07","page":92,"ar":"ولأن العقل عند التساوي يؤثر الصدق وإنقاذ الغريق على الكذب وإهلاكه وأنه لو لم يقبح إظهار المعجزة على يد الكاذب لم تثبت النبوة.","en":"They argue that, other conditions equal, reason prefers truthfulness and rescuing a drowning person to lying and causing his death; if granting miracles to a liar were not wrong, prophecy could not be established.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-092.08","page":92,"ar":"والجواب عن الأولين المنع بالمعنى المتنازع وعن التساوي بالحقيقة وعن الثالث أن عدم الوقوع من القطعيات العادية.","en":"The response denies that the first two intuitions prove moral value in the precise disputed sense, and explains the third by appeal to the established regularity of divine custom rather than an independent obligation imposed upon God.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-092.09","page":92,"ar":"وقد تمسكت المعتزلة بأن من عرف الله تعالى بذاته وصفاته ثم أشرك به ونسب كل نقص إليه علم قطعا أنه في معرض العقاب.","en":"The Muʿtazila further argue that someone who knows God and His attributes, then associates partners with Him and ascribes imperfections to Him, certainly knows himself to deserve punishment.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-092.10","page":92,"ar":"قلنا ما لم يعلم ذلك من تقرير الشرع وبأنه لو كان بالشرع لزم إفهام الأنبياء.","en":"We deny that this is known categorically unless it is learned from the establishment of revealed law. The subsequent objection—that, if it rested on law, instruction by the prophets would be required—continues onto p. 93, where its answer is said to have preceded.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-093.01","page":93,"ar":"الأنبياء وقد مر جوابه.","en":"—the prophets; its answer was given earlier.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-093.02","page":93,"ar":"فصل.","en":"Section.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-093.03","page":93,"ar":"لا خلاف في عدم التكليف بما يمتنع لذاته كجمع النقيضين ولا في وقوع التكليف بما يمتنع لسبق علم أو إخبار بأنه لا يقع.","en":"There is no disagreement about the impossibility of obliging something intrinsically impossible, such as combining contradictories; nor about commands concerning things known or foretold not to occur.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-093.04","page":93,"ar":"وإنما الخلاف فيما أمكن ولم يقع متعلقا لقدرة العبد أصلا كخلق الجسم أو عادة كالصعود إلى السماء.","en":"The dispute concerns what is possible in itself but not within the servant’s power at all—such as creating a body (outside the servant’s power altogether) or ascending to heaven (impossible under ordinary conditions).","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-093.05","page":93,"ar":"فعندنا يجوز لعدم القبح العقلي لكنه لا يقع لقوله تعالى لا يكلف الله نفسا إلا وسعها.","en":"On our view such obligation is conceptually permissible, since reason does not independently determine its evil; but it does not actually occur, because God says, “God does not burden a soul beyond its capacity.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-093.06","page":93,"ar":"وعند المعتزلة والشيعة لا يجوز لكونه سفها وعبثا.","en":"According to Muʿtazilites and Shiʿites it is impermissible, being foolish and pointless.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-093.07","page":93,"ar":"ومن ذهب إلى أن تكليف أبي لهب بأن يصدق بجميع ما جاء به النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم ومن جملته أنه لا يصدقه أصلا تكليف بجمع النقيضين.","en":"One argument says that commanding Abū Lahab to believe everything the Prophet brought—including the report that he would never believe—would require affirming contradictories.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-093.08","page":93,"ar":"وأجيب بأنه إنما كلف بتحصيل الإيمان وهو أمر ممكن في نفسه يمتنع لسابق علم أو إخبار بأنه لا يؤمن.","en":"The response distinguishes the command to attain faith, an intrinsically possible object, from the divine foreknowledge or report that it will not in fact occur.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-093.09","page":93,"ar":"فصل.","en":"Section.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-093.10","page":93,"ar":"الحق أن تعليل بعض أفعاله بالأغراض ثابت بالنص والإجماع وعليه مبنى القياس.","en":"The correct view is that some divine acts are explained by purposes, as Scripture and consensus attest and as analogical reasoning presupposes.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-093.11","page":93,"ar":"فالأقرب حمل الخلاف على عدم لزوم ذلك أو عمومه كما يشهد به استدلالهم بأنه لا بد من","en":"The controversy is best understood as concerning whether purposiveness is universally necessary, not whether purposes are ever mentioned; the argument requires an eventual termination in an act that is not performed for a further purpose, as explained on p. 94.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-094.01","page":94,"ar":"الانتهاء إلى ما لا يكون لغرض قطعا للتسلسل وأنه لا يعقل في تخليد الكفار نفع لأحد.","en":"—to some act not performed for any further end, lest an infinite regress result; they add that no benefit to anyone is apparent in the perpetual punishment of unbelievers.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-094.02","page":94,"ar":"ذهبت المعتزلة إلى أن الغرض من التكليف التعرض للثواب بدليل قوله تعالى ومن يطع الله ورسوله يدخله جنات.","en":"The Muʿtazila hold that the purpose of imposing obligations is to allow someone to earn reward, citing “Whoever obeys God and His Messenger, He shall admit him into gardens.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-094.03","page":94,"ar":"ولأن الإضرار بدون استحقاق ولا منفعة ظلم فيكون التعرض للمنفعة هي الجهة الحسنة للتكليف.","en":"They argue that causing injury without desert or benefit is injustice, so making reward attainable is what justifies obligation.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-094.04","page":94,"ar":"ورد بأن الترغيب قد يكون فضلا من الله تعالى وبأنه المالك فلا ظلم منه أصلا.","en":"The reply is that encouragement may be purely God’s generosity, and that, as absolute owner, He commits no injustice in the sense claimed.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-094.05","page":94,"ar":"ولو سلم لزوم الغرض فيجوز أن يكون هو الابتلاء أو الشكر أو حفظ النظام أو غير ذلك.","en":"Even if divine action required purposes, these could include testing, gratitude, the preservation of order, or other ends.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-094.06","page":94,"ar":"وبالجملة لا يعقل استحقاق النعيم الدائم بمجرد كلفة والعذاب الدائم بشرب جرعة خمر.","en":"In brief, a limited effort cannot by itself establish desert of everlasting felicity, nor could a single draught of wine by itself establish desert of perpetual punishment.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-094.07","page":94,"ar":"فصل.","en":"Section.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-094.08","page":94,"ar":"قد ورد في الكتاب والسنة نسبة الهداية والإضلال والطبع والختم على قلوب الكفرة إلى الله.","en":"Scripture and prophetic tradition attribute guidance, leading astray, sealing, and stamping unbelievers’ hearts to God.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-094.09","page":94,"ar":"فعندنا يعني خلق الهداية والضلال لأنه الخالق وحده.","en":"For us these expressions mean that He creates guidance and error, being the sole creator.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-094.10","page":94,"ar":"وعند المعتزلة الهداية الدلالة الموصلة إلى المنفعة أو البيان بنصب الأدلة والإضلال منع الألطاف للعلم بأنها لا تجدي أو الإسناد مجاز.","en":"For the Muʿtazila, guidance denotes an indication leading to benefit or an exposition by establishing proofs, for them, misguidance can mean the withholding of gracious assistance because God knows it would not prove effective; some such attributions are treated as figurative.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-094.11","page":94,"ar":"وأما اللطف والتوفيق والعصمة فعندنا خلق قدرة الطاعة والخذلان خلق قدرة","en":"As for divine gentleness, enabling success, and preservation from sin, our account relates them to the creation of the capacity for obedience, while forsaking relates to the creation of a capacity—[continued on p95].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-095.01","page":95,"ar":"المعصية وقيل العصمة أن لا يخلق الله في العبد الذنب وقيل خاصية يمتنع معها صدور الذنب.","en":"—sin. It has also been said that protection from sin (*ʿiṣma*) consists in God’s not creating sin in the servant; another account calls it a special characteristic with which the occurrence of sin becomes impossible.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-095.02","page":95,"ar":"وعند المعتزلة اللطف ما يختار المكلف عنده الطاعة أو يقرب منها مع تمكنه في الحالين.","en":"According to the Muʿtazila, gracious assistance (*luṭf*) is what leads a morally responsible person to choose obedience—or brings him closer to it—while retaining capacity in either case.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-095.03","page":95,"ar":"ويسميان المحصل والمقرب، والتوفيق اللطف المحصل للواجب، والخذلان منع اللطف، والعصمة اللطف المحصل لترك القبيح.","en":"The two kinds are called the securing kind (*al-muḥaṣṣil*) and the approximating kind (*al-muqarrib*). Divine enabling (*tawfīq*) is grace that secures performance of the required act; abandonment (*khidhlān*) is the withholding of grace; and protection from sin (*ʿiṣma*) is grace that secures abstention from the reprehensible act.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-095.04","page":95,"ar":"فصل.","en":"Section.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-095.05","page":95,"ar":"والأجل الوقت الذي علم الله بطلان حياة الحيوان فيه وهو واحد.","en":"An appointed term (*ajal*) is the time at which God knows an animal’s life will cease; for each it is one.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-095.06","page":95,"ar":"والمقتول ميت بأجله إلا أن موته مما خلقه الله عقب فعل العبد ووجوب الجزاء على القاتل لما اكتسبه من الفعل وارتكب من النهي.","en":"Someone killed dies at their appointed term. Nevertheless, that death is something God creates following the servant’s act; the killer incurs liability for what he has acquired by acting and for the prohibition he has transgressed.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-095.07","page":95,"ar":"ومعنى زيادة البر في العمر كثرة الخير للنصوص القاطعة على أنه لا يقدم ولا يتأخر عن الأجل.","en":"The “increase of lifespan” through righteousness is interpreted as an increase in blessedness or goodness, in keeping with decisive texts that the appointed term is neither advanced nor postponed.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-095.08","page":95,"ar":"فصل.","en":"Section.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-095.09","page":95,"ar":"الرزق ما ساقه الله تعالى إلى الحيوان فانتفع به وكل يستوفي رزقه، ولا يأكل أحد رزق غيره وقيل لينتفع به.","en":"Provision (*rizq*) is what God conveys to a living being so that it benefits from it. Each receives its provision, and no one eats another’s provision; another formulation defines it by what is meant to benefit the recipient.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-095.10","page":95,"ar":"وقد يخص بالمأكول، وقيده المعتزلة بأن لا يكون لأحد منعه، فيخرج الحرام، فلا يكون من رُزق في جميع عمره بالحرام ...","en":"Provision may be restricted to what is eaten. The Muʿtazila stipulate that no one may have the right to prevent the recipient from taking it, thereby excluding illicit consumption. On this definition, someone supported throughout life solely by illicit food or earnings would not count as being provided for—[completed on p. 96].","status":"STAGE64_WITNESS_OR_SEMANTIC_RECHECK_REQUIRED"},{"id":"KAL-096.01","page":96,"ar":"مرزوقا وقد دلت النصوص على ضمانه الأرزاق.","en":"—as a person receiving provision at all. Yet revealed texts establish God’s guarantee of provisions.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-096.02","page":96,"ar":"خاتمة: التسعير تقدير ما يباع به الشيء ويكون غلاء ورخصا بأسباب من الله تعالى فالمسعر هو الله وحده.","en":"Conclusion: price regulation is fixing the price at which goods are sold; prices rise and fall through causes ultimately from God, so He alone is the true determiner of prices.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-096.03","page":96,"ar":"فصل.","en":"Section.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-096.04","page":96,"ar":"المعتزلة أوجبوا على الله تعالى أمورا، وأكثروا في معنى الوجوب فيها اللطف، لأن منعه نقض للغرض وتقريب أو تحصيل للمعصية، ولأن الواجب لا يتم إلا به، فوجب أن لا يبقى كافر ولا فاسق وأن لا يخلو عصر من الأنبياء والأولياء.","en":"The Muʿtazila impose various obligations upon God, especially divine assistance, arguing that withholding it would thwart divine purposes and facilitate wrongdoing, and that what is indispensable to an obligation must also be obligatory. They thereby face hard cases of continued unbelief and sin and the consequence that no age should be devoid of prophets and saints.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-096.05","page":96,"ar":"والعوض في مقابلة الألم ونحوه لأن تركه ظلم.","en":"They also affirm compensatory reward for suffering, holding that to omit it would be unjust.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-096.06","page":96,"ar":"واختلفوا في الوجوب كونه في الآخرة وفي حبوطه بالذنوب وفي أن أعواض الكفار والفساق وغير العاقل تكون في الدنيا أو في الآخرة وأن البهائم تدخل الجنة وتخلق فيها الدود ومنها الأصلح للعباد في الدين وقيل في الدنيا.","en":"They differ over whether compensation is due in the hereafter, whether it is forfeited through sins, whether compensation for unbelievers, wrongdoers and nonrational beings occurs here or there, and whether animals enter Paradise; related disputes concern what is best for people in religion or worldly affairs.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-096.07","page":96,"ar":"ولا خلاف في الإقدار والتمكين لأن تركه بخل وسفه. قلنا فيلزم أن لا يخلق الكافر الفقير، وأن لا يخلده في النار، ولا يميت المحسن، ولا يبقي المسيء سليما، إبليس وذرياته.","en":"They do not disagree regarding the provision of capacity and enablement, maintaining that withholding them would be miserliness or folly. We reply that, by such reasoning, God would have to refrain from creating a destitute unbeliever or keeping him in the Fire, and would neither put a virtuous person to death nor leave a wicked one unharmed—consider Iblīs and his descendants.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-096.08","page":96,"ar":"فصل.","en":"Section.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-096.09","page":96,"ar":"تغاير الاسم والمسمى والتسمية ضروري والقول بأن","en":"The distinction among a name, the thing named, and the act of naming is evident. The claim that—[continued].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-097.01","page":97,"ar":"الاسم نفس المسمى والتسمية غيرهما أريد بالاسم المدلول والتمسك بقوله تعالى سبح اسم ربك الأعلى وقوله تعالى ولله الأسماء الحسنى ليس محل النزاع.","en":"—the name is identical with the named, while naming differs from both, uses “name” for what it signifies. Appeals to “Glorify the name of your Lord Most High” or “To God belong the beautiful names” do not settle the dispute.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-097.02","page":97,"ar":"ومبنى الخلاف أن الاسم إذا أطلق فالمراد به المسمى كأن زيد كاتب أو نفس اللفظ كأزيد مكتوب.","en":"The disagreement turns on whether “name,” when used, refers to its object—as in “Zayd is a writer”—or to the uttered expression—as in “Zayd” is written.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-097.03","page":97,"ar":"وإذا اتصف الباري بمعنى ولم يرد به إذن ولم يمنع ولا عرف إطلاقه وكان مشعرا بالجلال فهل يجوز إطلاقه عليه تعالى فمنعه الجمهور ولم يجز مثل العارف والفطن لتوهم الإخلال ولا مثل الحارث والزارع لعدم الإجلال.","en":"If a predicate correctly describes God but is neither expressly authorized nor prohibited, whether it may be used as a divine name is disputed. Most refuse expressions such as “clever” or “shrewd,” which suggest deficiency, and “farmer” or “sower,” which fail to express proper majesty.","status":"STAGE64_WITNESS_OR_SEMANTIC_RECHECK_REQUIRED"},{"id":"KAL-097.04","page":97,"ar":"ولا خلاف في كثرة أسماء الله تعالى باعتبار الصفات والأفعال والسلب والإضافات ولا في امتناع ما يكون باعتبار الجزء.","en":"No one disputes the multiplicity of divine names considered by reference to attributes, acts, negations and relations, nor the inadmissibility of names based on a constituent part [of the divine essence].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-097.05","page":97,"ar":"والحق ثبوت ما هو باعتبار نفس الذات وهو لفظ الله وإن كان الإله اسما للمعبود ولا تنحصر أسماؤه في تسعة وتسعين.","en":"The correct view also affirms a name referring to the essence itself—“Allah”—even though “deity” denotes one worthy of worship. His names are not limited to ninety-nine.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-097.06","page":97,"ar":"الباب السادس في السمعيات وفيه فصول.","en":"Chapter Six: revealed matters, comprising sections.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-097.07","page":97,"ar":"الفصل الأول: النبي إنسان بعثه الله لتبليغ ما أوحي إليه، وكذا الرسول وقد يخص الرسول بمن له شريعة وكتاب.","en":"First section: a prophet is a human whom God sends to convey what He reveals. A messenger is sometimes defined in the same way, though “messenger” is also restricted to one bringing a law and scripture.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-097.08","page":97,"ar":"ثم البعثة لطف من الله تعالى وفضل يتضمن مصالح كإفاضة العقل ومعاونته ورفع الإشكال وبيان المبهم.","en":"Sending prophets is graciousness and favor from God, embodying benefits such as enriching reason, assisting it, removing perplexities and clarifying what is obscure.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-098.01","page":98,"ar":"ويعرفها المبعوث بنصب الأدلة أو العلم الضروري ولأن منافع التكليف أكثر من مضاره وإن خفيت تفاصيل البعض عن البعض كآيات الصلاة والحج نحوها.","en":"The one sent is recognized by signs or through evident knowledge; the benefits of religious duties outweigh their costs even when their detailed significance is hidden, as with prayer and pilgrimage.","status":"STAGE64_WITNESS_OR_SEMANTIC_RECHECK_REQUIRED"},{"id":"KAL-098.02","page":98,"ar":"وطريق ثبوتها المعجزة وهي أمر خارق للعادة مقرون بالتحدي مع عدم المعارضة.","en":"The proof of prophecy is the miracle: an event contrary to customary order, accompanied by a challenge, without successful counterperformance.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-098.03","page":98,"ar":"ووجه دلالتها أنها بمنزلة صريح التصديق من يقول الدليل على أني رسول هذا الملك أن يقوم عن سريره ثلاثا ففعل فإنه يحصل به العلم الضروري.","en":"Its evidential force is comparable to explicit confirmation: if someone claims to be the king’s messenger and says the proof is the king’s rising three times from his throne, and the king does so, certainty results.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-098.04","page":98,"ar":"ولا يقدح فيه احتمال أن يكون ذلك لخاصية فيه أو اطلاع منه على خاصية في بعض الأجسام أو وضع فلكي أو يكون من ملك أو جن أو ابتداء عادة أو متروك المعارضة أو المانع أولا لغرض التصديق بل إجابة للدعوة أو معجزة لنبي آخر.","en":"Far-fetched possibilities—that the phenomenon has a hidden property, an astronomical cause, angelic or jinn mediation, an unfamiliar regularity, a challenge left unanswered, or an answer to prayer rather than confirmation—do not by themselves defeat its evidential force.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-098.05","page":98,"ar":"فإن الاحتمالات العقلية لا تنافي العلوم القطعية العادية على أن الكلام فيما ثبت العجز عن معارضته مع فرط الاهتمام وأنه شيء لا مؤثر فيه إلا الله.","en":"Such abstract possibilities do not displace ordinary certainty; the argument concerns an event whose resistance to counterperformance has been established despite intense incentive, and whose producing agent is none but God.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-098.06","page":98,"ar":"وأن حصول التصديق لا يتوقف على كونه غرضا ولا كون الباعث صادقا في إخباره ليدور بناء على أنه سمعي.","en":"The evidential inference does not depend upon divine confirmation being conceived as an aim, nor on assuming at the outset the speaker’s reliability through the revelation being proved.","status":"STAGE64_WITNESS_OR_SEMANTIC_RECHECK_REQUIRED"},{"id":"KAL-098.07","page":98,"ar":"فصل.","en":"Section.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-098.08","page":98,"ar":"محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم رسول الله لأنه ادعى الرسالة","en":"Muḥammad, blessings and peace upon him, is God’s messenger because he claimed the mission—[continued].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-099.01","page":99,"ar":"وأظهر المعجزة لأنه أتى بالقرآن المعجز لفصاحته بلغة العرب مع كثرتهم وشهرتهم بالعصبية ولم يطعنوا فيه مع حذاقتهم وعداوتهم بل نسبوه لكمال حسنه وبلاغته إلى السحر.","en":"—and presented a miracle: the inimitable Qurʾān in the Arabs’ own language, despite the great number of skilled and competitive Arabic speakers hostile to him; they could not refute its eloquence but sometimes attributed its power to magic.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-099.02","page":99,"ar":"فالطعن مدفوعه إجمالا والتفصيل في المقاصد وتعجيزهم كان من فصاحته لا لعدم تأتّي المعارضة مع سهولتها.","en":"The objections are answered in outline here, with fuller details elsewhere; the Arabs’ inability was attributed to its eloquence, not merely to divinely preventing an otherwise easy imitation.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-099.03","page":99,"ar":"فبطل القول بالصرفة، على أن نقصان البلاغة أدخل في الصرفة، ولأنه أخبر عن المغيبات كقصص موسى وعيسى وقوله تعالى «وعدكم الله مغانم كثيرة تأخذونها»، «الم غلبت الروم»، «سيهزم الجمع»، «لتدخلن المسجد الحرام»، «ليظهره على الدين كله»، «لا يأتون بمثله».","en":"This defeats the doctrine of ṣarfa, the claim that rivals were diverted from challenging the Qurʾān; even a reduction in rhetorical skill would be a stronger example of such diversion. Moreover, the Qurʾān reports unseen events, including narratives of Moses and Jesus and scriptural predictions of spoils, Roman fortunes, military defeat, entry into the sacred mosque and religious ascendancy. Its opponents do not produce its like.","status":"STAGE64_WITNESS_OR_SEMANTIC_RECHECK_REQUIRED"},{"id":"KAL-099.04","page":99,"ar":"ولأنه ظهرت منه أمور خارجة عن العادة كولادته مختونا مسرورا مع خاتم النبوة، وكونه مبصرا من خلفه كما كان مبصرا من قدامه.","en":"Other extraordinary events are reported of him: birth already circumcised, the seal of prophecy, and perceiving from behind as from in front.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-099.05","page":99,"ar":"وكونه غاية في صفات الكمال ومستجاب الدعوة، وخرور الأوثان، وسقوط شرف قصور الأكاسرة، وإظلال السحاب عليه، وانشقاق القمر، واقتلاع الشجر، وتسليم الحجر، وحنين الجذع.","en":"Reports also recount his consummate qualities, answered supplications, the falling of idols and of the battlements of Persian palaces, a cloud shading him, the splitting of the moon, a tree being uprooted, stones greeting him and the yearning of the palm trunk.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-099.06","page":99,"ar":"وشكاية الناقة وشهادة المشوية وتسبيح الحصى وغير ذلك.","en":"There are also stories of a camel complaining, cooked meat testifying, pebbles praising God, and other signs.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-099.07","page":99,"ar":"ومن الشواهد نصوص التوراة والإنجيل والزبور ومن","en":"Among the proofs adduced are passages of the Torah, Gospel and Psalms, and—[continued].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-100.01","page":100,"ar":"الإقناعات لأهل الإنصاف ما اجتمع فيه من الكمالات وما اشتملت عليه شريعته في كل باب وظهورها على سائر الأديان مع قلة الأعوان وكثرة الأعداء.","en":"Among persuasive proofs for fair-minded people are the many perfections combined in him, the comprehensive excellence of his law, and its ascendancy despite few supporters and many enemies.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-100.02","page":100,"ar":"وغاية متشبث المنكرين الطعن في النسخ مطلقا، وقد بين ذلك في موضعه، و[قراءة مقدمة الاستشهاد غير محررة] «تمسكوا بالسبت أبدا» و«هذه شريعة مؤبدة ما دامت السماوات والأرض».","en":"The chief resort of the deniers is to challenge abrogation altogether, a question treated elsewhere. They cite expressions attributed to Mosaic law, including “Keep the Sabbath forever” and “This law is perpetual as long as heaven and earth endure.” [The precise introduction to the citations requires an independent textual witness.]","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-100.03","page":100,"ar":"والجواب أن هذا افتراء أو عبارة عن طول الزمان ثم النص يدل على أنه مبعوث إلى الناس كافة وأنه لا نبي بعده ولا تنسخ شريعته وأنه أفضل الأنبياء وأمته خير الأمم.","en":"The response is that the disputed expressions either lack their alleged force or refer to a long duration. Texts establish that Muḥammad was sent to all people, that no prophet follows him, that his law is not abrogated, that he is the greatest of prophets and his community a leading community.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-100.04","page":100,"ar":"واختلفوا في الأفضل بعده فقيل آدم وقيل إبراهيم وقيل موسى وقيل عيسى.","en":"They differ over who is highest after him: Adam, Abraham, Moses, or Jesus are each named.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-100.05","page":100,"ar":"ودل الكتاب على معراجه إلى المسجد الأقصى وإجماع القرن الثاني على أنه في اليقظة وبالجسد ودل الخبر المستفيض على أنه إلى السماء وخبر الواحد إلى الجنة أو العرش أو طرف العالم.","en":"The Book indicates his night journey to al-Masjid al-Aqṣā. A reported consensus of the second century supports that it happened awake and bodily. Widely transmitted reports indicate the ascent to heaven, while solitary reports extend it to Paradise, the Throne, or the extremity of the world.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-100.06","page":100,"ar":"فصل.","en":"Section.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-100.07","page":100,"ar":"من شرائط النبوة الذكورة وكمال العقل وقوة الرأي والسلامة عما تنفر عنه الطباع السليمة أو يخل بالمروءة أو حكمة البعثة.","en":"Among the qualifications of prophecy are being male, sound reason, strong judgment and freedom from characteristics that repel sound natures or impair dignity or the purpose of sending a messenger.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-100.08","page":100,"ar":"ثم المختار أن الأنبياء معصومون عما ينافي","en":"The adopted position is that prophets are protected from what would be inconsistent with—[continued].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-101.01","page":101,"ar":"مقتضى المعجزة كالكذب في التبليغ وعن الكفر وتعمد الكبائر سمعا عندنا وعقلا عند المعتزلة وعن الصغائر المنفرة وتعمد غير المنفرة وعن سهو الكبيرة أيضا لئلا يلزم ما هو منتف قطعاً كحرمة اتباعهم ورد شهاداتهم ووجوب زجرهم واستحقاقهم العذاب والذم وعدم قبولهم عنه النبوة.","en":"—the evidential import of miracles: lying in transmitting revelation, unbelief, deliberate major sins, and repellent minor sins. The author grounds these exclusions in transmitted proof, while Muʿtazilites appeal to reason. The discussion turns on the scandal of rejecting their testimony, forbidding their example, or judging them deserving punishment.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-101.02","page":101,"ar":"ونحو ذلك وما نقل من ذنبهم وتوبتهم فما صح منه فعلى السهو أو ترك الأولى أو قبل البعثة.","en":"Reports of prophetic faults and repentance are interpreted as involving inadvertence, the abandonment of a better course, or events prior to the prophetic mission.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-101.03","page":101,"ar":"والأولى أن لا يحصر عددهم وإن ورد في الحديث أن عدد الأنبياء مئة ألف وأربعة وعشرون ألفا وعدد الرسل ثلاثمائة وثلاثة عشر أخذا من قوله تعالى منهم من قصصنا عليك ومنهم من لم نقصص.","en":"It is preferable not to restrict the number of prophets, even though reports mention 124,000 prophets and 313 messengers, in view of the verse that some messengers are recounted and others not.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-101.04","page":101,"ar":"والجمهور على عصمة الملائكة لقوله تعالى وهم لا يستكبرون يخافون ربهم من فوقهم ويفعلون ما يؤمرون ويسبحون الليل والنهار لا يفترون.","en":"Most scholars affirm angelic protection from sin, citing verses that they do not act arrogantly, fear their Lord, do as commanded, and tirelessly glorify God.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-101.05","page":101,"ar":"واحتج المخالف بقصة إبليس مع كونه من الملائكة وغيبتهم في حق آدم واستبعادهم جعله خليفة.","en":"The objector appeals to Iblīs supposedly being among the angels, to what is taken to be their backbiting of Adam, and to their disapproval of his being made vicegerent.","status":"STAGE64_WITNESS_OR_SEMANTIC_RECHECK_REQUIRED"},{"id":"KAL-101.06","page":101,"ar":"ورد بأن إبليس من الجن وعده من الملائكة تغليب وبأن الاغتياب إنما يكون لغرض إظهار نقص الغير بل قصدهم التعجب والاستفسار عن حكمة استخلاف من لا يليق مع وجود اللائق.","en":"The reply is that Iblīs is among the jinn, though included with the angels by predominance of designation; and backbiting consists in seeking to expose another’s deficiency, whereas the angels intended wonder and inquiry about the wisdom of appointing someone apparently less suitable when someone suitable exists.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-102.01","page":102,"ar":"وجود الأليق وأما تعذيب هاروت وماروت فحكاية ولم يكن منهما عمل بالسحر ولا اعتقاد لتأثيره بل تعليم مع تنبيه.","en":"As for the report of the punishment of Hārūt and Mārūt, it is a narrated account; the author nevertheless distinguishes it from their practicing sorcery or believing it independently efficacious, describing the matter as teaching with a warning.","status":"STAGE64_WITNESS_OR_SEMANTIC_RECHECK_REQUIRED"},{"id":"KAL-102.02","page":102,"ar":"ثم جمهور أصحابنا والشيعة على أن الأنبياء أفضل من الملائكة وبالغ بعضهم حتى فضل خواص البشر على خواص الملائكة وعوامهم على عوامهم.","en":"Most of our school, together with the Shiʿa, hold that prophets are superior to angels; some extend this to the elect of humanity over the elect of angels, and ordinary human beings over ordinary angels.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-102.03","page":102,"ar":"أما عقلا فلأن اكتساب الكمال والمواظبة على الطاعات مع الشواغل أدخل في استحقاق الثواب.","en":"One rational argument is that achieving perfection and persevering in obedience despite distracting temptations makes one more deserving of reward.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-102.04","page":102,"ar":"وأما سمعا فلقوله تعالى إن الله اصطفى آدم ونوحا وآل إبراهيم وآل عمران على العالمين.","en":"Scriptural evidence includes “God chose Adam, Noah, the family of Abraham, and the family of ʿImrān above all the worlds.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-102.05","page":102,"ar":"ومن جملتهم الملائكة ولأنه تعالى أمرهم بالسجود لآدم تعظيما وتكرمة وأمر آدم بتعليمهم الأسماء وقصدا إلى إظهار الفضل.","en":"The angels are among the beings included in that “all worlds”; furthermore, God commanded them to prostrate before Adam in honor and ennoblement, and commanded Adam to teach them the names, intending thereby to make his superiority manifest.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-102.06","page":102,"ar":"واحتج المخالف بأنها متصفة بالكمالات العلمية والعملية بالفعل قوية على الأفعال العجيبة مطلعة على أسرار الغيب سابقة إلى أنواع الخير منزهة عن الشرور والقبائح علومهم وأعمالهم أدوم وأقوم وأسلم.","en":"Opponents argue that angels already possess intellectual and practical perfections, perform extraordinary acts, know unseen secrets, promptly do good, are free of sin, and are more constant and secure in their knowledge and works.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-102.07","page":102,"ar":"وقوله تعالى قل لا أقول لكم عندي خزائن الله ولا أعلم الغيب ولا أقول لكم إني ملك وقوله تعالى علمه شديد القوى والعلم أفضل.","en":"They also cite “I do not tell you that I possess God’s treasuries, or know the unseen, or am an angel,” and “He of mighty powers taught him,” treating angelic knowledge as a superior perfection.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-102.08","page":102,"ar":"لن يستنكف المسيح أن يكون عبدا لله ولا الملائكة","en":"And “The Messiah will not disdain to be a servant of God, nor will the angels—” [continued].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-103.01","page":103,"ar":"المقربون قلنا الأول معارض بما مر وتأويل البواقي في كتب التفسير.","en":"—those brought near.” We answer that the first inference is opposed by earlier evidence, while the other verses have interpretations discussed in works of exegesis.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-103.02","page":103,"ar":"وأما تقديم ذكرهم فيجوز أن يكون لتقدمهم في الوجود أو في قوة الإيمان بهم.","en":"The order in which angels are mentioned may reflect temporal priority or the strength of faith in them, rather than superiority of rank.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-103.03","page":103,"ar":"ومن خوارق العادات كرامات الأولياء وتفارق المعجزة بالخلو عن دعوى النبوة فلا توجب التباس النبي بغيره ولا انسداد باب إثبات النبوة بل تفيد زيادة جلالة قدر الأنبياء حيث نالت أممهم تلك المرتبة ببركة الاقتداء بهم.","en":"Extraordinary events can also be miracles of saints (*karāmāt*). They differ from prophetic miracles because they are unaccompanied by a claim of prophecy, do not confuse a prophet with someone else, and may magnify the prophet’s standing because his followers reach such states by following him.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-103.04","page":103,"ar":"وتفارق السحر بأنها لا يجري فيها التعلم والتعليم ولا تأتي فيها المعارضة ولا تجامع النفس الشريرة ولا تكون إلا بمباشرة أعمال مخصوصة وكلاهما واقع لقصة مريم وآصف وغيرهما ما روي عن كثير من الصلحاء.","en":"Saintly wonders differ from sorcery in not proceeding by learned and taught techniques, not admitting an adversarial counter-challenge, and not accompanying an evil soul; [sorcery is associated with] performing specified operations. Both kinds of extraordinary occurrence are represented as actual: the former by the accounts of Mary, Āṣif and the pious, the latter by the evidence that follows.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-103.05","page":103,"ar":"ولقوله تعالى يعلمون الناس السحر ولما ثبت أنه سحر النبي وعائشة وابن عمر.","en":"[As to magic,] there is the verse “They teach people magic,” and the report that the Prophet was bewitched, associated here with ʿĀʾisha and Ibn ʿUmar. [The precise relation of the latter two names to the report requires separate hadith-source verification.]","status":"STAGE64_WITNESS_OR_SEMANTIC_RECHECK_REQUIRED"},{"id":"KAL-103.06","page":103,"ar":"ولا دلالة لقوله تعالى يخيل إليه من سحرهم على أنه لا حقيقة له والإصابة بالعين قد جرت مجرى المشاهدات.","en":"The verse “It was made to seem to him through their magic” does not show that all magic is merely imaginary; harm through the evil eye is treated as something attested in experience.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-103.07","page":103,"ar":"وفيها نزلت آية وإن يكاد الذين كفروا وفي جواز الاستعانة بالرقى والتمائم خلاف.","en":"The verse “Those who disbelieve nearly cause you to stumble” is cited in this connection; scholars differ regarding healing incantations and amulets.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-103.08","page":103,"ar":"والولي لا يبلغ درجة النبي ولا تسقط عنه التكاليف ولا تكون الولاية أفضل من النبوة.","en":"A saint does not reach a prophet’s rank; religious obligations do not fall away from him; sainthood is not higher than prophethood.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-103.09","page":103,"ar":"وأما ولاية النبي فقيل أفضل لما فيها من معنى","en":"As for the sainthood of a prophet, some judge it superior because it comprises—[continued].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-104.01","page":104,"ar":"القرب والاختصاص وقيل بل نبوته أفضل لما فيها من الوساطة بين الحق والخلق والقيام بمصالح الدارين مع شرف مشاهدة الملك.","en":"—intimacy and special nearness; others rank the prophetic office higher because it mediates between Truth and creation, serves interests in both worlds, and includes the honor of encountering the angel.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-104.02","page":104,"ar":"فصل في المعاد.","en":"Section: on resurrection and return.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-104.03","page":104,"ar":"يجوز إعادة المعدوم لأن الإمكان الذاتي لا يزول بحسب الأوقات على أن الوجود الأول ربما أفاد المادة الباقية زيادة استعداد لقبول الوجود في ذلك الوقت.","en":"Recreating what has ceased to exist is possible, for intrinsic possibility does not disappear merely with the passage of time; indeed, the initial existence may leave in surviving matter an increased preparedness to exist again.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-104.04","page":104,"ar":"واحتج المخالف بأن المعدوم لا إشارة إليه فلا حكم عليه وبأنه لا يبقى فرق بين المبدأ والمعاد لإعادة الوقت وبأنه يتخلل العدم بين الشيء ونفسه.","en":"Opponents argue that nothing can be pointed to or predicated of the nonexistent; that restoration would eliminate the difference between the beginning and the return if the very time were restored; and that nonexistence would intervene between a thing and itself.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-104.05","page":104,"ar":"والجواب أن الإشارة العقلية كافية والفرق حاصل بأن المبدأ واقع أولا والمعاد ثانيا وإن كان في زمان واحد وبهذا الاعتبار يجوز تخلل العدم بين الشيء ونفسه.","en":"The response is that intelligible reference suffices; the beginning and the restoration differ in their ordered occurrence, first and second, even under the stipulated identity of time, and in that respect a gap of nonexistence is conceivable.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-104.06","page":104,"ar":"وقد ثبت بالكتاب والسنة وإجماع الأمة المعاد الجسماني وحمل الآيات والأحاديث الواردة في الباب على التمثيل والتصوير للمعاد الروحاني أعني أحوال النفس في السعادة والشقاوة إلحاد.","en":"Bodily resurrection is established by Qurʾān, tradition, and communal consensus. Explaining bodily resurrection passages merely as metaphors for the soul’s bliss and misery is condemned as distortion.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-104.07","page":104,"ar":"ومن يقول بتجرد النفس وبقائها فالحشر على رأيه ظاهر وليس تناسخا لكونه عودا إلى أجزاء أصلية للبدن.","en":"On the view that the soul is immaterial and survives, bodily resurrection is intelligible as its return to original bodily constituents; this is not transmigration.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-105.01","page":105,"ar":"الأول وإن لم يكن الأول بعينه على ما يشعر به قوله تعالى كلما نضجت جلودهم بدلناهم جلودا غيرها.","en":"—the original, even if the restored body were not numerically the first in every respect, as suggested by “Whenever their skins are roasted, We replace them with other skins.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-105.02","page":105,"ar":"واحتج المنكرون بامتناع إعادة المعدوم وقد عرفت أنه لا يتوقف عليها.","en":"Deniers object that restoring a nonexistent thing is impossible, but the point has already been addressed, and resurrection does not depend upon the disputed premise as they suppose.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-105.03","page":105,"ar":"وبأنه لو أكل إنسان إنسانا فالأجزاء المأكولة إن أعيدت في بدن الآكل فلا يكون المأكول بعينه معادا أو في بدن المأكول فلا يكون الآكل بعينه معادا.","en":"They argue that if one person eats another, the consumed bodily parts cannot be restored in the eater without depriving the eaten person of numerical bodily identity, nor restored in the eaten without depriving the eater of it.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-105.04","page":105,"ar":"على أنه يلزم في أكل الكافر المؤمن تنعم الأجزاء العاصية أو تعذيب المطيعة.","en":"If an unbeliever consumes a believer, they add, sinful parts would be rewarded or obedient parts punished.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-105.05","page":105,"ar":"ورد بأن المعاد هو الأجزاء الأصلية من ابتداء الخلق ولعل الله يحفظها من أن تصير أجزاء أصلية لبدن آخر.","en":"The reply is that resurrection concerns the original constituents present from the body’s first formation, which God may preserve from becoming original constituents of another person.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-105.06","page":105,"ar":"وأما العرض فعلى تقدير لزومه يجوز أن تكون إيصال الأجزاء إلى المستحق.","en":"As for accompanying bodily accidents, supposing their restoration were required, God can assign the requisite parts to those entitled to them.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-105.07","page":105,"ar":"ثم النصوص منها ما هي لإثبات نفس الإعادة وهو قوله تعالى وهو الذي يبدأ الخلق ثم يعيده وقوله تعالى فسيقولون من يعيدنا قل الذي فطركم أول مرة.","en":"Of the texts, some establish the return itself, as in “He is the one who originates creation and then restores it,” and “They will say, ‘Who will restore us?’ Say, ‘The One who brought you into being the first time.’”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-105.08","page":105,"ar":"ومنها ما هي لإزالة استبعاد إحياء الرمم من يحيي العظام وهي رميم أإذا متنا وكنا ترابا.","en":"Other verses address doubts over reviving decayed bones, such as “Who will give life to bones when they have crumbled?” and “When we have died and become dust…?”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-105.09","page":105,"ar":"واختلفوا في أن الحشر إعادة بعد الفناء كما يشعر به قوله تعالى هو الأول والآخر وقوله تعالى كل شيء هالك إلا وجهه وقوله تعالى كما بدأنا أول خلق نعيده.","en":"Scholars dispute whether resurrection follows complete annihilation, citing passages on God as First and Last, the passing away of all things, and the restoration of creation as it began.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-106.01","page":106,"ar":"والبدء من العدم أو جمع بعد التفرق كما يشعر به قوله تعالى ربنا أرنا كيف تحيي الموتى إلى يحيي هذه الله بعد موتها وكذلك النشور وكذلك تخرجون.","en":"—or whether it is reassembly after dispersal, as suggested by the verses on showing how the dead are revived and how the resurrection occurs after death.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-106.02","page":106,"ar":"ثم الجنة والنار مخلوقتان الآن لقصة آدم وحواء مع ظواهر مثل أعدت وأزلفت وبرزت.","en":"Paradise and Hell are already created, according to the account of Adam and Eve and the plain meaning of verses such as “prepared,” “brought near,” and “made manifest.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-106.03","page":106,"ar":"قيل يمتنع خلقها في أفلاك هذا العالم لامتناع الخرق والالتئام وفي عناصرها لأنها لا تسع جنة عرضها عرض السماء والأرض وفي عالم آخر لأنه لا حاجة إلى تعدد الجهات فيكون كرّيا فيلزم الخلاء بين العالمين.","en":"One philosophical objection denies their location in existing celestial spheres or elements because of supposed astronomical impossibilities, insufficient space, or the purported need for a void between separate worlds.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-106.04","page":106,"ar":"ولا اشتماله على عناصر لها أحياز طبيعية يلزم أن يكون لعنصر واحد حيزان طبيعيان فيلزم الميل إليه وعنه.","en":"Nor, the objector claims, can that other world contain elements possessing natural places: the same element would then have two natural places and would consequently incline both toward and away from [the relevant place].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-106.05","page":106,"ar":"ورد بمنع المقدمات الفلسفية على أنه لا يمتنع كون العالمين في محيط بهما ولا كون العناصر مختلفة الطبائع أو تحيزها في أحد العالمين غير طبيعي.","en":"The reply denies these philosophical premises: two worlds might be contained within a wider encompassing reality, have elements of different natures, or possess elements whose positions are not natural in the hypothesized sense.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-106.06","page":106,"ar":"فإن قيل فيلزم هلاكهما لقوله تعالى كل شيء هالك إلا وجهه قلنا يحمل الهلاك على غير الفناء ولو سلم فالفناء لحظة لا ينافي الدوام عرفا.","en":"If one argues that “Everything perishes except His face” entails their destruction, it may refer to dependence rather than annihilation; even if an instant of cessation is granted, it need not contradict their commonly understood permanence.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-106.07","page":106,"ar":"والأكثرون على أن الجنة فوق السموات السبع وتحت العرش لقوله تعالى عند سدرة المنتهى عندها جنة المأوى.","en":"Most hold that Paradise is above the seven heavens beneath the Throne, citing “At the Lote Tree of the Boundary, near which is the Garden of Refuge.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-106.08","page":106,"ar":"والنار تحت الأرضين والحق التوقف.","en":"Hell is said to lie beneath the earths; the correct position is to suspend judgment on precise location.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-107.01","page":107,"ar":"فصل.","en":"Section.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-107.02","page":107,"ar":"سؤال القبر وعذابه وثوابه حق بالآيات والأحاديث المتواترة المعنى.","en":"Questioning in the grave, its punishment and its reward are true, established through verses and reports transmitting the meaning abundantly.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-107.03","page":107,"ar":"النار يعرضون عليها غدوا وعشيا، اغرقوا فأدخلوا نارا، يرزقون فرحين بما آتاهم الله من فضله.","en":"Among the cited verses are “They are exposed to the Fire morning and evening,” “They were drowned and admitted into Fire,” and “They receive provision, rejoicing in what God has given them.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-107.04","page":107,"ar":"القبر روضة من رياض الجنة أو حفرة من حفر النيران إذا وضع الميت في قبره.","en":"There are also reports that the grave becomes a garden from the gardens of Paradise or a pit of fire after the dead person is buried.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-107.05","page":107,"ar":"وليس ببعيد أن يوسع القادر المختار اللحد بحيث يمكن الجلوس فيه وأن يبقى من الأجزاء الأصلية قدر ما تقوم به الحياة.","en":"Nor is it far-fetched that the powerful, freely choosing [God] should enlarge the grave sufficiently to permit sitting in it, and that enough of the original bodily parts should remain to sustain life.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-107.06","page":107,"ar":"وأن لا يشاهد الناظر ما يجري على الميت وقوله تعالى لا تذوقون فيها الموت إلا الموتة الأولى.","en":"Nor is it impossible that an observer should fail to perceive what occurs to the dead; the verse concerning only one death is discussed in this connection.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-107.07","page":107,"ar":"وكنتم أمواتا فأحياكم ثم يميتكم ثم يحييكم ربنا أمتنا اثنتين وأحييتنا اثنتين.","en":"The text also cites “You were dead and He gave you life, then He will cause you to die and revive you,” and “Our Lord, You caused us to die twice and gave us life twice.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-107.08","page":107,"ar":"لا ينفي عذاب القبر لجواز أن لا يسمى ما يعقبه موتا أو أن يندرج في الموتة الأولى.","en":"This does not exclude punishment in the grave: the death that follows the relevant intermediate life need not be counted as a distinct death, or it may be subsumed under the first death.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-107.08A","page":107,"ar":"وبالجملة الذي ثبت من الدين أن للميت نوع حياة قدر ما يتألم ويتلذذ به وهل ذلك بإعادة الروح أم لا فيه تردد.","en":"In sum, what is established by religion is that the deceased possesses a kind of life sufficient to experience pain and pleasure; whether this involves the return of the soul remains uncertain.","status":"STAGE71_NEW_SOURCE_RECOVERED_NOT_FULL_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-107.09","page":107,"ar":"ثم جميع أحوال القيامة من المحاسبة وأهوالها والصراط والميزان والحوض","en":"All the events of Resurrection—including the reckoning and its terrors, the bridge, the balance, and the basin—[continue].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-108.01","page":108,"ar":"وتفاصيل أحوال الجنة والنار أمور ممكنة أخبر بها الصادق فوجب التصديق بها.","en":"The detailed conditions of Paradise and Hell are possible things conveyed by the truthful Messenger; assent to them is therefore required.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-108.02","page":108,"ar":"ولا استبعاد في أن يسهل الله تعالى العبور على الصراط وإن كان أحد من السيف وأدق من الشعر، وأن توزن صحائف الأعمال أو تجعل أجساما نورانية أو ظلمانية.","en":"God can make crossing the Bridge easy even if it is sharper than a sword and finer than a hair; deeds may be weighed as written records or given luminous or dark forms.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-108.03","page":108,"ar":"فلا حاجة إلى تأويل الصراط بطريق الجنة والنار وبالأدلة الواضحة والعبادات، والميزان بالعدل أو الإدراك.","en":"There is no need to explain the Bridge as merely a route to Paradise and Hell or as clear proofs and devotional duties, nor to reduce the Balance to justice or understanding.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-108.04","page":108,"ar":"فصل.","en":"Section.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-108.05","page":108,"ar":"الثواب فضل من الله والعقاب عدل منه، ومعنى وجوبهما أنه وعد أو أوعد فلا يخلف الله وعده على خلاف في الوعيد.","en":"Reward is God’s favor; punishment is His justice. Their “necessity” refers to God’s promise or threat: He does not break His promise, while the status of threatened punishment is disputed.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-108.06","page":108,"ar":"ومعنى استحقاقهما ملاءمة إضافتهما إلى الطاعات والمعاصي في مجاري العقول والعادات لأنه لا واجب على الله.","en":"Deserving them means the appropriateness of attaching them to obedience and disobedience in customary reason and usage; nothing is imposed as a duty upon God.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-108.07","page":108,"ar":"وإن الطاعات وإن كثرت لا تفي بشكر بعض النعم ولا مهما لو استحقاقا لما سقط عمن عاش على الكفر ثم آمن أو على الإيمان ثم كفر.","en":"Even abundant acts of worship do not repay all blessings; were reward strictly merited, the switch from lifelong disbelief to faith, or the reverse, would not have its acknowledged effects.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-108.08","page":108,"ar":"وقول المعتزلة أن عدم وجوبهما يفضي إلى التواني في الطاعات والاجتراء على المعاصي وأن إيجاب المشاق بلا نفع يقابلها ظلم ولا مضرة في تركها موجب لوجوب كل ما في فعله منفعة مردود بأن مجرد جواز الترك.","en":"The Muʿtazila argue that without obligatory recompense people would neglect obedience and dare disobey; that imposing onerous duties with no corresponding benefit is unjust; and that absence of harm in omitting a task would force obligation for anything beneficial. The reply begins: the mere possibility of omitting an act—[continued on p.109].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-109.01","page":109,"ar":"غير قادح ومجرد الوقوع كاف في المقصود وإن الفرض لا ينحصر فيما ذكر.","en":"—does not invalidate the purpose. The mere occurrence [of the act] suffices for what is intended, and the proposed purpose is not confined to the objects they mentioned.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-109.02","page":109,"ar":"فصل.","en":"Section.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-109.03","page":109,"ar":"لا خلاف في خلود من دخل الجنة ولا في خلود الكافر في النار سوى الكافر حكما كأطفال المشركين فهم خدم أهل الجنة.","en":"There is no dispute that those admitted to Paradise remain there, nor that unbelievers are eternally in Hell; borderline legal categories, such as children of polytheists, are discussed separately.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-109.04","page":109,"ar":"وقيل من علم الله فيه الإيمان في الجنة والكفر في النار.","en":"One view assigns those whom God knows would believe to Paradise and those whom He knows would disbelieve to Hell.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-109.05","page":109,"ar":"وأما من مات على الإيمان وترك التوبة عن كبيرة فعندهم يخلد في النار وعندنا لا بل يعفى عنه أو يخرج من النار بعد حين للنصوص الشاهدة بأنهم يخرجون من النار ويدخلون الجنة وليس قبل النار وفاقا.","en":"The Muʿtazila hold that an unrepentant believer who dies with a major sin remains in Hell; our position is that such a person may be pardoned or released after punishment, as indicated by texts describing their exit from Hell and entry into Paradise.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-109.06","page":109,"ar":"ولأن ثواب المستحق وعدا وعقلا لا يتصور إلا بالخروج ولأن دوام عذاب من شرب جرعة خمر بعد ما واظب على الطاعات لو لم يكن ظلما فلا ظلم.","en":"Furthermore, reward owed by promise—and on their rational account—cannot be realized except by release from punishment. And if the eternal torment of someone who drank a single mouthful of wine after persevering in obedience would not be injustice, nothing would be injustice.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-109.07","page":109,"ar":"فإن احتجوا بعمومات الوعيد بالخلود قلنا يخص بالكفار أو تعتمد السيئات بقيد الاستحلال أو يحمل الخلود على المكث الطويل أو نحو ذلك جمعا بين الأدلة.","en":"If opponents invoke general scriptural threats of eternal punishment, we restrict them to unbelievers or to sins treated as lawful, or take some language of remaining as signifying long duration, thereby reconciling the proofs.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-109.08","page":109,"ar":"وقالوا لو خرج الفاسق لخرج الكافر لتناهيهما، قلنا لا نسلم علية التناهي ولا صحة القياس في مقابلة النص ولا في الاعتقادات.","en":"They argue that a wrongdoer’s eventual departure would imply an unbeliever’s departure because both are finite agents; we deny the proposed ground of analogy, particularly against explicit texts and in doctrines of belief.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-110.01","page":110,"ar":"ثم الجمهور منهم على أن الكبيرة الواحدة تحبط جميع الطاعات مخالفة للنص والعقل والبعض على أن أيا من الطاعات والمعاصي أزيد أجرا أو وزرا أحبط الأخرى محضاً.","en":"Some hold that a single major sin nullifies all acts of obedience; others say good and evil acts counterbalance, whichever is greater canceling the corresponding share of the other. Both positions are challenged from text and reason.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-110.02","page":110,"ar":"بأن يسقط الأقل ولا يسقط من الأكثر شيء أو موازنة بأن يسقط الأقل ويسقط ما يقابله من الأكثر.","en":"There are further differences between simply canceling the smaller amount and subtracting an equivalent amount from the greater total.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-110.03","page":110,"ar":"وتمسكوا بمثل حبطت أعمالهم لا تبطلوا صدقاتكم أن تحبط أعمالكم.","en":"They support their thesis with such verses as “Their deeds are nullified,” “Do not nullify your charities,” and “lest your deeds be nullified.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-110.04","page":110,"ar":"ولا يفيد التنازع وهو بطلان حسنة كاملة بسيئة سابقة أو لاحقة.","en":"These texts do not prove the disputed claim that one full good deed is abolished through an earlier or later sin.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-110.05","page":110,"ar":"وعورض بمثل فمن يعمل مثقال ذرة خيرا يره وأنه لا كبيرة بربي وزرها على أجر معرفة الله فيجب أن يدوم بها جميع الكبائر.","en":"This is countered by verses such as “Whoever does an atom’s weight of good shall see it,” and by the argument that no major sin has a burden exceeding the reward due to knowing God; on the proposed balancing account, knowledge of God would then have to avert every major sin. [The print’s verb in this reductio is retained for second-witness checking.]","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-110.06","page":110,"ar":"فصل.","en":"Section.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-110.07","page":110,"ar":"يجوز العفو عن الكبائر بدون التوبة لأن العقاب حقه تعالى فله إسقاطه.","en":"Forgiveness of major sins without repentance is possible, because punishment is God’s right, which He may waive.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-110.08","page":110,"ar":"ودل على الوقوع مثل ويعفو عن السيئات ويعفو عن كثير إن الله يغفر الذنوب جميعا وعلى نفيه في الشرك إن الله لا يغفر أن يشرك به.","en":"Scriptural proofs include “He pardons misdeeds,” “He pardons much,” and “God forgives all sins”; associating partners with Him is singled out in “God does not forgive that partners be associated with Him.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-110.09","page":110,"ar":"وفي الأحاديث أيضا والتخصيص بالصغائر أو بما بعد التوبة أو الحمل على تأخير العقوبات المستحقة مع كونه خلاف الظاهر.","en":"Reports support this reading; restricting the passages to minor sins, postrepentance forgiveness, or postponement of punishment is contrary to their apparent sense.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-111.01","page":111,"ar":"وصريح الأحاديث لا يصح في البعض وقالت المعتزلة لمنع بسبب النصوص الواردة في وعيد الفساق فإن الخلف والكذب نقص لا يجوز على الله وعقلا بأن إغراء على القبيح.","en":"Clear reports undermine some restrictive interpretations. The Muʿtazila object that threats against grave sinners must be carried out, for failure to do so would amount to falsehood or encouragement to sin.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-111.02","page":111,"ar":"ورد بأنهم داخلون في عمومات الوعد أيضا فيصادم بطلان الخلف فيه إجماعا وبأن مجرد احتمال العقوبة يكون زاجرا فكيف مع الرجحان.","en":"The answer is that the same major sinners are included in general promises; this would clash with the unanimously denied breaking of the promise. Besides, the bare possibility of punishment is a deterrent—how much more when punishment is preponderantly expected.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-111.03","page":111,"ar":"وإذا جاز العفو عن الكبائر بدون التوبة فمع الشفاعة أولى قال الله تعالى واستغفر لذنبك وللمؤمنين والمؤمنات.","en":"If forgiveness of major sins is possible without repentance, it is all the more so with intercession. God commands, “Seek forgiveness for your sin and for believing men and women.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-111.04","page":111,"ar":"وقال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم «ادخرت شفاعتي لأهل الكبائر من أمتي» فمثل «لا يقبل منها شفاعة»","en":"The Prophet is cited as saying: “I have reserved my intercession for the grave sinners of my community.” Thus texts such as “No intercession will be accepted from it”—[continue into the following clause].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-111.05","page":111,"ar":"«ولا تنفع شفاعة الشافعين» بعد تسليم عموم الزمان والأحوال يخص بالكفار جمعا بين الأدلة.","en":"—and “Nor will the intercession of the intercessors benefit them,” even granting their generality across times and circumstances, are specified to unbelievers so that the evidences may be reconciled.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-111.06","page":111,"ar":"ثم لا خفاء في ورود الشرع بالشفاعة وحملها المعتزلة على طلب المنافع ويلزمهم أن يكون من سأل الله زيادة كرامة النبي شافعا له.","en":"The revealed law plainly affirms intercession; the Muʿtazila interpret it as seeking additional benefits. But then whoever asks God to augment the Prophet’s honor would, on their definition, count as an intercessor *for the Prophet*.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-111.07","page":111,"ar":"وأما الحمل على الصغيرة أو ما بعد التوبة فظاهر البطلان.","en":"Restricting it to minor sins or people who have already repented is manifestly inadequate.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-111.08","page":111,"ar":"ثم الكبيرة هي التي تشعر قلة الاكتراث بالدين أو التي خصت بالوعيد وقيل كل معصية فهي بالإضافة إلى ما دونها كبيرة وإلى ما فوقها صغيرة.","en":"A major sin is either one evincing disregard for religion, or one specifically threatened with punishment. Others define gravity comparatively: an offense is major relative to a lesser one and minor relative to a greater one.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-111.09","page":111,"ar":"وقيل هي الشرك والقتل والقذف والزنا والفرار","en":"Others enumerate idolatry, murder, false accusation of sexual misconduct (*qadhf*), fornication, and flight—[continued on p.112].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-112.01","page":112,"ar":"من الزحف والسحر وأكل مال اليتيم والعقوق والإلحاد في الحرم وقد يزاد الربا والسرقة وشرب الخمر.","en":"—from battle, sorcery, consuming an orphan’s property, disobedience to parents, violating the sanctuary; some also add usury, theft and drinking wine.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-112.02","page":112,"ar":"فصل.","en":"Section.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-112.03","page":112,"ar":"التوبة في الشرع هي الندم عن المعصية لكونها معصية وقيل مع العزم على الترك في الاستقبال.","en":"In the law, repentance is regret over sin *because it is sin*; some add resolve not to repeat it.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-112.04","page":112,"ar":"وقالت المعتزلة اعتقاد أنه أساء وأنه لو أمكنه رد تلك المعصية لردها وهي واجبة سمعا لقوله تعالى توبوا إلى الله.","en":"Muʿtazilites describe it as recognizing the wrong and wishing, were it possible, to undo it. Repentance is obligatory by revelation: “Repent to God.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-112.05","page":112,"ar":"وقالوا عقلا لما فيها من دفع الضرر وكذا ثبوت القبول ووجوبها على الفور حتى يأثم التارك مثل حقه.","en":"They also argue for rational obligation because repentance averts harm, and affirm its acceptance and immediacy.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-112.06","page":112,"ar":"ثم سقوط العقوبة عندنا بمحض الكرم وعند أكثرهم بنفس التوبة ولا يلزم تجددها كلما تذكر الذنب وتصح التوبة عن بعض الذنوب خاصة.","en":"For us, remission of punishment proceeds solely from divine generosity; many opponents tie it to repentance itself. Repeating repentance every time a sin is remembered is not necessarily required, and repentance from some sins in particular is valid.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-112.07","page":112,"ar":"وتكفي الإجمال وإن علم تفاصيل الذنوب وقد يتوقف تحققها على واجب آخر كرد المغصوب أو بذله.","en":"General repentance may suffice even with awareness of individual offenses, although its completion can require further duties, such as returning stolen property or making restitution.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-112.08","page":112,"ar":"وقد يلزم ذلك الواجب الآخر معها كحد القذف وقضاء الصلاة وإرشاد من أضله والاعتذار إلى من آذاه.","en":"Other obligations can remain alongside repentance, including prescribed penalties, making up missed prayers, correcting those misled and apologizing to people wronged.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-112.09","page":112,"ar":"ويجب الأمر بالواجب والنهي عن الحرام ويندب الأمر بالمندوب والنهي عن المكروه بشرط العلم بوجه المعروف والمنكر وتجويز التأثير وانتفاء المفسدة.","en":"Commanding obligatory conduct and forbidding prohibited conduct are duties; encouraging recommended conduct and discouraging disliked conduct are recommended, subject to knowledge of the act, possible benefit and avoidance of greater harm.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-112.10","page":112,"ar":"ولا يختص","en":"This is not restricted—[continued].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-113.01","page":113,"ar":"بالوالي إلا ما يفضي إلى القتال ولا بالمجتهد إلا ما يفتقر إليه وهو فرض كفاية يسقط بقيام البعض.","en":"—to a ruler, except actions leading to fighting, nor to a jurist except where specialist judgment is required. It is a communal obligation discharged when enough people perform it.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-113.02","page":113,"ar":"ولا دلالة لقوله تعالى «عليكم أنفسكم» على نفي الوجوب ولا «لا إكراه في الدين» منسوخ.","en":"“Take care of yourselves” does not establish that the duty is absent; nor does “There is no compulsion in religion,” which Taftāzānī here treats as abrogated, refute it.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-113.03","page":113,"ar":"فصل.","en":"Section.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-113.04","page":113,"ar":"الإيمان في اللغة التصديق وفي الشرع تصديق النبي فيما علم مجيئه به بالضرورة.","en":"In ordinary language *īmān* is assent; legally it is assent to what is necessarily known to have been brought by the Prophet.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-113.05","page":113,"ar":"والأكثرون على أنه لابد من الإقرار باللسان وكثير من السلف على أنه التصديق والإقرار والعمل.","en":"Most add a verbal confession, and many early authorities include assent, confession, and works together.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-113.06","page":113,"ar":"ولا يخرج بترك العمل من الإيمان خلافا للمعتزلة ولا يدخل في الكفر خلافا للخوارج.","en":"Abandoning works does not in itself extinguish faith, contrary to the Muʿtazilites, nor render one an unbeliever, contrary to the Khārijites.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-113.07","page":113,"ar":"فإن قيل كيف لا ينتفي الكل بانتفاء الجزء قلنا المراد أنه يطلق على أساس النجاة وعلى الكمال المنجي.","en":"If it is asked how the whole could survive the loss of a part, we reply that “faith” may name the foundation of salvation or its complete and fully saving realization.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-113.08","page":113,"ar":"والدليل على أنه فعل القلب كتب في قلوبهم الإيمان وقلبه مطمئن بالإيمان ولم تؤمن قلوبهم ولمّا يدخل الإيمان في قلوبهم.","en":"The evidence that faith belongs to the heart includes “He inscribed faith in their hearts”; “his heart is secure in faith”; “their hearts have not believed”; and “faith has not yet entered your hearts.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-113.09","page":113,"ar":"وفي الحديث اللهم ثبت قلبي على دينك في قلبه مثقال حبة من خردل من الإيمان.","en":"Prophetic reports speak of the heart’s remaining firm in religion and of a mustard-seed’s weight of faith in the heart.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-113.10","page":113,"ar":"والاكتفاء بالكلمتين إنما كان في حكم الدنيا من عصمة الدم والمال وحقيقة الإيمان التصديق والإذعان والقبول المعبر عنه بالفارسية بكرویدن.","en":"The two testimonies suffice for worldly legal protection of life and property; faith itself is assenting, submitting, and accepting—expressed by a Persian term meaning acceptance or believing.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-114.01","page":114,"ar":"الإنكار والتكذيب لا مجرد العلم والمعرفة الحاصلة لبعض الكفار يعرفونه كما يعرفون أبناءهم ليعلمون أنه الحق من ربهم وجحدوا بها واستيقنتها أنفسهم.","en":"Its opposite is rejection and denial, not merely a lack of knowledge: some unbelievers recognized the truth as they recognized their sons and were inwardly certain of it while denying it.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-114.02","page":114,"ar":"ويقابله حينئذ الجهالة والنكارة وقد وقع في عبارة السلف مكان التصديق المعرفة والعلم والمراد العلم التصديقي.","en":"By contrast, the opposites of mere cognition would be ignorance or unfamiliarity. When earlier authorities use “knowledge” or “recognition” for faith, the intended knowledge is assent, not bare awareness.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-114.03","page":114,"ar":"ولم يطرأ على الإيمان والتصديق نقل ولذا كانوا يمتثلون من غير توقف واستفسار وإنما خص متعلقه بأمور مخصوصة.","en":"The ordinary sense of assent was not replaced by an entirely new technical sense, which explains immediate compliance without asking for a wholly new definition; the law specifies the objects of assent.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-114.04","page":114,"ar":"ولهذا صح في جواب أخبرني عن الإيمان أن تؤمن بالله وملائكته وكتبه ورسله.","en":"Thus, to the request “Tell me about faith,” the response correctly enumerates believing in God, His angels, His books and His messengers.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-114.05","page":114,"ar":"فإن قيل الإيمان مأمور به فيلزم أن يكون فعلا اختياريا والتصديق المقابل للتكذيب كيفية من أقسام العلم.","en":"An objection: faith is commanded, so it must be a voluntary act, whereas assent—contrasted with denial—is a quality belonging to knowledge.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-114.06","page":114,"ar":"قلنا ليس معنى كون المأمور به اختياريا أن يكون من مقولة الفعل البتة بل أن يصح تعلق القدرة به وكسبه بالاختيار وإن كان هو في نفسه كيفية كالعلم والنظر وغيرها.","en":"We answer that a commanded object need not belong to the Aristotelian category of action; it must be something to which power and voluntary acquisition can relate, even if it is intrinsically a quality, like knowledge or examination.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-114.07","page":114,"ar":"كالقيام والقعود والتسخن والتبرد والصلاة والصوم فغاية الأمر أنه يشترط كون التصديق حاصلا بالاختيار ومباشرة الأسباب.","en":"Examples are standing, sitting, becoming warm or cool, praying, and fasting. The point is that assent is required to arise through volition and the undertaking of its means.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-114.08","page":114,"ar":"وأما أنه معنى غير ما جعل في المنطق مقابلا للتصور وفسر بكونه إذعانا فلا وعلى ما ذكر فاليقين الخالي من","en":"It does not follow that faith is a different kind of cognition from the assent opposed to conception in logic, or from the indicated notion of acceptance. The argument then turns to a certainty devoid of—[continued].","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-115.01","page":115,"ar":"الإذعان كالسفسطائي ولبعض الكفار لا يكون تصديقاً بل تصوراً أو واسطة.","en":"Submission or assent, like that of a sophist or certain unbelievers, is not always [properly called] assent in the relevant sense; it may be conception or some intermediate state.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-115.02","page":115,"ar":"واليقين المقارن للإذعان بلا كسب واختيار لا يكون إيماناً شرعاً.","en":"Certainty accompanied by assent, if it is devoid of acquisition and choice, does not count as faith in the legal sense.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-115.03","page":115,"ar":"فيلزم أن يكون تصديق الملائكة بما أتى إليهم والأنبياء بما أوحي إليهم والصديقين بما سمعوا عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم أو وقع في قلوبهم عند مشاهدة المعجزة كله مكتسباً بالاختيار.","en":"On that account, the assent of angels to what reached them, of prophets to what was revealed to them, and of the truly faithful to what they heard from the Prophet or found in their hearts on witnessing a miracle must all be considered voluntarily acquired.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-115.04","page":115,"ar":"أو يكون بعد تمكنهم من تحصيل ذلك بالاختيار.","en":"Or it must have occurred after they were able to obtain it by choice.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-115.05","page":115,"ar":"وربما يناقش في حصول اليقين بدون الإذعان وفي كون بعض الكفار موقنين بجميع ما جاء به النبي غير مصدقين.","en":"One may dispute whether certainty can exist without assent, and whether some unbelievers can be certain of everything the Prophet brought while still failing to assent.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-115.06","page":115,"ar":"وأن كفرهم مبني على عدم التصديق به لا على عدم الانقياد به بناء على ظهور أمارات الإنكار من الإباء عن الأوامر وقبول الأحكام ونحو ذلك لكن صدق وسجد للصنم.","en":"Their unbelief may instead be traced to their refusal to assent, inferred from signs of denial such as rejecting commands and rulings—although a person might assent and yet prostrate to an idol.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-115.07","page":115,"ar":"وإذ قد ثبت أن الإيمان اسم للتصديق ولا نقل وأن المؤمن قد يؤمر وينهى كقوله تعالى يا أيها الذين آمنوا لا تقدموا.","en":"Faith, as established, is a name for assent without semantic transfer; one who believes can also receive commands and prohibitions, as in “O you who believe, do not put yourselves forward.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-115.08","page":115,"ar":"وأن العمل قد يعطف عليه مثل قوله آمنوا وعملوا الصالحات وقد ينهى عنه وإن طائفتان من المؤمنين اقتتلوا.","en":"Works may be coordinated with faith in expressions such as “those who believed and did righteous deeds”; and believers can be censured for wrongdoing, as in the verse concerning two parties of believers who fight.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-115.09","page":115,"ar":"وأن الإيمان شرط العبادة وأن من صدق وأقر قبل أن يعمل مؤمن من ظهور الأعمال غير.","en":"Faith is a prerequisite for worship, and one who assents and confesses is counted a believer before the appearance of works—[the argument continues].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-116.01","page":116,"ar":"داخلة في حقيقة الإيمان فما أطلق عليه كثير من السلف من أنه اسم للتصديق والإقرار والعمل أرادوا الإيمان الكامل.","en":"—even though works are not included in the essential definition of faith. Thus, when many of the early authorities spoke of faith as assent, confession and works, they meant complete faith.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-116.02","page":116,"ar":"كما قيل إن الإقرار ركن زائد لا يفوت الإيمان بفوته.","en":"Similarly, it is said that outward confession is an additional pillar whose absence does not itself extinguish inward faith.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-116.03","page":116,"ar":"والمعتزلة ينكرون إطلاق الإيمان على مجرد التصديق بالأمور المخصوصة كما في الآيات المذكورة ولكنهم يدعون النقل إلى الأعمال.","en":"The Muʿtazilites reject applying “faith” to bare assent concerning the specified objects and instead claim that the term has been transferred to include works.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-116.04","page":116,"ar":"لقوله تعالى وذلك دين القيمة وأن الدين عند الله الإسلام والإسلام هو الإيمان لما سيأتي.","en":"They appeal to “That is the upright religion” and “The religion with God is Islam”; the relation between Islam and faith will be addressed shortly.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-116.05","page":116,"ar":"ولقوله تعالى إنما المؤمنون الذين إذا ذكر الله وجلت قلوبهم وما كان الله ليضيع إيمانكم.","en":"Other citations include “Believers are only those whose hearts tremble when God is mentioned” and “God would not let your faith go to waste.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-116.06","page":116,"ar":"قلنا يجوز أن يكون ذلك إشارة إلى الإخلاص والتدين وأن يراد أن المعتبر دين الإسلام وأن يكون الإسلام غير الإيمان.","en":"The reply is that these may refer to sincerity and religious observance; the “religion” in question may be the religion of Islam, while Islam and faith might have distinct senses.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-116.07","page":116,"ar":"وأن يراد المؤمنون الكاملون وأن يكون الإيمان مجازاً في الصلاة أو يراد التصديق بوجوبها.","en":"“Believers” may mean believers possessing complete faith; “faith” may designate prayer figuratively or assent to the obligation of prayer.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-116.08","page":116,"ar":"وأما مثل لا يزني الزاني وهو مؤمن فقط الظاهر ومثل وما يؤمن أكثرهم بالله إلا وهم مشركون.","en":"As for such reports as “The fornicator does not fornicate while he is a believer,” the apparent sense must be interpreted in context, as also the verse “Most of them do not believe in God without associating others with Him.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-116.09","page":116,"ar":"ومن الناس من يقول آمنا بالله معنى التصديق بالله وحده وباللسان فقط.","en":"The verse “Among people are those who say: We believe in God” may address verbal profession alone rather than genuine inner assent.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-116.10","page":116,"ar":"والكفر بمثل سجدة الصنم وإلقاء المصحف في القاذورات ليس لكونه إخلالاً بالعمل والاقتصار على الإيمان.","en":"Acts such as prostrating to an idol or casting the Qurʾān into filth constitute unbelief not merely by falling short in works while keeping faith intact—[continued on p117].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-117.01","page":117,"ar":"الإيمان بل لأن الشرع جعل لبعض المعاصي أمارة التكذيب.","en":"Rather, the Law has made certain transgressions signs of denial.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-117.02","page":117,"ar":"فمرتكب الكبيرة عندنا مؤمن وعندهم ليس بمؤمن ولا كافر لأن له بعض أحكام المؤمن كعصمة الدم والمال وبعض أحكام الكافر كعدم أهلية الإمامة وعدم أهلية القضاء والشهادة.","en":"According to us, the perpetrator of a major sin is a believer; according to the Muʿtazilites, neither believer nor unbeliever. They reason that such a person retains some legal effects of belief, such as protection of life and property, but lacks certain qualifications such as holding the imamate, judgeship or giving testimony.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-117.03","page":117,"ar":"فجعلوا له منزلة بين المنزلتين واسمًا بين اسمين وزعموا أن هذا أخذ بالمتفق عليه وهو الفسق وترك المختلف فيه وهو الإيمان والكفر.","en":"They therefore assigned the grave sinner a position between the two positions, and a name between the two names. They claimed this adopts what is agreed upon—iniquity (fisq)—and avoids what is disputed, namely faith and unbelief.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-117.04","page":117,"ar":"ورد بأنه ترك للمجتمع عليه وهو عدم الواسطة.","en":"The response is that the view abandons another agreed matter: the absence of an intermediate category.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-117.05","page":117,"ar":"وعند الخوارج هو كافر تمسكاً بظواهر النصوص الواردة بكفر الفساق تغليظاً.","en":"According to the Khārijites, the grave sinner is an unbeliever, relying upon apparently literal statements describing sinners as unbelievers, although these may be expressions of severe warning.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-117.06","page":117,"ar":"والباطنية بانحصار العذاب على الكفار تأويلا، ونحو ذلك.","en":"The Bāṭiniyya are also mentioned in connection with interpreting punishment as restricted to unbelievers, and similar interpretations.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-117.07","page":117,"ar":"وقيل هو منافق لأن عصيانه دليل كذبه في دعوى تصديقه، ورد بالمنع وما جعل مثل الكذب من علامات النفاق فمؤول.","en":"Another view calls the sinner a hypocrite, arguing that disobedience betrays the falsity of his professed assent. This inference is denied; traditions treating lying and similar conduct as signs of hypocrisy require interpretation.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-117.08","page":117,"ar":"فصل: الإجماع على أن كل مؤمن مسلم وبالعكس وأن حكمهما واحد لأن مرجعهما إلى القبول والإذعان، ولكن لتغاير مفهومهما قد يتعاطفان.","en":"Section: There is consensus that every believer is a Muslim and conversely, and that their legal ruling is one, because both refer to acceptance and submission. Yet because their concepts differ, they can be conjoined as distinct expressions.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-117.09","page":117,"ar":"مثل إن المسلمين والمسلمات والمؤمنين والمؤمنات فما زادهم إلا إيماناً وتسليماً.","en":"Thus revelation juxtaposes “Muslim men and Muslim women, believing men and believing women”; it can likewise associate assent with submission.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-117.10","page":117,"ar":"ولإطلاق الإسلام على الاستسلام والانقياد الظاهر قد يثبت مع نفي الإيمان كقوله ...","en":"And since “Islam” can be applied to outward surrender and compliance, it may be affirmed in a case where faith is denied, as in the following scriptural statement—[continued on p. 118].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-118.01","page":118,"ar":"قالت الأعراب آمنا قل لم تؤمنوا ولكن قولوا أسلمنا ولكن السؤال عن متعلق الإيمان وعن شرائع الإسلام.","en":"“The Bedouins said, ‘We believe.’ Say: You have not believed; rather say: We have submitted.” The discussions of faith’s object and Islam’s practices must be distinguished.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-118.02","page":118,"ar":"وورد في الحديث الإيمان أن تؤمن بالله ... والإسلام أن تشهد أن لا إله إلا الله الخ.","en":"In the well-known report, faith is described as believing in God and the other articles; Islam as testifying that there is no god but God, and so forth.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-118.03","page":118,"ar":"والجمهور على أن الإيمان لا يزيد ولا ينقص لما أنه التصديق البالغ حد اليقين وإنما يتفاوت إذا جعل اسماً للطاعات.","en":"The majority hold that faith neither increases nor decreases insofar as it is assent attaining certainty; it varies if the name is extended to obedient deeds.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-118.04","page":118,"ar":"ورد بأن اليقين أيضاً يتفاوت قوة وضعفاً وأن إيمان آحاد الأمة لا يساوي إيمان الأنبياء قطعاً.","en":"The objection is that certainty itself varies in strength, and the faith of ordinary members of the community is certainly not equal to that of the prophets.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-118.05","page":118,"ar":"وأن ظاهر الكتاب والسنة قبول الزيادة والنقصان وإذا تليت عليهم آياته زادتهم إيماناً.","en":"Moreover, the apparent import of Scripture and reports supports increase and decrease: “When His signs are recited to them, they increase them in faith.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-118.06","page":118,"ar":"ليزدادوا إيماناً مع إيمانهم ويزداد الذين آمنوا إيماناً.","en":"Other cited expressions include “that they may increase in faith along with their faith” and “that those who believe may increase in faith.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-118.07","page":118,"ar":"وفي الحديث أن الإيمان يزيد حتى يدخل صاحبه الجنة وينقص حتى يدخل صاحبه النار.","en":"A report is cited describing faith increasing until its possessor enters Paradise and decreasing until its possessor enters the Fire.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-118.08","page":118,"ar":"والحمل على الزيادة بحسب الدوام والثبات والاستعداد وبحسب زيادة المؤمن به عند ملاحظة التفاصيل أو زيادة الآثار والأنوار تكلف.","en":"Explaining the increase solely through persistence, stability, predisposition, added detail of what is believed, or an increase of its effects and illuminations is strained.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-118.09","page":118,"ar":"ثم كثير من الصحابة والمجتهدين على صحة الاستثناء في الإيمان بأن يقال أنا مؤمن إن شاء الله تعالى تأدباً أو تبركاً أو تردداً فيما هو آية النجاة أعني إيمان الموافاة والعبرة بالوفاة بمعنى أنه المنجي وإن كان الناجز إيماناً ثابتاً وكذا الكفر والسعادة والشقاوة.","en":"Many Companions and jurists allow the reservation “I am a believer, God willing,” as reverence, invocation of blessing, or uncertainty about the faith by which a life ends and salvation is attained. The faith presently possessed may still be real, as may the present state of unbelief and the categories of felicity and wretchedness.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-118.10","page":118,"ar":"والآخرون على","en":"Others take the contrary position—[continued].","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-119.01","page":119,"ar":"منعه للإيهام الشك في الناجز.","en":"They disallow the reservation because it suggests doubt about one’s actual present faith.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-119.02","page":119,"ar":"فصل: الجمهور على صحة إيمان المقلد لصدق التعريف عليه وعدم الدليل على اشتراط الدليل والقياس على إيمان اليائس فاسد لأن الهلاك كونه إيماناً دفع عذاب ولا يلزم بقاء العبد قدرة التصرف في نفسه والاستمتاع بها.","en":"Section: the majority accept the faith of one who follows authority without demonstrative proof: the definition applies, and there is no evidence making demonstration an essential condition. The analogy to faith at the point of despair is defective, since that situation has distinct conditions.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-119.03","page":119,"ar":"وأما المانعون فالمعتزلة يشترطون في كل مسألة التمكن من إقامة الحجة ودفع الشبهة.","en":"Those who disallow such faith include Muʿtazilites requiring the capacity, in each question, to establish an argument and resolve an objection.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-119.04","page":119,"ar":"والشيخ اكتفى باعتقاد دليل في الجملة وإلى هذا رجع المتأخرون من المعتزلة.","en":"Another theologian requires only possession of an argument in general; later Muʿtazilites are said to have returned toward this view.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-119.05","page":119,"ar":"حيث قالوا الخلاف فيمن نشأ في شاهق جبل ولم يتفكر فأخبره إنسان بما يجب عليه اعتقاده فصدقه.","en":"They specify that the dispute concerns a person raised on a remote mountaintop who has never reflected, but is told what must be believed and assents.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-119.06","page":119,"ar":"وأما من نشأ في دار الإسلام ولو في الصحاري وتواتر عنده حال النبي فمن أهل النظر.","en":"By contrast, one raised in Islamic territory, even in a desert, and acquainted through widespread reports with the Prophet’s condition has grounds for rational consideration.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-119.07","page":119,"ar":"وقال بعضهم أن وجوب النظر إنما هو في حق البعض وأما العاجزون كالعوام فلا يكلفون إلا تقليد الحق أو سماع أوائل الدلائل.","en":"Some say that inquiry is obligatory only for some, while those incapable of reasoning, such as the unlearned, need only follow the truth or hear the rudiments of proofs.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-119.08","page":119,"ar":"وليس الخلاف في إجراء أحكام الإسلام بل في أنه هل يعاقب عقوبة الكافر والكفر عدم الإيمان عما من شأنه وإن خلا عن تكذيب وإنكار.","en":"The dispute is not over applying the outward rulings of Islam but over whether such a person receives the punishment of unbelief. Unbelief is discussed as absence of faith where faith ought to be present, even without explicit denial or rejection.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-119.09","page":119,"ar":"ومن فسره بالجحد بالله أراد الجهل على ما قطعنا أنه من أحكامه إجمالا وتفصيلا.","en":"Those who define it in terms of denial of God treat ignorance of what is requisite as relevant to the rulings; the detailed wording needs rechecking.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-119.10","page":119,"ar":"والتكفير ببعض","en":"And declaring unbelief because of certain—[continued].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-120.01","page":120,"ar":"الأفعال مع بقاء كمال التصديق أن سلم فمبني على أن الشارع جعل لبعض المحظورات علامة التكذيب وكذا لبعض التأويلات في الأصول.","en":"—acts, notwithstanding the persistence of complete assent, if admitted, is based upon the Lawgiver’s treating certain forbidden acts as signs of denial, as likewise certain doctrinal interpretations concerning first principles.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-120.02","page":120,"ar":"والكافر إن أظهر الإيمان خص باسم المنافق وإن سبق إسلامه فالمرتد وإن آل اعتقاده إلى تعدد الإله فالمشرك.","en":"An unbeliever who displays faith is specifically called a hypocrite; one who previously professed Islam, an apostate; one whose belief entails multiple gods, an associationist.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-120.03","page":120,"ar":"وإن تدين ببعض الكتب السماوية فالكتابي وإن اعتقد استناد الحوادث إلى الزمان فالدهري.","en":"One adhering to certain revealed books is a scripturalist (*kitābī*); one attributing events ultimately to time is called a *dahrī*.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-120.04","page":120,"ar":"وإن نفي الصانع فالمعطل وإن أظهر شعائر الإسلام وأبطن عقائد هي كفر وفاقاً فالزنديق.","en":"One denying the Maker is a denialist (*muʿaṭṭil*); one outwardly exhibiting Islam while inwardly harboring doctrines of unbelief is a *zindīq*.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-120.05","page":120,"ar":"والجمهور على أن من كان مخالف الحق من أهل القبلة ليس بكافر ما لم ينكر شيئاً من ضروريات الدين.","en":"The majority hold that one of the people of the qibla who differs from the truth is not an unbeliever unless he denies something necessarily established in religion.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-120.06","page":120,"ar":"لأن النبي ومن بعده لم يفتشوا عن العقائد والتحقق عن الأصول التي هي من ضروريات الدين إنما كان لشرحها وظهور أدلتها.","en":"For the Prophet and those after him did not interrogate people’s private doctrines; determining the fundamental teachings concerns their explanation and the manifestness of their evidences.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-120.07","page":120,"ar":"والمعتزلة يكفرون بأكثر العقائد المخصوصة بأهل السنة والجماعة ولذا قال الأستاذ نكفر من كفرنا.","en":"Muʿtazilites declare unbelief on account of many doctrines specific to the Sunnis, which occasioned the statement “We declare unbelievers those who declare us unbelievers.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-120.08","page":120,"ar":"والفسق هو الخروج من طاعة الله بارتكاب الكبيرة أو الإصرار على الصغيرة والبدعة مخالفة أهل الحق في العقيدة وحكمها البغض والإهانة.","en":"Iniquity (*fisq*) is departing from obedience to God through committing a major sin or persisting in a minor one. Doctrinal innovation (*bidʿa*) is opposition to the people of truth in belief; its prescribed treatment, in the author’s formulation, is aversion and humiliation.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-120.09","page":120,"ar":"ومنهم من جعل المخالفة في بعض الفروع منها ومنهم من زاد كل أمر لم يكن في عهد الصحابة.","en":"Some extend innovation to certain subsidiary questions; others include everything that did not occur in the Companions’ age—[continued].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-121.01","page":121,"ar":"في عهد الصحابة ومن هاهنا جاز كون بعض البدعة حسنة.","en":"—during the Companions’ time; on this broader classification, some innovations may be good.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-121.02","page":121,"ar":"فصل: الإمامة رئاسة عامة في أمر الدين والدنيا خلافة عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم.","en":"Section: the imamate is a general headship over religious and worldly affairs in succession to the Prophet.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-121.03","page":121,"ar":"ثم نصب الإمام واجب على الخلق سمعاً عندنا للإجماع ولكونه مقدمة لما يجب من إقامة الحدود من منافع لا تحصى.","en":"Appointing an imam is obligatory upon the community by revealed authority according to us, on the grounds of consensus and because it is a necessary means for duties such as enforcing legal penalties and securing innumerable benefits.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-121.04","page":121,"ar":"وعقلاً عند بعض المعتزلة لما فيه من دفع الضرر.","en":"Some Muʿtazilites make its obligation rational, because the imamate prevents harm.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-121.05","page":121,"ar":"ورد بأن هذا القدر لا يوجب استحقاق تاركه الذم والعقاب وعلى الله عند الشيعة لكونه لطفاً محصلاً للمعرفة مقرباً إلى الطاعة.","en":"The reply is that the benefit alone does not entail blame and punishment for leaving it undone; the Shiʿites instead maintain that God is obliged to provide an imam as grace facilitating knowledge and obedience.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-121.06","page":121,"ar":"ورد بأنه لا وجوب على الله وأنه يتضمن مفاسد وإن قلت على أنه لو سلم فكمال اللطف إظهاره فلم يجب إذ لو وجب لأظهره.","en":"The response denies that anything is obligatory upon God, observes possible harms, and argues that if the fullest grace required the imam’s manifest presence, such manifestation would have occurred.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-121.07","page":121,"ar":"وقول الخوارج أنه لا يجب أصلاً لما فيه من إثارة الفتنة فاسد لقيام الدليل ولأن فتنة عدمه أشد.","en":"The Khārijite claim that no imam is obligatory, because the office causes discord, is rejected on the ground of the argument for it and the more serious discord arising from its absence.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-121.08","page":121,"ar":"ويشترط فيه التكليف والحرية والذكورة والعدالة وزاد الجمهور الشجاعة والاجتهاد وإصابة الرأي لظهور الاحتياج إليها.","en":"Conditions include legal capacity, free status, being male, and uprightness. The majority add courage, independent legal competence, and sound judgment, because their need is evident.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-121.09","page":121,"ar":"وكونه قرشياً لقوله عليه السلام الأئمة من قريش إلا قدّموا قرشياً.","en":"He must belong to Quraysh, on the basis of the report “The imams are from Quraysh” and precedents involving Qurashī candidates.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-121.10","page":121,"ar":"ولأن شرف النسب أثر في الآراء وخالف الخوارج وأكثر المعتزلة لقوله عليه الصلاة والسلام أطيعوا ولو أمر عليكم عبد حبشي أجْدَع.","en":"The Khārijites and many Muʿtazilites dissent, citing the report to obey even if a mutilated Abyssinian slave is appointed over you.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-122.01","page":122,"ar":"وعند الاضطرار يكون ذو شوكة نصب أو استولى.","en":"In an emergency, the office may pass to a person possessing sufficient coercive strength, whether through appointment or taking control.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-122.02","page":122,"ar":"واشترط الشيعة كونه هاشمياً بل علوياً وأفضل أهل زمانه ليصح تقديم المفضول.","en":"Shiʿites stipulate Hashimite—and indeed ʿAlid—descent and superiority over contemporaries; the question whether one less excellent may be advanced is disputed.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-122.03","page":122,"ar":"ورد بالمنع إذ ربما يكون المفضول أصلح وإن يكون معصوماً قياساً على النبوة.","en":"It is answered that a less excellent person may be more suitable, while analogy with prophecy is invoked to argue for impeccability.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-122.04","page":122,"ar":"ولكونه واجب الإطاعة ولأن المعصية ظلم وعهد الإمامة لا يناله الظالمون ولأنه لو عصى لافتقر إلى إمام آخر وتسلسل ولكان ناقضاً للشرع وقد شرع حافظاً له.","en":"Arguments for the imam’s impeccability are drawn from the duty of obedience, the exclusion of wrongdoers from the covenant, the alleged regress if a sinful imam required another imam over him, and the danger of subverting the law which he is to guard.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-122.05","page":122,"ar":"ورد بمنع الجامع وبأنه إنما يجب فيما لا يخالف الشرع وعند المخالفة يرجع إلى الأدلة والاجتهاد وبأن عدم العصمة لا يوجب المعصية فضلاً عن الظلم.","en":"The objections deny the relevant analogy; obedience holds only where commands do not contravene the Law; disputed cases revert to proofs and judgment; and non-impeccability does not itself imply actual wrongdoing.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-122.06","page":122,"ar":"وأن وجوبه شرعي لا عقلي وبأنه ليس حافظاً له بذاته.","en":"The duty to obey is legally rather than rationally established, and the imam does not guard the law simply through his own essence.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-122.07","page":122,"ar":"ثم الجمهور على ثبوت الإمامة وانعقادها باختيار أهل الحل والعقد إذ قد اشتغل الصحابة بعد وفاة النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم وبعد قتل عثمان بالبيعة والاختيار من غير نكير.","en":"The majority hold that the imamate is constituted through selection by those qualified to bind and loosen; the conduct of the Companions after the Prophet’s death is cited, as are later precedents of allegiance and selection.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-122.08","page":122,"ar":"وخالف الشيعة لأنه قد يخفى على أهل البيعة بعض الشروط كالعصمة والأفضلية ومعرفة الدين كله ولأنه ليس إليهم توليته مثل القضاء والاحتساب ولأن فيه إثارة الفتنة.","en":"Shiʿites object that electorates may not know an imam’s necessary qualities—impeccability, superior excellence, complete knowledge of religion—and deny that the office may be conferred by ordinary human appointment.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-122.09","page":122,"ar":"ولأن من اختاروه يكون خليفة منهم لا من الله ورسوله.","en":"The chosen incumbent, they argue, would be the people’s deputy, rather than God’s or the Messenger’s.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-123.01","page":123,"ar":"بمنع الاشتراط ومنع الخفاء بمعنى عدم الظن وبأنه لو سلم عدم تفويض مثل القضاء فلوجوب الإمام وبأنه لا فتنة عند الإذعان للحق.","en":"These conditions are rejected; the alleged unknowability is disputed, and the possibility of appointing other authorities does not entail denial of the community’s role in selecting an imam.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-123.02","page":123,"ar":"واعتبار الترجيح، ولو سلم ففتنة عدم الإمام أشد، وأن من اختاروه خليفة الله ورسوله بدليل الشرع.","en":"Consider also the assessment of relative advantages. Even if the objection is granted, the strife ensuing from the absence of an imam would be worse; the one selected is the successor to God and His Messenger by the authorization of the Law.","status":"STAGE58_CLAUSE_VISUALLY_CORRECTED_NOT_PAGE_CERTIFIED"},{"id":"KAL-123.03","page":123,"ar":"وفيه إكمال الدين واستخلاف ووصية من النبي فلا يرد «اليوم أكملت لكم دينكم»، وأنه كان يستخلف ويوصي البتة.","en":"The response invokes the completion of religion and the Prophet’s practice of appointing deputies and making testamentary instructions; thus the verse “Today I have perfected your religion” is not conclusive against this account, for he did indeed appoint deputies and give instructions.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-123.04","page":123,"ar":"وأما ادعاؤهم النص الجلي على علي فَقَدْح على أكابر الصحابة بالجهل والعناد والفساد بل في علي إذ لم يقم بالأمر ولم يحتج بالنص.","en":"As for the alleged explicit designation of ʿAlī, the author objects that it would impugn the senior Companions as ignorant or obstinate, and would raise a difficulty concerning ʿAlī’s own failure to assert the alleged designation as decisive proof.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-123.05","page":123,"ar":"بل قد قدح في الكتاب حيث أثنى عليهم وجعلهم خير أمة.","en":"It would also, he argues, conflict with scriptural praise of the Companions as the best community.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-123.06","page":123,"ar":"روى أن عليًا قبل الشورى وقال لطلحة إن أردت بايعتك وعاون أبا بكر وعمر وأشار إليهما بالصلح وصلى معهما الجمع والأعياد.","en":"The author cites reports that ʿAlī accepted deliberation and said to Ṭalḥa, “If you wish, I shall pledge allegiance to you”; that he assisted Abū Bakr and ʿUmar, counseled reconciliation, and joined them in Friday and festival prayers.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-123.07","page":123,"ar":"وأن كثيرًا من عظماء أهل البيت أنكروا النص الجلي وأن العباس قال لعلي امدد يدك لأبايعك.","en":"He further cites that many leading members of the Prophet’s Household denied any explicit designation, and that al-ʿAbbās told ʿAlī, “Extend your hand, that I may pledge allegiance to you.”","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-123.08","page":123,"ar":"فصل: الإمام بعد رسول الله أبو بكر لإجماع أهل الحل والعقد، وقد ثبت انقياد علي وتسميته إياه خليفة والثناء عليه حيا وميتا.","en":"Section: The imam after the Messenger of God was Abū Bakr, the author argues, on the basis of agreement among the people of binding and loosening; he adduces reports of ʿAlī’s acquiescence, his calling Abū Bakr “caliph,” and his praising him both during his lifetime and after his death.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-123.09","page":123,"ar":"والاعتذار عن التأخر، ولأن الكل اتفقوا على إمامة أبي بكر أو علي أو العباس، ثم أجمعوا ...","en":"The author also cites the explanation of ʿAlī’s delayed allegiance. He then argues that the agreed candidates were Abū Bakr, ʿAlī and al-ʿAbbās, and that agreement subsequently converged—[continuing on p. 124]—upon Abū Bakr.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS","editorial_note":"1912 Cairo print p.123 distinctly ends «ثم أجمعوا», continuing p.124 «فيه فتعين». Full page 123 upper matn compared clause by clause. | Rejoin the explicit proof by elimination and consensus, instead of leaving the page end unspecified."},{"id":"KAL-124.01","page":124,"ar":"فيه فتعين، وقد يتمسك بقوله تعالى ﴿ستدعون إلى قوم أولي بأس شديد﴾.","en":"—upon him, and so his appointment was determined. A further argument may be drawn from the verse: “You will be called to [fight] a people of great might.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS","editorial_note":"1912 p.124 begins with «فيه فتعين» completing «ثم أجمعوا» from p.123; line then introduces the Qurʾānic citation. | Restores the previously omitted conclusion that specifies Abū Bakr before adding the new proof."},{"id":"KAL-124.02","page":124,"ar":"والداعي إما أبو بكر أو عمر باتفاق المفسرين وقوله صلى الله عليه وسلم اقتدوا بالذين من بعدي أبي بكر وعمر والخلافة بعدي ثلاثون سنة.","en":"The summoner is identified as Abū Bakr or ʿUmar, and the reports “Follow those after me, Abū Bakr and ʿUmar” and “The caliphate after me will last thirty years” are cited.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-124.03","page":124,"ar":"وبأنه صلى الله عليه وسلم استخلفه في الصلاة ولم يعزله ولذا قال علي قدمك رسول الله لأمر ديننا أفلا نقدمك لأمر دنيانا.","en":"The Prophet appointed him to lead prayer and did not remove him; a statement attributed to ʿAlī infers that one advanced in religion may be advanced in worldly leadership.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-124.04","page":124,"ar":"وقالت الشيعة على انتفاء العصمة والأفضلية والنص في غيره ورد بالمنع ولقوله تعالى إنما وليكم الله ورسوله.","en":"Shiʿites object that Abū Bakr lacked impeccability, supreme excellence, or explicit designation, adducing verses including “Your guardian is only God and His Messenger…”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-124.05","page":124,"ar":"والمراد بالولي المتصرف في الأمر إذ ولاية النصرة تعم الجميع.","en":"The debated word *walī* is read either as holder of governing authority or as guardian in mutual aid, which may encompass the whole community.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-124.06","page":124,"ar":"وأجيب بأن سوق الآية لولاية المحبة والنصرة، وأما وصف المؤمنين فللمدح ولزيادة الشرف، و[قراءة العبارة التالية غير محررة]، على أن الحصر لنفي التنازع.","en":"The reply takes the verse to concern affection and mutual support rather than political appointment. The believers’ description can be praise or an added honour; “while they bow” can alternatively be read as coordinated wording about believers bowing in prayer (unlike the Jewish prayer invoked in this argument), or as describing them as humble. Hence neither the plural subject nor the restrictive wording necessarily singles out ʿAlī. [The elliptical wording of the Cairo print at this point still requires direct witness collation.]","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS","editorial_note":"Direct print contains «وهم راكعون»/bowing and the alternatives of coordination and humility; the author’s longer Sharḥ al-Maqāṣid explains the syntax, without being itself a variant of Tahdhīb."},{"id":"KAL-124.07","page":124,"ar":"ولم تكن الإمامة حينئذ كذلك، وحمل صيغة الجمع على الواحد بعيد، وولاية التصرف بالفعل لم يكن لعلي حينئذ، وفي المآل لا يستقيم في الله تعالى ورسوله.","en":"At that time the imamate was not of that kind; applying a plural expression to just one person is strained, and ʿAlī had no operative governmental authority then. Reading it instead as future authority does not work for God and His Messenger.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-124.08","page":124,"ar":"وما تواتر من قوله من كنت مولاه فعلي مولاه أنت مني بمنزلة هارون من موسى إلا أنه لا نبي بعدي.","en":"The reported statements “For whomever I am *mawlā*, ʿAlī is his *mawlā*,” and “You are to me as Aaron was to Moses, except that no prophet follows me,” are discussed.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-124.09","page":124,"ar":"لأن المراد بالمولى المتصرف في الأمر إذ لا صحة","en":"The argument turns on whether *walī/mawlā* denotes authority over affairs; the refutation continues on the next page.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-125.01","page":125,"ar":"ولا فائدة لغيره ومنزلة هارون عامة فثبتت له الخلافة.","en":"The objectors argue that other readings would be pointless and that Aaron’s rank was broadly inclusive, so succession is established.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-125.02","page":125,"ar":"ورد بأنه لا تواتر في علي ولا عبرة بالآحاد في مقابلة الإجماع بل لا صحة له ولو سلم فلا حصر فيه ويبطلهما عدم الاحتجاج بهما عند الاحتياج.","en":"The response denies the alleged evidentiary weight and argues that isolated reports cannot overturn consensus; even if accepted, they do not establish exclusive appointment, particularly since they were not cited decisively when needed.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-125.03","page":125,"ar":"وهذا يندفع سلموا عليه بأمرة المؤمنين والضمير لعلي أنت الخليفة من بعدي إنه إمام المتقين هذا خليفتي عليكم.","en":"Further expressions cited by the opposing side include greeting ʿAlī as Commander of the Faithful, “You are the successor after me,” “He is the imam of the godfearing,” and “This is my caliph over you.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-125.04","page":125,"ar":"أنت أخي ووصيي وخليفتي من بعدي وقاضي ديني بكسر الدال.","en":"Further alleged designation reports include “You are my brother, testamentary executor, successor after me, and one who settles my debt.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-125.05","page":125,"ar":"وقد يحتج بأن غيره لا يصلح لظلمهم استحقاق كفرهم وفساد دينهم وطعن منفصلة في حق كل من الثلاثة.","en":"Some argue that the first three caliphs were unfit on grounds of alleged wrongdoing or defects; the subsequent objections must be assessed separately.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-125.06","page":125,"ar":"ورد بأن بعضها افتراء وبعضها غير قادح وللبعض تأويلات.","en":"The reply is that some allegations are fabrications, others irrelevant to legitimacy, and others admit alternative interpretations.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-125.07","page":125,"ar":"ثم عمر لتفويض أبي بكر الأمر إليه وإجماع الأمة عليه ثم عثمان لأن عمر جعل الأمر شورى بين ستة ووقع الاتفاق على عثمان.","en":"ʿUmar then held the imamate through Abū Bakr’s appointment and communal agreement, and ʿUthmān through the six-member consultation instituted by ʿUmar.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-125.07A","page":125,"ar":"ثم علي لإجماع أهل الحل والعقد على مبايعته.","en":"Then came ʿAlī, by the agreement of those qualified to bind and loosen to pledge allegiance to him.","status":"STAGE73_1912_PRINT_RESTORED_CLAUSE"},{"id":"KAL-125.08","page":125,"ar":"ثم آل الأمر إلى الحسن وبعد ستة أشهر من بيعته سلم الأمر لمعاوية تسكيناً للفتنة فانتقلت الإمامة إلى الملك والسلطنة.","en":"The narrative proceeds to al-Ḥasan, who relinquished authority to Muʿāwiya after six months to quiet the discord; the polity moved toward kingship and sultanate.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-125.09","page":125,"ar":"والأفضلية بترتيب الخلافة أما إجمالاً فلأن اتفاق أكثر العلماء على ذلك يشعر بوجود دليل مهم عليه.","en":"Excellence is ranked in the order of the caliphs: generally, the agreement of many scholars is held to indicate substantial evidence for this ordering.","status":"READING_NEEDS_RECHECK"},{"id":"KAL-126.01","page":126,"ar":"وأما تفصيلاً فلقوله تعالى وسيجنبها الأتقى الذي يؤتي ماله يتزكى وهو أبو بكر.","en":"As for particular proofs, he cites “The most godfearing, who gives his wealth to purify himself, will be kept away from it,” and applies the verse to Abū Bakr.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-126.02","page":126,"ar":"ولقوله صلى الله عليه وسلم ما طلعت الشمس ولا غربت بعد النبيين والمرسلين على أحد أفضل من أبي بكر.","en":"He cites a report: “After the prophets and messengers, the sun has neither risen nor set upon anyone better than Abū Bakr.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-126.03","page":126,"ar":"وقوله خير أمتي أبو بكر ثم عمر ولو كان بعدي نبي لكان عمر.","en":"He further cites “The best of my community is Abū Bakr, then ʿUmar,” and “Were there a prophet after me, it would be ʿUmar.”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-126.04","page":126,"ar":"وقوله عثمان أخي ورفيقي في الجنة وبعض ذلك ما تواتر من آثارهم وأخبارهم ومساعيهم في الإسلام.","en":"He adduces reports of ʿUthmān’s brotherhood and companionship in Paradise, together with the widely transmitted reports of the Companions’ deeds, circumstances, and efforts in the service of Islam.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-126.05","page":126,"ar":"وقالت الشيعة الأفضل علي وقوله تعالى قل لا أسألكم عليه أجراً إلا المودة في القربى وجبريل وصالح المؤمنين.","en":"Shiʿites assert the superiority of ʿAlī and cite verses concerning love of the Prophet’s kin and the assistance of Gabriel and righteous believers.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-126.06","page":126,"ar":"وقوله عليه الصلاة والسلام من أراد أن ينظر إلى آدم الحديث ولحديث الطير ولأنه أزهد وأعلم.","en":"Further traditions are brought forward—including a saying beginning “Whoever wishes to look upon Adam…,” the bird report, and the claim that ʿAlī was more ascetic and more learned—to argue for his distinction.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-126.07","page":126,"ar":"وأجيب بعد التسليم بأن الكلام في الأكرم عند الله، وأما بعدهم فقد ثبت أن فاطمة سيدة نساء العالمين وأن الحسن والحسين سيدا شباب أهل الجنة.","en":"The response distinguishes the question of who is greatest before God, conceding the special honors attributed to Fāṭima and to al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-126.08","page":126,"ar":"وأن العشرة الذين منهم الأئمة الأربعة وطلحة والزبير وعبد الرحمن وسعد وسعيد وأبو عبيدة مبشرون بالجنة.","en":"The ten named Companions—including the four caliphs, Ṭalḥa, al-Zubayr, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Saʿd, Saʿīd and Abū ʿUbayda—are said to have received good tidings of Paradise.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-126.09","page":126,"ar":"ثم الفضل بالعلم والتقوى والحق تعظيم جميع الصحابة والكف عن الطعن فيما جرى بينهم سيما المهاجرين والأنصار لما ورد في الكتاب والسنة من الثناء عليهم.","en":"Excellence rests in knowledge and godfearing conduct; the sound position is to honor all Companions and refrain from denigrating their conflicts, particularly the Emigrants and Helpers, owing to scriptural praise of them.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-126.10","page":126,"ar":"وقوله الله الله في أصحابي لا تسبوا أصحابي خير القرون قرني.","en":"Reports cited include “Fear God concerning my Companions,” “Do not revile my Companions,” and “The best generations are my generation…”","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-126.11","page":126,"ar":"وتوقف علي","en":"Discussion of ʿAlī’s refraining—[continued on the final page].","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-127.01","page":127,"ar":"عن بيعة أبي بكر لحيرته وحزنه وعن نصرة عثمان لعدم رضاه وعن قبول بيعته لإعظام الحادثة وعن قتال القتلة لشوكتهم أو لأنه رأى عدم مؤاخذة البغاة لما أتلفوا من المال والدم.","en":"His delay in pledging allegiance to Abū Bakr is explained by perplexity or grief; questions concerning the defense of ʿUthmān, the acceptance of his own allegiance, and the pursuit of the killers are explained through concerns about the event, power, and liability for acts committed in rebellion.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-127.02","page":127,"ar":"وتوقف جماعة عن الخروج معه إلى الحروب كان لاجتهاد أو لعدم إلزام منه لا لنزاع في إمامته، والمصيب في حرب الجمل وحرب صفين وحرب الخوارج علي.","en":"Some refrained from joining him in the wars because of their own independent judgment or because he had not required them to join—not because they disputed his imamate. In the Battle of the Camel, the Battle of Ṣiffīn, and the war against the Khārijites, ʿAlī was in the right.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-127.03","page":127,"ar":"والمخالفون بغاة لا كفرة ولا فسقة لما لهم من الشبهة ولهذا نهى علي عن لعن أهل الشام.","en":"Those who opposed him were rebels, not unbelievers or morally corrupt persons, because they possessed an interpretive uncertainty; this is why ʿAlī forbade cursing the people of Syria.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-127.04","page":127,"ar":"خاتمة: قد وردت أحاديث صحيحة في ظهور إمام من ولد فاطمة وفي نزول عيسى وفي خروج الدجال وغير ذلك من الأشراط.","en":"Conclusion: sound reports describe the coming of an imam descended from Fāṭima, the descent of Jesus, the emergence of the Antichrist and other signs of the Hour.","status":"1912_PRINT_FIRST_VISUAL_PASS"},{"id":"KAL-127.05","page":127,"ar":"كدابة الأرض ويأجوج ومأجوج وطلوع الشمس من مغربها والخسفات الثلاثة وقلة العلم والأمانة وكثرة الفسق والخيانة ورئاسة الفساق والأرذال.","en":"These include the Beast of the Earth, Gog and Magog, the rising of the sun in the west, the three sinkings of the earth, the dwindling of knowledge and trustworthiness, the prevalence of disobedience and betrayal, and the leadership of the wicked and base.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-127.06","page":127,"ar":"ويشبه أن يكون هذا عند قرب الساعة فلا ينافي خيرية آخر الأمة على ما قال صلى الله عليه وسلم: مثل أمتي مثل المطر لا يدرى أوله خير أم آخره.","en":"These events appear to occur near the Hour; this does not contradict the excellence of the latter part of the community, in accordance with the Prophet’s saying: “My community is like rain: one cannot tell whether its beginning or its end is better.”","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"},{"id":"KAL-127.07","page":127,"ar":"رزقنا الله خير الآخرة والأولى ووفقنا للعلم بما يحب ويرضى، إنه خير موفق ومعين، والحمد لله رب العالمين.","en":"May God grant us the good of the Hereafter and of this world, and grant us success in knowing what He loves and approves. He is the best giver of success and helper. Praise belongs to God, Lord of all worlds.","status":"SECOND_VISUAL_PASS_CORRECTED"}]};
